{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists","id":1297255,"title":"A Different Take: Heroes as Protagonists and Beasts as Antagonists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-16T08:12:11-07:00","id":1297255,"title":"A Different Take: Heroes as Protagonists and Beasts as Antagonists?","content":"<b>EDIT-</b>For the sake of clarity, the intended purpose of this thread was to see if there is potential in a &quot;flipped script&quot; take on Beast using the mechanics of the game and whether or not I should actually buy the book for Beast or if I should save my money and just do a little tweaking to Hunter: The Vigil with the same base concept. It is not intended to attack fans of Beast or anyone else, although I admit I should have made this more apparently clear in my original opening post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alright, it's no secret that Beast is the least favorite of the CofD gamelines in my opinion for a wide variety of reasons that I'm sure most of you already know by now, so I won't repeat them all.<br /> <br /> Normally, I just invoke Rule Zero and excise Beast entirely from my CofD games, but I actually had an idea recently to fix that. It's subversive and intentionally runs counter to the default themes of Beast anyway, but I was never one for thematic purism to begin with.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Beasts and find them unsympathetic, and often times, I actually kind of root for the Heroes and find their strawman portrayals in the early Beast works to be cringe-inducing at best. The fact that the main villains of the game are literally called &quot;Heroes&quot; just reeks of punk contrarianism, which I am not a fan of. But it has given me an idea of sorts.<br /> <br /> What if someone did a fan game that was an inverse of Beast: The Primordial? One where you played as the Heroes and the Beasts were the true evil in the setting?<br /> <br /> Before anyone accuses me of trolling, I want to make it clear that this is not meant as an attack on anyone who likes Beast the way it is. If you like Beast as written, that's fine by me. You do you and to each their own. Have fun gaming the way you like to.<br /> <br /> However, I do not like Beast as written and I want to change it to fit my liking, something more in line of action-horror, dark modern adventure, and stories of Good vs. Evil (with the Heroes being Good and the Beasts being Evil) because that's more to my tastes.<br /> <br /> However, I am not as familiar with the mechanics of Beast (I boycotted the game at launch and so I don't have a copy of it) and I am wondering about the potential of a Heroes fan game, with the archetypes being based on literary and mythic heroes such as Hercules, King Arthur, Odysseus, Robin Hood, etc.<br /> <br /> There could be room for tragedy, a Hero risking becoming the very monsters he fights. However, I like the dynamic struggle between Good and Evil as a theme, even if it is an old one.<br /> <br /> Would anyone be willing to give such a fan game a chance? Is there potential in a direct subversion of Beast's premise?<br /> <br /> Or should I just keep doing what I was doing and act like Beast isn't there in my CofD games?<br /> <br /> Any constructive feedback is appreciated. Let's keep it civil and not bring any off-topic issues into this thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-18-2019, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T08:19:35-07:00","id":1297256,"title":"","content":"Well things is, if you want a game of heroes fighting against monster, you should consider Hunter the Vigil, Heroes are monster, as much as the beasts they hunt They don't hesistate to gather a group of mundane human sycophant and point them at the Beast they're hunting to sacrifice them so they can swoop down and avenge the poor, poor human who tried to fight back against the &quot;monster&quot; and get all the glory. Hunters could work very well against Beasts, Heroes already give Hunters a dark reflection of what they could become.<br /> <br /> Personally i like beasts that tries to act humane, i find it very interesting that Beast don't have a moral trait like Integrity, Wisdom or Humanity. <br /> Any game aside from mortal is based on the trope of &quot;You are a monster now&quot; and i find that Beast have an interesting spin on it, you are defenitely a monster, but it's up to you to choose how you will act as a person, some beasts even fight their inhumane kin.<br /> Heroes don't have that luxury, they are egomaniacs bent on getting as much glory as possible by slaying beasts, to the point that they don't ever bother with slaying other supernatural because killing them don't yield the sick joy and rush of power they get when they put down a Beast<br /> <br /> So yeah, a new Hunter conspiracy focusing on Beasts could be a very cool idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 03-16-2019, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T08:33:29-07:00","id":1297259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297256#post1297256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well things is, if you want a game of heroes fighting against monster, you should consider Hunter the Vigil, Heroes are monster, as much as the beasts they hunt They don't hesistate to gather a group of mundane human sycophant and point them at the Beast they're hunting to sacrifice them so they can swoop down and avenge the poor, poor human who tried to fight back against the &quot;monster&quot; and get all the glory. Hunters could work very well against Beasts, Heroes already give Hunters a dark reflection of what they could become.<br /> <br /> Personally i like beasts that tries to act humane, i find it very interesting that Beast don't have a moral trait like Integrity, Wisdom or Humanity.<br /> Any game aside from mortal is based on the trope of &quot;You are a monster now&quot; and i find that Beast have an interesting spin on it, you are defenitely a monster, but it's up to you to choose how you will act as a person, some beasts even fight their inhumane kin.<br /> Heroes don't have that luxury, they are egomaniacs bent on getting as much glory as possible by slaying beasts, to the point that they don't ever bother with slaying other supernatural because killing them don't yield the sick joy and rush of power they get when they put down a Beast<br /> <br /> So yeah, a new Hunter conspiracy focusing on Beasts could be a very cool idea</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm well aware of Hunter: The Vigil and I find it awesome. <br /> <br /> But I want to subvert the &quot;Heroes as egomaniac glory hounds&quot; and instead make them the main protagonists, allied with Hunters but more focused and possibly empowered as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T08:37:37-07:00","id":1297260,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would work really well as Raw, Heroes don't work well with groups at all and all their mechanics are focused on their obsession towards Beasts, you would need to re-write a lot of it, but i think i remember a supllement for hunter about Heroes called Hunter Tooth and Nail that dealt with them, you might want to check it out !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T08:42:24-07:00","id":1297262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297260#post1297260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it would work really well as Raw, Heroes don't work well with groups at all and all their mechanics are focused on their obsession towards Beasts, you would need to re-write a lot of it, but i think i remember a supllement for hunter about Heroes called Hunter Tooth and Nail that dealt with them, you might want to check it out !</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know it wouldn't work well as written, so I'm intending to re-write it so Heroes can work well with groups (especially Hunters, Mages, and Princesses, if we're including fan games) and instead flipping the script where Beasts cannot work well in groups of non-Beasts.<br /> <br /> Basically I am intending to fully subvert Beast's themes and premise and instead flip the script. I want a game where Beasts are so dangerous and evil that even other shady characters in the CofD such as Vampires don't want to deal with them.<br /> <br /> In this setting, Hunters are too over-burdened to deal with the threat of the Beasts, while the other splats have their own issues, leaving the Heroes to bear the brunt of the fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:34:01-07:00","id":1297268,"title":"","content":"This is not a different take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:36:58-07:00","id":1297270,"title":"","content":"Yeah it's kinda Heroes from their PoV now that i think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 03-16-2019, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T09:50:23-07:00","id":1297275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297270#post1297270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it's kinda Heroes from thei PoV now that i think about it</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, like, asides from, what Primordial's take on it does for the Beasts themselves, it isn't just like a particular other gameline, it is literally any modern fantasy game that borrows plays into the mythic hero archetype, of which there are literally dozens of games that communicate that, often better than what you could wring out of the Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> The reason Beast works is that it flipped the actual narrative on it's head and then wildly innovated from there to create a player character that is highly distinctive from both it's peers in the Chronicles world <i>and</i> the larger discussion concerning the type of stories (including games that play with them). There's nothing quite like Beast out there, whether you like it or not.<br /> <br /> Also, taking this larger meta out of the picture for a second, Heroes as the Protagonists is one of the more recursive subjects of conversation in Primordial, and has been pretty much ever since we got any details on the Beast/Hero dynamic. Hell, I am looking over <i>someone else's</i> attempt at the subject right now to give them ideas on how to refine it. This idea is not new in the slightest, and that should at least be noted.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yes, in case anyone is wondering, the first thing I am telling the person I am reviewing material for is that this has been done to death and there's no good reason to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-16-2019, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:24:14-07:00","id":1297287,"title":"","content":"not only that, but it's been stated that Camilla hasn't even read the new Beast. and a LOT of people doing these hero things haven't while claiming beast makes them strawmen. heck, conquering heroes does a great job of giving them depth<br /> <br /> also, all this crap about beast being irredeemable monsters is so stupid whenever vampires, werewolves, demons, mummies, snd other supernaturals are brought up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tooth and nail has Yuris group. a compact that thinks beast are the greatest evil and try to rehabilitate victims, and the Merrick institute, a conspiracy that can fight beast in the dream realm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-16-2019, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:45:37-07:00","id":1297292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297287#post1297287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> also, all this crap about beast being irredeemable monsters is so stupid whenever vampires, werewolves, demons, mummies, snd other supernaturals are brought up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always wonder where such individuals (who think that) stand on Changeling's Autumn Court. Considering, based on my purely anecdotal evidence, that Autumn tends to be a very popular Court. And unlike Beasts, they chose to feed on fear whereas a Beast has to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:09:12-07:00","id":1297296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297275#post1297275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, like, asides from, what Primordial's take on it does for the Beasts themselves, it isn't just like a particular other gameline, it is literally any modern fantasy game that borrows plays into the mythic hero archetype, of which there are literally dozens of games that communicate that, often better than what you could wring out of the Storyteller system.<br /> <br /> The reason Beast works is that it flipped the actual narrative on it's head and then wildly innovated from there to create a player character that is highly distinctive from both it's peers in the Chronicles world <i>and</i> the larger discussion concerning the type of stories (including games that play with them). There's nothing quite like Beast out there, whether you like it or not.<br /> <br /> Also, taking this larger meta out of the picture for a second, Heroes as the Protagonists is one of the more recursive subjects of conversation in Primordial, and has been pretty much ever since we got any details on the Beast/Hero dynamic. Hell, I am looking over <i>someone else's</i> attempt at the subject right now to give them ideas on how to refine it. This idea is not new in the slightest, and that should at least be noted.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, yes, in case anyone is wondering, the first thing I am telling the person I am reviewing material for is that this has been done to death and there's no good reason to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love Beast myself even if it's been a while since i red it, and don't relly sympathize with Heroes, i tend to view them as either tragic victims or dangerous sociopaths. But i'm really curious how a Hunter would act when confronted with a conflict between a Beast and a Hero<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297287#post1297287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, all this crap about beast being irredeemable monsters is so stupid whenever vampires, werewolves, demons, mummies, snd other supernaturals are brought up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, nearly all the CofD games revolve around you being a monster, and Beasts aren't necessarly more awful than the others or more morally degenerated than some mortals","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":12946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","user":"Emerick","date":". 03-16-2019, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:22:17-07:00","id":1297297,"title":"","content":"I can't see this end well, Camilla.<br /> <br /> For starters, reading the OP makes me groan for how much it willfully ignores what even Beast detractors admit the books say. No need to like the book nor the game because, it's worth repeating, not all gamelines are for everyone, but to dislike something, with its flaws and weak points, is different than to dislike something that only exists to you.<br /> <br /> But the main reason I doubt you'll have an easy road ahead is there's a lapse of logic between what you feel, what you want to do, and what you're asking. You find Beasts repulsive and yet want to make them even worse so everyone would be well within their rights to slay them without a thought? That makes things worse and only serves to confirm your own bias. Also, a game about heroes killing monsters, with them being the protagonists of the events and the focus of their consequences? That's hardly anything new, either as a game or a topic discussed around here.<br /> <br /> First, the book allows that, straight from the core. The only difference is that you would made their enemies so horrible, any conflict in there would be gone. I get that you don't like it, but there's this tightrope Beast walks on between the mythical ideal of Heroes and Beasts as forces of Good &amp; Darkness and how it manifests in less than absolute ways in the setting reality which is a rather big deal for the game themes, one of its central conflicts and reasons to be.<br /> <br /> Long story short, if you subvert a subversion and ignore everything that made it interesting in the first place, you'll have something emptier than both the original trope, its deconstruction and even what one good reconstruction would do. I'm an advocate for Beast &amp; Heroes to always feel and confront with tensions towards a clearer, more platonic and &quot;simple&quot; life, but a source of struggle more than anything else.<br /> <br /> So I don't think there's much potential for this idea as something more than your own personal hack for the game. Aspects of it are there, others build upon foundations that don't exist and overall it offers something that it's either done better elsewhere or I doubt would pique the interest of those who like the game for the unusual narrative avenues it offers.<br /> <br /> Can't speak for others, naturally, but I personally see no way this sort of fan game can gain much traction in this specific context. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-16-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T11:30:42-07:00","id":1297301,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Heroes had gotten another Name if there would really be such a call to &quot;redeem&quot; them.. I mean the person who hunts down and Kills vampires is traditionally the &quot;Hero&quot; of that.. same with the person who hunts down and kills werewolves... I mean honestly how is an Compact/Conspiracy dedicated to Hunting Beasts... not the appropriate thing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:01:49-07:00","id":1297306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297301#post1297301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Heroes had gotten another Name if there would really be such a call to &quot;redeem&quot; them.. I mean the person who hunts down and Kills vampires is traditionally the &quot;Hero&quot; of that.. same with the person who hunts down and kills werewolves... I mean honestly how is an Compact/Conspiracy dedicated to Hunting Beasts... not the appropriate thing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd also like to add that hunters should, <i>by all means</i>, hunt and kill Beasts. The Begotten, in all their shapes and incarnations, are so perfect as antagonists for Hunter it's almost too easy. I'd be quite disappointed if there's no mention of Beast-lite monsters throughout Hunter 2nd Edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:31:00-07:00","id":1297313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297297#post1297297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see this end well, Camilla.<br /> <br /> For starters, reading the OP makes me groan for how much it willfully ignores what even Beast detractors admit the books say. No need to like the book nor the game because, it's worth repeating, not all gamelines are for everyone, but to dislike something, with its flaws and weak points, is different than to dislike something that only exists to you.<br /> <br /> But the main reason I doubt you'll have an easy road ahead is there's a lapse of logic between what you feel, what you want to do, and what you're asking. You find Beasts repulsive and yet want to make them even worse so everyone would be well within their rights to slay them without a thought? That makes things worse and only serves to confirm your own bias. Also, a game about heroes killing monsters, with them being the protagonists of the events and the focus of their consequences? That's hardly anything new, either as a game or a topic discussed around here.<br /> <br /> First, the book allows that, straight from the core. The only difference is that you would made their enemies so horrible, any conflict in there would be gone. I get that you don't like it, but there's this tightrope Beast walks on between the mythical ideal of Heroes and Beasts as forces of Good &amp; Darkness and how it manifests in less than absolute ways in the setting reality which is a rather big deal for the game themes, one of its central conflicts and reasons to be.<br /> <br /> Long story short, if you subvert a subversion and ignore everything that made it interesting in the first place, you'll have something emptier than both the original trope, its deconstruction and even what one good reconstruction would do. I'm an advocate for Beast &amp; Heroes to always feel and confront with tensions towards a clearer, more platonic and &quot;simple&quot; life, but a source of struggle more than anything else.<br /> <br /> So I don't think there's much potential for this idea as something more than your own personal hack for the game. Aspects of it are there, others build upon foundations that don't exist and overall it offers something that it's either done better of elsewhere or I doubt would pique the interest of those who like the game for the unusual narrative avenues it offers.<br /> <br /> Can't speak for others, naturally, but I personally see no way this sort of fan game can gain much traction in this specific context. Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to take a second here to say I am being...polite in my response to Cam, largely because (being blunt) I don't want to get banned from the forums-but I do want to take a second here to just say I could just <i>unload</i> on Cam's desires vs <i>any reality</i> of art/game development, from cynical to aspirational. It is really about dealing with creatures who are on the opposite ends of, say, Scott McCloud's spectrum between idea, form, idiom, structure, craft, and surface.<br /> <br /> Simply put, though, not only has the basic idea of this thread been done better, even it's cheapest forms, time and time again in a variety of games and even fan hacks(like the ones that <i>don't </i>ignore the problem of the Hero/Beast dichotomy)-<br /> <br /> Not only that, but it lacks an understanding that games as story require asking something of the medium, in the form of a idea or what the particular form can do. Since Storyteller Games rely on it's mechanical cohesion between the various franchises, each gameline within it relies on it's different ideas within the framework to make itself compelling, particularly since it depends on also relating the primary themes of Chronicles on the whole. This is why, even with more lines than the original World of Darkness, it is impressive that Chronicles not only has eleven gamelines to it's name, but that they still strive for an ambition of more beyond that, and seem to at least have answers for it-because there's also a deliberate coursing of the direction and dialogue here.<br /> <br /> And that's really worth diving into: regardless of whether or not the games speak to any one person's <i>desires</i>, Chronicle games, and White Wolf games on a larger scale, speak to the <i>needs</i> of almost everyone in some form or capacity, because it's interest in personal horror, angst, and drama means that it relates and often says something both real and aspirational to...really, anyone. You can see this almost any post about how people relate to Beast, in how a lot of people feel the validation, not from the idea that their natures merely have a place, but a <i>functional</i> place in the universe, that who they are is not divorced from the reality they deal with even as it might be divorced from the reality <i>some people perceive,</i> and in fact might even be useful in building better worlds.<br /> <br /> That's true for a lot of White Wolf games, really. In a world that, as long as White Wolf has existed in, has made certain types of being so controversial as to be political, it is affirmative that not only does the seeming &quot;monstrosity&quot; of a wide variety of alienating patterns, natures, and behaviors are okay to be, but can, also, be of benefit to the world around them when acknowledged and handled correctly. The games transmute both the feelings of anxiety and loneliness and more asides and the states of being that might cause them into not states of acceptance but belonging, even if the current society doesn't accept them.<br /> <br /> Long story short, what this proposition misses is that what makes these games speak to people is that they carry something human in their hearts with them, which can and does include both personal horror, angst, and drama, as well as the cathartic transgression and ultimate True Acceptance of such things into <i>the world as it is.</i><br /> <br /> Even shorter summary: Look, this concept is a hollow wreck, and there comes a point where even escapist-aimed fantasy needs something in it before we're all just playing the original Jumpman for empty psycho-spiritual calories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:34:27-07:00","id":1297314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297306#post1297306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also like to add that hunters should, <i>by all means</i>, hunt and kill Beasts. The Begotten, in all their shapes and incarnations, are so perfect as antagonists for Hunter it's almost too easy. I'd be quite disappointed if there's no mention of Beast-lite monsters throughout Hunter 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the record, I love and adore all three of the Hunter Organizations, and do advocate Hunters against Beasts, even as I readily argue on their behalf. Balance is needed in discussions regarding humanity vs monstrosity.<br /> <br /> It's not like there isn't a case against Beasts, it just doesn't lie within the Heroic perspective, which is basically bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:40:04-07:00","id":1297319,"title":"","content":"Short answer: just go play Hunter: the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Slightly longer answer: just go play Hunter: the Vigil, and if need be, suck it up and just dig out D20 Modern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T12:55:23-07:00","id":1297329,"title":"","content":"Scion is a good choice for &quot;Heroes&quot; that are legit and upfront as well with some actual mythological connotations that work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T13:40:00-07:00","id":1297346,"title":"","content":"Loosely related:<br /> <br /> It's not like you can't play an absurd game that still has a meaningful conversation.<br /> <br /> Case in point, Devil May Cry 5 continues it's surprisingly humanist theme with a lot more nuance than expected, and part of that nuance is <i>Michael Jackson as a powerset</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:16:59-07:00","id":1297353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists#post1297255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, it's no secret that Beast is the least favorite of the CofD gamelines in my opinion for a wide variety of reasons that I'm sure most of you already know by now, so I won't repeat them all.<br /> <br /> Normally, I just invoke Rule Zero and excise Beast entirely from my CofD games, but I actually had an idea recently to fix that. It's subversive and intentionally runs counter to the default themes of Beast anyway, but I was never one for thematic purism to begin with.<br /> <br /> I don't like the Beasts and find them unsympathetic, and often times, I actually kind of root for the Heroes and find their strawman portrayals in the early Beast works to be cringe-inducing at best. The fact that the main villains of the game are literally called &quot;Heroes&quot; just reeks of punk contrarianism, which I am not a fan of. But it has given me an idea of sorts.<br /> <br /> What if someone did a fan game that was an inverse of Beast: The Primordial? One where you played as the Heroes and the Beasts were the true evil in the setting?<br /> <br /> Before anyone accuses me of trolling, I want to make it clear that this is not meant as an attack on anyone who likes Beast the way it is. If you like Beast as written, that's fine by me. You do you and to each their own. Have fun gaming the way you like to.<br /> <br /> However, I do not like Beast as written and I want to change it to fit my liking, something more in line of action-horror, dark modern adventure, and stories of Good vs. Evil (with the Heroes being Good and the Beasts being Evil) because that's more to my tastes.<br /> <br /> However, I am not as familiar with the mechanics of Beast (I boycotted the game at launch and so I don't have a copy of it) and I am wondering about the potential of a Heroes fan game, with the archetypes being based on literary and mythic heroes such as Hercules, King Arthur, Odysseus, Robin Hood, etc.<br /> <br /> There could be room for tragedy, a Hero risking becoming the very monsters he fights. However, I like the dynamic struggle between Good and Evil as a theme, even if it is an old one.<br /> <br /> Would anyone be willing to give such a fan game a chance? Is there potential in a direct subversion of Beast's premise?<br /> <br /> Or should I just keep doing what I was doing and act like Beast isn't there in my CofD games?<br /> <br /> Any constructive feedback is appreciated. Let's keep it civil and not bring any off-topic issues into this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a subversive idea. This, in fact, the opposite of a subversive idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:18:00-07:00","id":1297368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297287#post1297287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">not only that, but it's been stated that Camilla hasn't even read the new Beast. and a LOT of people doing these hero things haven't while claiming beast makes them strawmen. heck, conquering heroes does a great job of giving them depth<br /> <br /> also, all this crap about beast being irredeemable monsters is so stupid whenever vampires, werewolves, demons, mummies, snd other supernaturals are brought up.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Tooth and nail has Yuris group. a compact that thinks beast are the greatest evil and try to rehabilitate victims, and the Merrick institute, a conspiracy that can fight beast in the dream realm</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hate the Devouring. So much. But the entire things reeks of Slapdash tweaks like a broken Piece of wall that has a poster taped on to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T15:20:15-07:00","id":1297369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297368#post1297368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hate the Devouring. So much. But the entire things reeks of Slapdash tweaks like a broken Piece of wall that has a poster taped on to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>TBF, Beast PG does provide an in-game alternative where some Beasts' Devouring more closely resembles the KS Draft's Homecoming. There's no mechanical differences but it's there if you want to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T16:48:46-07:00","id":1297384,"title":"","content":"I don't get the hate for the Devouring, though it's somewhat irrelevant to the issue of subverting a subversion doesn't really do much but get you a lesser copy of the original like a photocopy of a photocopy.<br /> <br /> The Devouring does two things: it adds ambiguity as to whether Beasts were born that way and simply waiting to hatch, or are made by Horrors seeking out humans that dream too deeply. It adds a better built in hook for Beasts to have social bonds with other Beasts from the start.<br /> <br /> Neither of these are negative changes in any fashion I can conceive. The core book's writing isn't great, because it was a last minute tweak in response to feedback to the KS preview manuscript, but the fundamental concept being bad baffles me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:09:41-07:00","id":1297391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297384#post1297384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the hate for the Devouring, though it's somewhat irrelevant to the issue of subverting a subversion doesn't really do much but get you a lesser copy of the original like a photocopy of a photocopy.<br /> <br /> The Devouring does two things: it adds ambiguity as to whether Beasts were born that way and simply waiting to hatch, or are made by Horrors seeking out humans that dream too deeply. It adds a better built in hook for Beasts to have social bonds with other Beasts from the start.<br /> <br /> Neither of these are negative changes in any fashion I can conceive. The core book's writing isn't great, because it was a last minute tweak in response to feedback to the KS preview manuscript, but the fundamental concept being bad baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of people view it as a monster destroying your soul to make you into a monster/ a being it can puppet around for its own designs. Then they just keep pointing out the line that it eats your soul and blah blah blah. (No offense to anyone here, just comes up in a miscellanious thread of one board a lot, so it gets boring after the millionth time you hear that and terrible interpretations justified on poor use of the &quot;the fear must be real&quot; line.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:10:22-07:00","id":1297392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297384#post1297384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the hate for the Devouring, though it's somewhat irrelevant to the issue of subverting a subversion doesn't really do much but get you a lesser copy of the original like a photocopy of a photocopy.<br /> <br /> The Devouring does two things: it adds ambiguity as to whether Beasts were born that way and simply waiting to hatch, or are made by Horrors seeking out humans that dream too deeply. It adds a better built in hook for Beasts to have social bonds with other Beasts from the start.<br /> <br /> Neither of these are negative changes in any fashion I can conceive. The core book's writing isn't great, because it was a last minute tweak in response to feedback to the KS preview manuscript, but the fundamental concept being bad baffles me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with the Devouring is it gets too close to vampirism for my tastes. I don't see that ambiguity helping anything because it questions the agency of the actors involved. <br /> <br /> In the original Homecoming, they were always different in a way that stood them apart from other people, and the choice of facing that aspect of what they always were and waking it up versus letting sleeping dragons lie and continuing with the missing pieces of their life shows some contrast of acceptance and denial. <br /> <br /> The Devouring just... Messed with that, badly. And presenting the Horror as something new to the equation of the person damages the agency of self acceptance.<br /> <br /> This is simple for me to fix, though. I just don't have the Devouring in my games and substitute the Homecoming. I don't like that that means there are sections of the books that are basically wasted space to me due to that decision. But that's fine. The rest of the material is still useful enough to me. <br /> <br /> For those that like the Devouring, they can enjoy that for their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:14:01-07:00","id":1297393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297391#post1297391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A lot of people view it as a monster destroying your soul to make you into a monster/ a being it can puppet around for its own designs. Then they just keep pointing out the line that it eats your soul and blah blah blah. (No offense to anyone here, just comes up in a miscellanious thread of one board a lot, so it gets boring after the millionth time you hear that and terrible interpretations justified on poor use of the &amp;quot;the fear must be real&amp;quot; line.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a significant world of difference between a monster that makes a home in you and a monster that was there ever since the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:17:03-07:00","id":1297394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297392#post1297392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue with the Devouring is it gets too close to vampirism for my tastes. I don't see that ambiguity helping anything because it questions the agency of the actors involved.<br /> <br /> In the original Homecoming, they were always different in a way that stood them apart from other people, and the choice of facing that aspect of what they always were and waking it up versus letting sleeping dragons lie and continuing with the missing pieces of their life shows some contrast of acceptance and denial.<br /> <br /> The Devouring just... Messed with that, badly. And presenting the Horror as something new to the equation of the person damages the agency of self acceptance.<br /> <br /> This is simple for me to fix, though. I just don't have the Devouring in my games and substitute the Homecoming. I don't like that that means there are sections of the books that are basically wasted space to me due to that decision. But that's fine. The rest of the material is still useful enough to me.<br /> <br /> For those that like the Devouring, they can enjoy that for their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>After the bit about the nascent horrors in the Player's Guide, I've kind of mentally viewed it as a slowpoke -&gt; slowbro scenario.*<br /> <br /> *Totally not because slowbro makes an odd amount of sense for how to explain an Anakim with a lot of pratcice using their Nightmares. :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:20:58-07:00","id":1297395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297346#post1297346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loosely related:<br /> <br /> It's not like you can't play an absurd game that still has a meaningful conversation.<br /> <br /> Case in point, Devil May Cry 5 continues it's surprisingly humanist theme with a lot more nuance than expected, and part of that nuance is <i>Michael Jackson as a powerset</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's also a pretty good inspiration for:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">an intelligent Rampant.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:32:54-07:00","id":1297397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297394#post1297394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After the bit about the nascent horrors in the Player's Guide, I've kind of mentally viewed it as a slowpoke -&gt; slowbro scenario.*<br /> <br /> *Totally not because slowbro makes an odd amount of sense for how to explain an Anakim with a lot of pratcice using their Nightmares. :3</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I'm not really understanding what you mean there... ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:46:22-07:00","id":1297401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297397#post1297397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I'm not really understanding what you mean there... ^^;</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Pok\u00e9mon games, the in-fiction explanation* for the Pok\u00e9mon Slowpoke evolving into Slowbro is that a particular other monster latches onto its tail and, through a combination of ecstatic inspiration and cutting off its original means of fishing for sustenance, leads it to become a more active and intelligent hunter.<br /> <br /> In the same way, a larval Horror biting down on the nascent connection to the Primordial Dream possessed by a deep dreamer causes them to develop into a Beast.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* The pure-mechanical explanation is &quot;your Slowpoke hit Level 37 or whatever other evolution trigger the game you're playing has for Slowpoke.&quot;</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T18:40:23-07:00","id":1297412,"title":"","content":"the devouring makes sense to me, the human still must consciously make the decision after all (but I do agree it needs work)<br /> <br /> now that I'm calmed down, I must say if you want a &quot;subversive&quot; Hero game, do this. make the hero and beast relationship the same, but make heroes that are more self aware of the fact that reality is not black and white. In fact make this the core theme: heroes must maintain a proper view of morality, fight against a plain black and white view. call this Judgement or something I dont know, but dont make beasts irredeemably evil, or other monsters for that matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:04:19-07:00","id":1297425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297297#post1297297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see this end well, Camilla.<br /> <br /> For starters, reading the OP makes me groan for how much it willfully ignores what even Beast detractors admit the books say. No need to like the book nor the game because, it's worth repeating, not all gamelines are for everyone, but to dislike something, with its flaws and weak points, is different than to dislike something that only exists to you.<br /> <br /> But the main reason I doubt you'll have an easy road ahead is there's a lapse of logic between what you feel, what you want to do, and what you're asking. You find Beasts repulsive and yet want to make them even worse so everyone would be well within their rights to slay them without a thought? That makes things worse and only serves to confirm your own bias. Also, a game about heroes killing monsters, with them being the protagonists of the events and the focus of their consequences? That's hardly anything new, either as a game or a topic discussed around here.<br /> <br /> First, the book allows that, straight from the core. The only difference is that you would made their enemies so horrible, any conflict in there would be gone. I get that you don't like it, but there's this tightrope Beast walks on between the mythical ideal of Heroes and Beasts as forces of Good &amp; Darkness and how it manifests in less than absolute ways in the setting reality which is a rather big deal for the game themes, one of its central conflicts and reasons to be.<br /> <br /> Long story short, if you subvert a subversion and ignore everything that made it interesting in the first place, you'll have something emptier than both the original trope, its deconstruction and even what one good reconstruction would do. I'm an advocate for Beast &amp; Heroes to always feel and confront with tensions towards a clearer, more platonic and &quot;simple&quot; life, but a source of struggle more than anything else.<br /> <br /> So I don't think there's much potential for this idea as something more than your own personal hack for the game. Aspects of it are there, others build upon foundations that don't exist and overall it offers something that it's either done better elsewhere or I doubt would pique the interest of those who like the game for the unusual narrative avenues it offers.<br /> <br /> Can't speak for others, naturally, but I personally see no way this sort of fan game can gain much traction in this specific context. Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it helps, I'm mainly intending this idea for personal use in my own chronicles. I may post a variant of it for others to use, but I am aiming for personal use first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T20:53:37-07:00","id":1297433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297425#post1297425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If it helps, I'm mainly intending this idea for personal use in my own chronicles. I may post a variant of it for others to use, but I am aiming for personal use first.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, something significant you'll need to overcome is building some kind of sense of conflict that works for a horror setting. Heroes as they are, are effectively superhuman in comparison to Hunters (and even more so when specifically targeting Beasts unless they're Kinslayers). And I don't mean &quot;sense of conflict&quot; as in, &quot;they fight Beasts&quot;. I mean some kind of conflict about what they do, who they are, why they hunt, and so forth.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure how you're going to square that circle. Hunters get away with it because they're largely normal humans fighting against monsters, so they have the horror aspect of being the underdog in their fights. Heroes? They can absolutely wreck Beasts with the powers they get, and they get stronger for each one they kill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:14:35-07:00","id":1297437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297433#post1297433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, something significant you'll need to overcome is building some kind of sense of conflict that works for a horror setting. Heroes as they are, are effectively superhuman in comparison to Hunters (and even more so when specifically targeting Beasts unless they're Kinslayers). And I don't mean &amp;quot;sense of conflict&amp;quot; as in, &amp;quot;they fight Beasts&amp;quot;. I mean some kind of conflict about what they do, who they are, why they hunt, and so forth.<br /> <br /> And I'm not sure how you're going to square that circle. Hunters get away with it because they're largely normal humans fighting against monsters, so they have the horror aspect of being the underdog in their fights. Heroes? They can absolutely wreck Beasts with the powers they get, and they get stronger for each one they kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>has a point. I would recommend changing how anathema works (it pains me to say that, since I think it's an awesome ability, but it's also insanely powerful)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T22:45:41-07:00","id":1297462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists#post1297255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, it's no secret that Beast is the least favorite of the CofD gamelines in my opinion for a wide variety of reasons that I'm sure most of you already know by now, so I won't repeat them all</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt the numbers add up on that. I see people playing and talking about Beast much more often than Hunter, Demon, Mummy, Sin Eater or Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297392#post1297392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devouring just... Messed with that, badly. And presenting the Horror as something new to the equation of the person damages the agency of self acceptance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally feel &quot;the more the merrier,&quot; different takes on beasts working leaves greater room. Also it was even in core that sometimes horrors are created on the spot by rare and talented dreamers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T07:11:52-07:00","id":1297503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297425#post1297425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If it helps, I'm mainly intending this idea for personal use in my own chronicles. I may post a variant of it for others to use, but I am aiming for personal use first.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrugs*<br /> <br /> Does not help me but hey, if this allows you to handle better the fact that Beast is a gameline that exists, there's nothing wrong with it. I'll still point out that none of us would come to your table and tell you how to run your games, whether you liked them in the first place or not. That said,I have no reason whatsoever to interfere with someone's personal homerules, no matter how invested I am with a certain game.<br /> <br /> Beast has its weak spots and several vocal critics, some of whom are rather big voices in our little subculture. You're not alone among those that don't like. But, and allow me to get more blunt here, I just don't care. Criticism is criticism, and it's important to consider its valid points in order to improve but, so to say, I still am going to get Beast's skull tattooed on my arm if I manage to deal with a thing and celebrate, no matter what others think about this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-17-2019, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:22:25-07:00","id":1297514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297503#post1297503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*shrugs*<br /> <br /> Does not help me but hey, if this allows you to handle better the fact that Beast is a gameline that exists, there's nothing wrong with it. I'll still point out that none of us would come to your table and tell you how to run your games, whether you liked them in the first place or not. That said,I have no reason whatsoever to interfere with someone's personal homerules, no matter how invested I am with a certain game.<br /> <br /> Beast has its weak spots and several vocal critics, some of whom are rather big voices in our little subculture. You're not alone among those that don't like. But, and allow me to get more blunt here, I just don't care. Criticism is criticism, and it's important to consider its valid points in order to improve but, so to say, I still am going to get Beast's skull tattooed on my arm if I manage to deal with a thing and celebrate, no matter what others think about this game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that is perfectly fine with me. If you like Beast, that's good. You do you.<br /> <br /> Again, I am not attacking anyone who likes Beast as it is written. We're all entitled to our own opinions equally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:46:33-07:00","id":1297517,"title":"","content":"Nobody want help you with your demand: this is the real answer, i guess.<br /> I only read non-compliance about your vision. 3 page of critics and none idea for your personal idea.<br /> I doubt that here you can take any help, the mass of users &quot;need&quot; to invalidate any sense of your personal choice over any other concern.<br /> I am sadded by this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 03-17-2019, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T08:56:22-07:00","id":1297520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297517#post1297517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody want help you with your demand: this is the real answer, i guess.<br /> I only read non-compliance about your vision. 3 page of critics and none idea for your personal idea.<br /> I doubt that here you can take any help, the mass of users &quot;need&quot; to invalidate any sense of your personal choice over any other concern.<br /> I am sadded by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering the tone of my replies and the fact I said multiple times, in this very thread, that Camilla's choices are their own and there's no problem with them, this is just rude. A tone that, I might add, was far more considerate than their own on the various past occasion they spoke of Beast and its fans. So I won't stay silent while you say we're the bad guys of the situations (no, there's no bad guys in this situation, for the record).<br /> <br /> And with that, there's yet another reminder I should stay clear of this kind of threads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:12:55-07:00","id":1297521,"title":"","content":"My best shot at being helpful for the OP is to really just say, &quot;If you want to subvert something, it really helps to actually read the material you're trying to subvert. Because it's obvious when you haven't.&quot;<br /> <br /> If they don't want to do that.... Then nothing is really going to help them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:26:17-07:00","id":1297523,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that the Beast fan community here is... kinda touchy? We get a lot of people that openly admit to not even reading the whole final core book (let alone the supplements or actually trying the game itself), that come here to 'fix' the game by posting ideas that essentially strip Beast of what makes it a unique and interesting game in a very crowded RPG market for something literally dozens of other games already do (many of them other WoD/CofD games at that). Camilla has been very vocal about their dislike of the game before, and the &quot;this isn't mean to be an attack on the fans&quot; refrain is difficult to treat innocently if someone has to keep repeating it... they know it's not going to be well received in the first place. It's like the classic, &quot;I don't mean to be racist, but...&quot; disclaimer. Either people aren't going to care because it was offensive anyway, or you're just priming people to consider your statement in that light. If you feel like you have to qualify it that way, you either need to consider not saying it, or rephrasing it because that's a giant red flag you're saying it wrong. This is no different in construction. If you have to say, &quot;this isn't meant to be an attack on Beast fans,&quot; you're probably going to be interpreted as doing so anyway, or you're phrasing things in a fashion unlikely to get your point across to/get positive responses from Beast fans.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Beast.... why post a fan-game that basically has nothing to do with what Beast is about in the Beast subforum? Just head on down to the general CofD and start a fan-game about what you want to play if the existing games aren't scratching an itch you have. Esp. if you know this is a reoccurring issue around here.<br /> <br /> Also, however much it might suck to hear? If you ask for criticism, sometimes the feedback you get from your chosen sample group is going to be, &quot;nope, this sucks.&quot; It's not sad that happens. You're hearing something worth considering before moving forward. That's a good and useful thing once you get past any frustration with it. It's pretty important to consider that the time and energy for Camilla to turn BtP into what they want out of a game, compared to turning HtV into what they want from a game, is actually a waste of time that isn't going to get better results for the investment.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:38:19-07:00","id":1297526,"title":"","content":"Um, maybe I should be more clear in the OP...<br /> <br /> I might be willing to buy the corebook for Beast so I can research the mechanics for this fan project and let go of my old boycott.<br /> <br /> BUT with everyone assuming the worst in me, I'm just going to say &quot;Fuck it&quot; and stick to Hunter: The Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T09:52:03-07:00","id":1297529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297526#post1297526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, maybe I should be more clear in the OP...<br /> <br /> I might be willing to buy the corebook for Beast so I can research the mechanics for this fan project and let go of my old boycott.<br /> <br /> BUT with everyone assuming the worst in me, I'm just going to say &quot;Fuck it&quot; and stick to Hunter: The Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all honesty, I can't recommend it to you. There's plenty of themes and tones that just are not your thing. I'm not talking about what you <i>think </i>it's in there, I'm talking about I know there is and the fact I've been around here for more than a decade and have a rather clear idea of what you enjoy and what you don't.<br /> <br /> And no, it's not a criticism of you or assuming the worse, it's me saying &quot;Camilla, I appreciate the will to give it a try, but I really do think you'd waste your money&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to give Beast a chance as a whole, go for it. Especially with PDFs: I loved the core but I'm the first to admit each supplement helps this gameline immensely. The mechanics are also cool. But if you're looking for something to use for a fan project, I think your resources would be better used elsewhere (because there are arguably closer starting points to what you aim for than Beast).<br /> <br /> In the same way my friends warn me about series or comics they think I would not like, I swear. I still watch and read some, but I'm often thankful they told me in the first place.<br /> <br /> EDIT: But the choice is <i><b>obviously</b></i> yours and you can even do it and come back here with renewed knowledge to criticize Beast, just so we're clear. I'd be ok with it. Hell, I'd consider it a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-17-2019, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:26:36-07:00","id":1297558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297517#post1297517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody want help you with your demand: this is the real answer, i guess.<br /> I only read non-compliance about your vision. 3 page of critics and none idea for your personal idea.<br /> I doubt that here you can take any help, the mass of users &quot;need&quot; to invalidate any sense of your personal choice over any other concern.<br /> I am sadded by this.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297433#post1297433\">is</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297437#post1297437\">profoundly</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297297#post1297297\">untrue</a>. Those are just a few examples that point out things they see as problematic or give suggestions. Furthermore, telling someone &quot;Hey, that thing you wanna do with x? You can easily get that with y!&quot; as a few here did, IS helping someone achieve their goal, albeit in different way. I'd also like to point out that you yourself didn't provide any sort of support for his vision in favour of an uncalled-for comment against the other posters, which I too consider rather rude. That this is your only comment in this thread doesn't really help matters, because to me, that makes it feel like you just came here to complain about this perceived lack of help.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> <br /> I'll try not to repeat what others said too much.<br /> Being as clear as possible in the OP helps, especially if you were boycotting the gameline so far and the other stuff. The written word is an instrument that isn't optimal for communication, because it leaves a lot open to interpretation. Reading the same e-mail while happy or angry or sad would yield different interpretations of what you consider the intended message to be. And people tend to base their interpretations on their available knowledge. Had you included &quot;I am considering getting the core for this fansplat to research Hero abilities etc.&quot;, the tone of some messages might've been quite a bit different. (This is my personal interpretation of the posts of this thread, obviously.)<br /> <br /> I think playing a Hero-focused game is more problematic than making up a Hunter conspiracy. Not that we don't have sympathetic Heroes (and the Core explicitly states that it tends to focus on low-Integrity varieties, because those are the ones Beasts tend to clash with; high-Integrity ones get little wordcount due to being not too relevant), so you'd have something you could build on even on the core as is. But the lack of information on high-integrity Heroes and their goals/tasks (What do Heroes do when they do their job right? How do they perceive the world/their own spot in it?) would make that a bit work intense, and the themes would be a bit hard to pull off. Plus the fact that this 'subversion of a subversion' might end up quite tasteless, which would be a shame: if you invest time, you'd like to have something to show for it, I assume.<br /> As others already mentioned, in addition to problems like you'd have the lack of conflict, and conflict drives a story, you'd also have a PC or several who basically play on easy: Heroes are made to combat Beasts, their abilities help them a lot, the &quot;Kill = Powerup&quot; would escalate the PC's power quickly, and then you'd have the problem of reduced stakes: unlike e.g. Hunters, Heroes don't bleed to death, so the danger of confrontation is somewhat lessened.<br /> If you take Hunter and go from there, you'll get your result much quicker and cleaner, and can save money (you weren't very keen on getting the Core, after all, and getting it for just a fan game is a tad much, I'd think, even if that might make you appreciate the game more than you do now).<br /> Being the Hero that hunts monsters also would basically require you to make Beasts more sympathetic if you don't want to drift into a clearcut black-and-white game (which gets boring quickly imo). To me, what makes these games the most fun is the different layers: is a Beast Ravager that throws bricks into rich peoples houses worse than a Kindred that feeds on their blood? A Promethean Cathar that studies the underworld by taking part in drug-deals and robberies? Why/why not? Not the answer, but the reasoning of the people making those answers is what makes this interesting.<br /> One example: PC's come to find the bloody trails of a Beast in their city. They meet with Hunters to get some information.<br /> One Hunter cell considers Beasts the worst, because they put themselves on a pedestal, 'teaching' through pain and fear, robbing people of their agency and scaring them for life.<br /> Another thinks they're pretty much harmless, because they don't cause as much 'harm': they don't tend to turn people into Vitae-junkies, they don't tend to accidentally kill people (as much as Kindred for example), and they don't suddenly lose control and murder someone because they were surprised by them lighting a cigarette or something - all they do is give people some fright, maybe some bruises (I exaggerate, this is an IC point of view). Both valid opinions.<br /> Now you have an Eshmaki that feeds by beating people up - but he focuses on people brutalizing other people, so mobsters, human traffikers, pimps and the occasional Kindred.<br /> Cell 1 wants to see the Eshmaki dead.<br /> Cell 2 thinks he's a piece of shit, but a useful one. Is there a clearcut answer to this scenario? I don't think so. That's what would make your characters' decision interesting and fun.<br /> A Hunter's answers could range from 'It is a supernatural abomination and thus must die!' (sounds kinda speciesist, though), to &quot;It harms fellow humans, so it is a threat, who knows what it'll do when it runs out of prey/finds easier targets?&quot; to &quot;Let's see if we can find some understanding...&quot; or even &quot;Hell, keeps some scum off my back AND makes the area a nicer place for the kids? Let 'im do his thing!', depending on what brought them to the Hunt in the first place, their lives, etc.<br /> A Hero on a quest to kill Beasts doesn't have as much wiggle room here, and might end up with more simplistic answers because &quot;it's their role&quot;: &quot;he probably also does worse things we don't know about&quot;, &quot;they all do worse sometime&quot;, &quot;It's regrettable, but it must be done&quot; or somesuch (the last of which at least carries some potential for an interesting chronicle imo). He is less likely to consider the impact of the Beast on this society, because 'Heroes bring wisdom and glory' after facing the monster, the monster doesn't bring safety and happiness. He is less likely to consider the Beast trying to make the best out of a shitty situation (and having to break people's boney or uncontrollably torment your loved ones with nightmares IS a shitty situation, especially if the guy isn't really suited to fighting and basically only makes it out of those thanks to spending Satiety on Relentless Hunter, forcing him to feed more often). A Hero is less likely to decide Cell 2 has a point and just leave the guy alone, or meet them, size them up, and establish a common understanding or something. Because they have something akin to a God-given mandate to hunt those beings. They're called to do so. This is slightly coloured by my perception of low-Integrity Heroes, so take it with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> <br /> tl;dr: Imho, the thematic clashes would be less interesting than what you'd get using Hunter is what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:48:01-07:00","id":1297561,"title":"","content":"To chime in:<br /> <br /> If you want to play a game of &quot;people who hunt wicked Monsters&quot;, that's basically what Hunter is.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep Beast, but have the opposite side as equally valid, I can offer some hacks, but they require Beast mechanics (and so, won't do any good without the Core Book).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T13:52:37-07:00","id":1297575,"title":"","content":"The more I consider this, the more I am thinking I should have worded my OP much better than I did and maybe I'm better off just sticking to Hunter: The Vigil for what I am aiming for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T14:35:18-07:00","id":1297586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297575#post1297575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more I consider this, the more I am thinking I should have worded my OP much better than I did and maybe I'm better off just sticking to Hunter: The Vigil for what I am aiming for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take this is a setback, and instead see it more as a shortcut to what you ultimately want to achieve (Revision is a big part of the writing process, after all). More good homebrew is good for all of us, and another good Beast-focused Hunter conspiracy would be something everyone in this subforum would enjoy to see and maybe use =)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T16:12:52-07:00","id":1297600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297517#post1297517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <di