r?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>let it go, the dude who typed that literally only posted that, he hasn't been on here since","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T23:43:56-07:00","id":1297650,"title":"","content":"something something standing in a hell of their own making and asking why it's hot.<br /> <br /> The real question is pretty legit &quot;How many times do we have to teach you this lesson, old man?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T01:00:56-07:00","id":1297655,"title":"","content":"It is very simple: if you can &amp; would give a help with Camilla's Idea, do it.<br /> You cant? You would not? Dont post.<br /> 4 page almost of spam.Good luck, i am sorry for this Camilla: i have no idea for your project but feel for you.<br /> This was a creative topic, now is a shoot and be shooted. I am the only one that see this as a problem, i see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 03-18-2019, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T04:16:28-07:00","id":1297685,"title":"","content":"In my defense, I could have worded my opening post a LOT better than I did now that I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T08:26:33-07:00","id":1297729,"title":"","content":"So do that now. Identify what it is you actually want to do and edit the OP with a new opening that says that (but also add a note that it was changed due to feedback and then link up to the point where you have made the change so new readers can jump ahead if they want).<br /> <br /> That said, I think you need to work out what you actually want. You don't like Beast based on some early release and core themes, so why make a game based on it? What about it DO you like? How do you feel a new gameline that is about good guys fighting bad guys will fit into ChroD? What are the Themes and Moods of the game? What is the External conflict? What is the Internal conflict?<br /> <br /> These are the things that you need to answer to start creating a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T09:47:55-07:00","id":1297747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297655#post1297655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is very simple: if you can &amp; would give a help with Camilla's Idea, do it.<br /> You cant? You would not? Dont post.<br /> 4 page almost of spam.Good luck, i am sorry for this Camilla: i have no idea for your project but feel for you.<br /> This was a creative topic, now is a shoot and be shooted. I am the only one that see this as a problem, i see.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) He asked for feedback on an idea. He got it. We helped him by giving honest answers with critical feedback about the idea.<br /> 2) This is not an isolated affair, and dealing with it as though it were doesn't help anyone and disregards Cam.<br /> <br /> Everything brought to the table has been paid for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T10:35:24-07:00","id":1297762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297650#post1297650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something something standing in a hell of their own making and asking why it's hot.<br /> <br /> The real question is pretty legit &quot;How many times do we have to teach you this lesson, old man?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not going to lie, you're showing signs of near-obsessive hatred of me and it's creeping me the fuck out.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be your enemy or your rival, and if anything I'd like to make peace","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T11:39:39-07:00","id":1297777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297601#post1297601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> let it go, the dude who typed that literally only posted that, he hasn't been on here since</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Based on their subsequent reply, I'm guessing they're trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T16:34:42-07:00","id":1297828,"title":"","content":"So out of curiosity Cam, what <i>does</i> your idea of a game session look like, anyways? I know what the media you like are, but I can't actually imagine what an ideal game session run by you would look like. Like, what's a hook, twist, and climax you'd run for a night? What are some action set pieces you'd like to get out, and what does the space between them look like?<br /> <br /> Genuinely curious, and it might help with understanding your problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T17:10:47-07:00","id":1297832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297828#post1297828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So out of curiosity Cam, what <i>does</i> your idea of a game session look like, anyways? I know what the media you like are, but I can't actually imagine what an ideal game session run by you would look like. Like, what's a hook, twist, and climax you'd run for a night? What are some action set pieces you'd like to get out, and what does the space between them look like?<br /> <br /> Genuinely curious, and it might help with understanding your problems.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is actually a very good question.<br /> <br /> I've never really ran a prolonged campaign as I don't have many gaming buddies IRL (I live in a fairly remote area nowadays) and I've always been a player more than a GM, and I get intimidated and lose confidence in myself when I try to get an online campaign up and running.<br /> <br /> But if I had things my way, I would imagine there would be a lot of in-character interaction and heavy RP and immersion. Players talking to each other and having conversations in character as well as extended dialogue and conversations between PC's and NPC's, I like the idea of NPC's being at least somewhat detailed enough for players to interact with through RP.<br /> <br /> I know it sounds weird given my disdain for personal horror and angst, but it's part of how I play WoD and CofD, namely since most of my experience with WoD/CofD IRL has been through LARP, I'm a role-player at heart and I really like getting into character.<br /> <br /> But I also like a sense of style, action and combat and looking cool while doing it. For some reason, there is a large portion of the WoD/CofD fanbase that thinks these things are inherently bad when in all honesty, I love the idea of intense combat scenes interspersed with heavy RP in the non-combat scenes (which would ideally be longer than the combat scenes)<br /> <br /> I unironically love katanas and anime, and even the whole trenchcoat ninja style. Partly it's because the &quot;serious personal horror&quot; crowd irrationally hates that stuff, but also because I always enjoyed it unironically despite what everyone else thinks about it. The fact that I didn't vomit in disgust at the mere thought of a character having a katana or not being insufferably angsty is part of what sparked this whole debacle way back in 2010 (the old White Wolf Forums were a lot more hostile than Onyx Path and moderation was also more arbitrary)<br /> <br /> Basically, I want a game that is somewhat serious but also fun. It's not totally &quot;lol random Dudes of Legend&quot; but also not &quot;Woe is me! Downer endings are mandatory and anything else is Trenchcoat-and-Katana bad wrong fun&quot; either<br /> <br /> I also don't like the brash contrarianism of the Punk ethos (and the subculture said mindset spawned from) which seems ironic given my history here, but between IRL and online experiences, I just find the whole punk thing to be a major red flag of something to avoid.<br /> <br /> The kind of hook would be a story of redemption and salvation (in the case of Vampire and Changeling) or a story of adventure and danger (in the case of Hunter, Princess, or Heroes) with a clear and present evil (Belial's Brood, Privateers, True Fae, Beasts, groups like Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club) to be either a powerful temptation in a game like Vampire or a dangerous enemy to be defeated in the case of a game like Hunter or Mage. <br /> <br /> Of course, the climax of a game session could either be a crucial revelation in the plot or a good old-fashioned skirmish, with an ideal twist being the tried and true &quot;Bigger Bad&quot; (like a group of Beasts or the local Brood thugs being mere pawns of a larger group like the Invictus or The Ascending Ones) or being betrayed and deceived by a supposed ally or accomplice.<br /> <br /> I know I'm simple-minded and probably cliched, but we all have to start somewhere and to be honest, as much as I lash out on here, I lash out even more towards myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T17:48:50-07:00","id":1297836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297832#post1297832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The kind of hook would be a story of redemption and salvation (in the case of Vampire and Changeling) or a story of adventure and danger (in the case of Hunter, Princess, or Heroes) with a clear and present evil (Belial's Brood, Privateers, True Fae, Beasts, groups like Ashwood Abbey and the Hunt Club) to be either a powerful temptation in a game like Vampire or a dangerous enemy to be defeated in the case of a game like Hunter or Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing though, none of the lines of chronicle of darkness has a clear manichean Good guys vs Bad guys, sure there are some antagonist that are clearly monstrous or inhumane, but the protagonist of those stories aren't shinning knights in armor or romantic heroes. Even the most noble hunter still has to face the fact that he has to sometimes murder other sentient being that may even have been human once or still act as if they were. <br /> <br /> You can have a Hero or Hunter going against a Beast that scare the living shit of childs that live in their neighborhood but then what, they don't physcally harms the child, and maybe they try to control their unger but don't quite manage to keep it under control, do they deserve to die for having atavistic need that they cannot ignore ? Do they deserve to die because of what they are and not who they are ? Do you deserve to die for your diet and the pain you might cause to other beings ? Is anything sentient bieng that isn't human inherently evil , or can they have a place in the metaphysical eco system of the world ? <br /> <br /> That the kind of question Chronicle and Beast is about, it's totally fine to want a game where you're playing the good guys and the antagonisty of the story is clearly and litteraly evil, but i don't think that Beast's Heroes of Chronicle of Darkness is the game for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:13:37-07:00","id":1297838,"title":"","content":"I would like to reiterate that, again, I'm asking what <i>exactly</i> would a session look like?<br /> <br /> To give a comparison, let's say I need to run a game of Beast tonight, got four hours. I decide to lean into both my background, my group's background, and some of the stuff going on in my house, like Devil May Cry 5.<br /> <br /> So make a session look like this:<br /> <br /> My hook: A changeling is escaping a hunting party of Loyalists, and our play group manages to catch a bit of this, following the runners back into the Hedge. Whoever this changeling is, they are wanted <i>badly</i>, and it's going to take a more than just a big hit to get the hunters off the changeling's case-the session will be sort of about creating a brutal but effective deception.<br /> My twist: The changeling in question managed to escape by scapegoating someone important to the group(I'll reference a former pc to quickly make this Important For the Players) over into the Stranger's hands, and did so because fear and opportunity can lead to bad decisions. So now we've got a question of justice vs mercy.<br /> My climax: it ultimately matters how they respond to the twist, but regardless, I can trust my group to also want make it clear as hell that any fuckers coming for them and theirs from Arcadia is going to pay with blood and terror. They might give the guy back, they might fake his death, they might do anything, but we do have a confrontation with the hunters to make it clear they need to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Action scenes: So everyone loves the motorcycle from DMC 5, and that just gets us into the mood for a ridiculous and badass chase scene, so I figure we'll have an admixture of motorcycles and ridiculously fast hobgoblins in the Hedge. I decide I'll bullshit and give the crew a limited ability to do Hedge Shaping, because they haven't been able to play Changeling 2 yet and that's badass. I also have a vague desire to do a concrete, neon and rain sort of scene for the finale, with the vague framing of the theater involved. No particular action for it, but the vague image is awesome enough.<br /> Downtime: Man, there has got to be a bar here, because this reminds me of that old Changeling short story, Root Beer.<br /> <br /> And that's enough that I can start working a game in the evening.<br /> <br /> Soooooo what would a session with you look like? What does a rollicking story of redemption and salvation look like at the table of Cam?<br /> (Also, has anyone pointed out how weird it is to like redemption/salvation stories but not like personal drama and angst? The narratives of the former tend to drip with the latter elements.)<br /> <br /> (Also, not play too much into a pure evil/good dichotomy, but in defense of Cam here, it's worth noting that this scenario <i>is </i>actually pretty black and white on the whole, with the one point that allows for redemption and salvation to be a thing.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-18-2019, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:22:42-07:00","id":1297841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297836#post1297836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing though, none of the lines of chronicle of darkness has a clear manichean Good guys vs Bad guys, sure there are some antagonist that are clearly monstrous or inhumane, but the protagonist of those stories aren't shinning knights in armor or romantic heroes. Even the most noble hunter still has to face the fact that he has to sometimes murder other sentient being that may even have been human once or still act as if they were. <br /> <br /> You can have a Hero or Hunter going against a Beast that scare the living shit of childs that live in their neighborhood but then what, they don't physcally harms the child, and maybe they try to control their unger but don't quite manage to keep it under control, do they deserve to die for having atavistic need that they cannot ignore ? Do they deserve to die because of what they are and not who they are ? Do you deserve to die for your diet and the pain you might cause to other beings ? Is anything sentient bieng that isn't human inherently evil , or can they have a place in the metaphysical eco system of the world ? <br /> <br /> That the kind of question Chronicle and Beast is about, it's totally fine to want a game where you're playing the good guys and the antagonisty of the story is clearly and litteraly evil, but i don't think that Beast's Heroes of Chronicle of Darkness is the game for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>this is some good feedback. If I may add, Beast is actually a lot more in the grey area for BOTH sides than many people seem to think. for every beast controlling their urges, there is another who fully embraced their monstrous side with no care for lessons. for every hero killing every beast no matter how good, there is a Hero who is killing truly monstrous beast (and I would argue that a Knight templar of a Hero fighting a monstrous Beast is the better side).<br /> <br /> lastly, while heroes are less aware of what their condition is, the gameline (and from the perspective of some beasts, in fact) acknowledges that Beast may not be as right as they believe themselves to be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T18:50:31-07:00","id":1297852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297838#post1297838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to reiterate that, again, I'm asking what <i>exactly</i> would a session look like?<br /> <br /> To give a comparison, let's say I need to run a game of Beast tonight, got four hours. I decide to lean into both my background, my group's background, and some of the stuff going on in my house, like Devil May Cry 5.<br /> <br /> So make a session look like this:<br /> <br /> My hook: A changeling is escaping a hunting party of Loyalists, and our play group manages to catch a bit of this, following the runners back into the Hedge. Whoever this changeling is, they are wanted <i>badly</i>, and it's going to take a more than just a big hit to get the hunters off the changeling's case-the session will be sort of about creating a brutal but effective deception.<br /> My twist: The changeling in question managed to escape by scapegoating someone important to the group(I'll reference a former pc to quickly make this Important For the Players) over into the Stranger's hands, and did so because fear and opportunity can lead to bad decisions. So now we've got a question of justice vs mercy.<br /> My climax: it ultimately matters how they respond to the twist, but regardless, I can trust my group to also want make it clear as hell that any fuckers coming for them and theirs from Arcadia is going to pay with blood and terror. They might give the guy back, they might fake his death, they might do anything, but we do have a confrontation with the hunters to make it clear they need to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Action scenes: So everyone loves the motorcycle from DMC 5, and that just gets us into the mood for a ridiculous and badass chase scene, so I figure we'll have an admixture of motorcycles and ridiculously fast hobgoblins in the Hedge. I decide I'll bullshit and give the crew a limited ability to do Hedge Shaping, because they haven't been able to play Changeling 2 yet and that's badass. I also have a vague desire to do a concrete, neon and rain sort of scene for the finale, with the vague framing of the theater involved. No particular action for it, but the vague image is awesome enough.<br /> Downtime: Man, there has got to be a bar here, because this reminds me of that old Changeling short story, Root Beer.<br /> <br /> And that's enough that I can start working a game in the evening.<br /> <br /> Soooooo what would a session with you look like? What does a rollicking story of redemption and salvation look like at the table of Cam?<br /> (Also, has anyone pointed out how weird it is to like redemption/salvation stories but not like personal drama and angst? The narratives of the former tend to drip with the latter elements.)<br /> <br /> (Also, not play too much into a pure evil/good dichotomy, but in defense of Cam here, it's worth noting that this scenario <i>is </i>actually pretty black and white on the whole, with the one point that allows for redemption and salvation to be a thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I got you. I was confused at first but yeah, give me a minute to think it out and I can definitely outline my idea of an ideal game session for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T21:29:14-07:00","id":1297881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297832#post1297832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that I didn't vomit in disgust at the mere thought of a character having a katana or not being insufferably angsty is part of what sparked this whole debacle way back in 2010</div> </div> </div> </div>To be brief, blunt, and minimally off-topic:<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>No, Cam, the fact that you <i>keep saying shit like this unprompted </i>is part of what sparked this whole debacle</b>, and your having maintained this behavior for nearly a decade has made several people very impatient with you over it because after this long it starts to look like you're either wholly incapable of thinking about what you're saying or actively trying to make people angry.<br /> <br /> Your opinions on your own idea of personal horror are known to many and do not need to share posting real-estate with questions and ideas about adjusting published content to suit your needs or taking cues from it to make your own material. As I told you some time ago, it's seldom the case that people need to know what your homebrew <i>isn't</i>\u200b.<br /> <br /> That out of the way\u2026<br /> <br /> If you absolutely <i>must</i> try to turn the recurring antagonist role of Beast on its head and aren't fussed about &quot;local nobody becomes glorious monster-slayer&quot; being the furthest thing from a fresh take, you could play into the Hero-Beast adversarial relationship by cutting out the middleman halfway through; if you're set on painting Heroes as near-universally justified then there's no need to root the Begotten in a single consistent human character.<br /> <br /> Lean on the fact that the Horror is a psychic entity from the collective unconscious \u2014 each one of the Astral entities called the Insatiable forms in response to a Hero's confrontation with the very idea of fear (or the power vacuum of such a creature being slain by its nemesis). The Lair remains consistent, but the Horror takes root among mortal wickedness and supernatural monstrosity, spreading fear and destruction until forced to retreat by the loss of its footholds, cornered into physical reality by the loss of its stronghold, or killed in the heart of its dream-fortress.<br /> <br /> Advancement then proceeds normally by tracking down the core of a given predatory idea and ending its hold on a population, at which point the character gets some boon that makes it easier for them to fight monsters but pushes a wedge between them and normal humans \u2014 and on a long enough timescale, maybe a Hero who lets the glory of their legend cloud their judgment lets another Hero's nemesis into their heart.<br /> <br /> There's a gameplay loop to be had there, and the existing mechanics for Heroes are sufficiently simple that you can scale growth to taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T23:15:17-07:00","id":1297891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297881#post1297881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be brief, blunt, and minimally off-topic:<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>No, Cam, the fact that you <i>keep saying shit like this unprompted </i>is part of what sparked this whole debacle</b>, and your having maintained this behavior for nearly a decade has made several people very impatient with you over it because after this long it starts to look like you're either wholly incapable of thinking about what you're saying or actively trying to make people angry.<br /> <br /> Your opinions on your own idea of personal horror are known to many and do not need to share posting real-estate with questions and ideas about adjusting published content to suit your needs or taking cues from it to make your own material. As I told you some time ago, it's seldom the case that people need to know what your homebrew <i>isn't</i>\u200b.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth.<br /> <br /> I like Katanas. I like Trenchcoats. I like characters who have fun as much as I love characters dealing with their own shit and the stuff tossed on them. I like <i>Devil May Cry</i>, for Pete's sake. I imagine a lot of people enjoy all of these things. I imagine they enjoy these kinds of things while still enjoying what Chronicles is.<br /> <br /> The problem is not the surfaces, images, icons, and styles you like. Hell, at this point, it's not even the perspectives that reject depth anymore (though your rejection of the weird ass things you do make you come off as shallow, man).<br /> <br /> It's that this shit is old and often doesn't have a place in any of the conversations you bring it up in. It doesn't have a place <i>here in your own homebrew thread</i>.<i> You are distracting yourself from what you set out to do</i>.<br /> <br /> Positive, negative, or otherwise, feedback will be provided when asked for-but people are going to stop when all anyone is doing is pissing into the wind.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Again I find myself having to ask the question of what, exactly, did you think was going to happen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-19-2019, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T00:58:22-07:00","id":1297902,"title":"","content":"Also, I want to nip something here, provide some validation before cutting it off:<br /> <br /> It's okay to hate things, and even sit down and seriously talk about what you think is wrong with something. No one says you have to like, say, Beast the Primordial or even not critique it.<br /> <br /> But if this thread is, shall we say, a typical example of how the OP handles these discussions, I want to take a second to just say, by contrast,<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/950278-dissecting-transgression-arcane-reviews-genius\">this is how <i>I</i> shat on a popular piece of media.</a><br /> <br /> Now, I'm not saying you have to write 23,500+ words to make it okay, but you will notice that there is a difference between that thread and this one.<br /> <br /> You'll also notice the post in question has 20 likes.<br /> <br /> <i>Just saying.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T01:15:13-07:00","id":1297903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vernuf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297777#post1297777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Based on their subsequent reply, I'm guessing they're trolling.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If Someone said they wanted to make a game about vampires and then started describing it as about fighitng off an inner beast and deal with slow degeneration into a mindless creature and I'd suggest they look at Requiem or Masquerade. Vigil provides all the tools needed to play people who hunt Beasts or even Beast strawmen or what have you without having to buy a who new book the GM seems to dislike?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T03:39:07-07:00","id":1297916,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, while I reacted to Camilla's post much like Satchel... I realized something:<br /> <br /> The only thing that Beast, and playing as Beasts, is missing from what Camilla wants out of a gaming session.... is a reason to use katanas. Beast favors Athletics and Brawl for combat focused characters to keep up with their theme as bestial creatures that use their bodies to fight instead of weapons. Otherwise everything, even the &quot;doing it because I get a kick out of pissing certain people off for playing what they think is badwrongfun,&quot; you can get out of just playing Beast.<br /> <br /> Reasons for lots of immersive RP and social interactions? Check. The crossover and brood mechanics give a strong game play loop that puts mechanical goodies as rewards for engaging in this. If you want those fun Nightmares and Kinship Merits... you need to go have your PC have all that social RP to form the bonds that like to the Condition that leads to access to those.<br /> <br /> Atavism focused combat Beasts are insanely intense combatants that with strong style and lots of action. Sure you'll get more Attack on Titan (as a Titan Shifter), Parasyte, or Tokyo Ghoul in visual/action themes than you'd get trench coats and katanas... but like I said the katanas are the lacking part... there's plenty of cool clothes in those anime.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Beast that compels the Begotten to be &quot;woe is me&quot; about anything. Their response to being part of a cycle of violence that's supposed to end with them dying is presented not as &quot;alas what a poor fate we have,&quot; but, &quot;fuck that noise, I'm not dying because some narrative says so.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game has explicit endings to aim for in the Inheritances, and you can actively pursue the &quot;good&quot; ones while avoiding the &quot;downer&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find the Beast fans around here particularly upset at the idea of an action heavy Beast game because... it's pretty damn common for Beasts to get violent.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't actually &quot;brash contrarianism&quot; or even all that punk. Yes, Beasts reject the monomyth... but because it says they're supposed to die just for existing. &quot;I want the right to live because I am what I am, and that shouldn't be a death sentence,&quot; isn't really all that contrarian or punk to assert. Plus Beasts get their power from being the ones with power, not fighting the ones with power as punk encourages as an aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about redemption and salvation as irresponsible Beasts, or ones stuck at Satiety 0, are brought back to their senses to live a more balanced life.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about adventure and danger as they explore the world around them, their kin, and their enemies.<br /> <br /> There are clear and present &quot;evil&quot; things to fight in the Insatiable, plus any of the equally irredeemable bad guys from the other game lines Beasts might get drawn into fighting; Beasts are awesome allies to have for most supernaturals when it comes to fighting things like the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So... the katana aesthetic (which isn't disallowed, just not effective)... is really all that's missing.<br /> <br /> Yet Camilla hates the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T04:52:52-07:00","id":1297922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297916#post1297916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, while I reacted to Camilla's post much like Satchel... I realized something:<br /> <br /> The only thing that Beast, and playing as Beasts, is missing from what Camilla wants out of a gaming session.... is a reason to use katanas. Beast favors Athletics and Brawl for combat focused characters to keep up with their theme as bestial creatures that use their bodies to fight instead of weapons. Otherwise everything, even the &amp;quot;doing it because I get a kick out of pissing certain people off for playing what they think is badwrongfun,&amp;quot; you can get out of just playing Beast.<br /> <br /> Reasons for lots of immersive RP and social interactions? Check. The crossover and brood mechanics give a strong game play loop that puts mechanical goodies as rewards for engaging in this. If you want those fun Nightmares and Kinship Merits... you need to go have your PC have all that social RP to form the bonds that like to the Condition that leads to access to those.<br /> <br /> Atavism focused combat Beasts are insanely intense combatants that with strong style and lots of action. Sure you'll get more Attack on Titan (as a Titan Shifter), Parasyte, or Tokyo Ghoul in visual/action themes than you'd get trench coats and katanas... but like I said the katanas are the lacking part... there's plenty of cool clothes in those anime.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Beast that compels the Begotten to be &amp;quot;woe is me&amp;quot; about anything. Their response to being part of a cycle of violence that's supposed to end with them dying is presented not as &amp;quot;alas what a poor fate we have,&amp;quot; but, &amp;quot;fuck that noise, I'm not dying because some narrative says so.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The game has explicit endings to aim for in the Inheritances, and you can actively pursue the &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; ones while avoiding the &amp;quot;downer&amp;quot; ones.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find the Beast fans around here particularly upset at the idea of an action heavy Beast game because... it's pretty damn common for Beasts to get violent.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't actually &amp;quot;brash contrarianism&amp;quot; or even all that punk. Yes, Beasts reject the monomyth... but because it says they're supposed to die just for existing. &amp;quot;I want the right to live because I am what I am, and that shouldn't be a death sentence,&amp;quot; isn't really all that contrarian or punk to assert. Plus Beasts get their power from being the ones with power, not fighting the ones with power as punk encourages as an aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about redemption and salvation as irresponsible Beasts, or ones stuck at Satiety 0, are brought back to their senses to live a more balanced life.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about adventure and danger as they explore the world around them, their kin, and their enemies.<br /> <br /> There are clear and present &amp;quot;evil&amp;quot; things to fight in the Insatiable, plus any of the equally irredeemable bad guys from the other game lines Beasts might get drawn into fighting; Beasts are awesome allies to have for most supernaturals when it comes to fighting things like the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So... the katana aesthetic (which isn't disallowed, just not effective)... is really all that's missing.<br /> <br /> Yet Camilla hates the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This post amused me greatly, thanks!<br /> To use Katana, just make a Lightning Strike using beast, potentially with Eye of heaven and weakness exposed, works great with swords <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:00:11-07:00","id":1297954,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> raised an excellent point. If we moved from talking about Cam's OP idea towards the topic of their preferenceres in gaming *, then Beast has less obstacles to get there than others, at least in relative terms.<br /> <br /> Heavy Arms said the most of it, but I want to reiterate it's ridiculously easy to do play Beast as an action-heavy, even animesque game with little amounts of inner conflicts. I mean, you have character whose souls are empowered by monsters, encouraged to interact with other gamelines' friends &amp; foes, and whose special abilities tend to be rather spectacular and impactful, if not always destructive.<br /> <br /> It takes very little to shift away from the sort of conflicts and tones Cam dislikes and focus on others, and I mean in the game as written. Don't spend much time with Heroes (perhaps only the low Integrity ones) and use other kind of antagonists. Regardless from the fact that evil Beasts can get utterly <i>vile </i>(and that's without taking Insatiables into account), you have monstrous critters from all the Inheritances and all the baddies from other gamelines ready to use.<br /> <br /> It's not unreasonable for a team of Beast to become monster hunters and use their nightmarish awesome powers to fight fire with fire and never have to worry too much of being wrong about it. Especially because, in such a packed game, there would be plenty of chances to satisfy their Hungers via &quot;righteous&quot; confrontation against bad people (and their henchmen).<br /> <br /> It's there, if you want, and it's not even a hack. For what I can attest, there's always plenty of action in my Beast games because my group needs some of that too. Sure, I decide to use some of the other tools Primordial offers as well, but I do agree that the game might be closer to aspects of what you like than you think<br /> <br /> P.S. Holy hell, this game is not perfect but I am always puzzled by what people sometimes think there actually is in these books without having read them. A degree, I can accept (even understand). Some, I admit it's true. But some other stuff? Just unexplainable.<br /> <br /> * <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> , since this has to be the first time I actually get into one of these with you: do you really have to repeat the same speech about katanas, trenchcoats and angst every single time, regardless of the topic? It's rather weird and out of nowhere. We could be speaking about typical recipes of 18th century Prussia and you'd still bring that up. I'm joking but it's true. The fact that each time the conversation gets there, and did so for pretty much 10 years, logorates any will to have a dialogue with you. I assure you that if you could only let it go here and there, people's attitude towards you would improve massively.<br /> <br /> I get that feelings sometimes are hard to get through written word but no, I'm not being hostile, I'm not being sarcastic and I'm not making fun of you. I'm saying that, in order to have a better life around here, <i>because I know it hurts you that people often don't seem to have patience for you, <b>because you said as much not long ago</b></i>, that's the simplest thing you can do and it would already do wonders. Just that.<br /> <br /> And I'm sure you won't address this point, but I had to try and tell you, because I have this stupid idea that if you've been part of this community for a while, then we're all <i>ohana </i>and do my best to care. Dumb as fuck, I know, but I can't help it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-19-2019, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:22:56-07:00","id":1297961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297903#post1297903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If Someone said they wanted to make a game about vampires and then started describing it as about fighitng off an inner beast and deal with slow degeneration into a mindless creature and I'd suggest they look at Requiem or Masquerade. Vigil provides all the tools needed to play people who hunt Beasts or even Beast strawmen or what have you without having to buy a who new book the GM seems to dislike?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say you were giving good advice. I was talking about The Throne earlier, not you. My apologies for the lack of clarity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6356,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","user":"vernuf","date":". 03-19-2019, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6356-vernuf","name":"vernuf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T08:34:57-07:00","id":1297963,"title":"","content":"So, to start answering my own questions, taken from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> s response to Arc (and ignoring the parts that others have already said just don't need to be mentioned) we have this:<br /> <br /> Themes<br /> Redemption and Salvation<br /> <br /> Moods<br /> Adventure and Danger<br /> <br /> The question now becomes Redemption and Salvation for who? The PCs? The antagonists? (Note, this does conflict with the the Clear and Present evil thing though, since it is not so clear of an evil if they can be redeemed)<br /> <br /> Assuming we are making a Heroes game, then we have clear Adventure in the hunt for Beasts and diving into their Lairs. Danger has some mechanical issues with the way Heroes are currently written as others have said since they get so much stronger with each Beast kill, but maybe an escalating power level to absurd degrees works for Camilla's gametype preference","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:37:54-07:00","id":1297980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297916#post1297916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, while I reacted to Camilla's post much like Satchel... I realized something:<br /> <br /> The only thing that Beast, and playing as Beasts, is missing from what Camilla wants out of a gaming session.... is a reason to use katanas. Beast favors Athletics and Brawl for combat focused characters to keep up with their theme as bestial creatures that use their bodies to fight instead of weapons. Otherwise everything, even the &quot;doing it because I get a kick out of pissing certain people off for playing what they think is badwrongfun,&quot; you can get out of just playing Beast.<br /> <br /> Reasons for lots of immersive RP and social interactions? Check. The crossover and brood mechanics give a strong game play loop that puts mechanical goodies as rewards for engaging in this. If you want those fun Nightmares and Kinship Merits... you need to go have your PC have all that social RP to form the bonds that like to the Condition that leads to access to those.<br /> <br /> Atavism focused combat Beasts are insanely intense combatants that with strong style and lots of action. Sure you'll get more Attack on Titan (as a Titan Shifter), Parasyte, or Tokyo Ghoul in visual/action themes than you'd get trench coats and katanas... but like I said the katanas are the lacking part... there's plenty of cool clothes in those anime.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Beast that compels the Begotten to be &quot;woe is me&quot; about anything. Their response to being part of a cycle of violence that's supposed to end with them dying is presented not as &quot;alas what a poor fate we have,&quot; but, &quot;fuck that noise, I'm not dying because some narrative says so.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game has explicit endings to aim for in the Inheritances, and you can actively pursue the &quot;good&quot; ones while avoiding the &quot;downer&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find the Beast fans around here particularly upset at the idea of an action heavy Beast game because... it's pretty damn common for Beasts to get violent.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't actually &quot;brash contrarianism&quot; or even all that punk. Yes, Beasts reject the monomyth... but because it says they're supposed to die just for existing. &quot;I want the right to live because I am what I am, and that shouldn't be a death sentence,&quot; isn't really all that contrarian or punk to assert. Plus Beasts get their power from being the ones with power, not fighting the ones with power as punk encourages as an aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about redemption and salvation as irresponsible Beasts, or ones stuck at Satiety 0, are brought back to their senses to live a more balanced life.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about adventure and danger as they explore the world around them, their kin, and their enemies.<br /> <br /> There are clear and present &quot;evil&quot; things to fight in the Insatiable, plus any of the equally irredeemable bad guys from the other game lines Beasts might get drawn into fighting; Beasts are awesome allies to have for most supernaturals when it comes to fighting things like the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So... the katana aesthetic (which isn't disallowed, just not effective)... is really all that's missing.<br /> <br /> Yet Camilla hates the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disconnect expressed here is why I am really deeply curious what Cam's idea of an actual game session looks like.<br /> <br /> (Also, while not much facilitates the katana aesthetic, there's also not much that stops you from having it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297922#post1297922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This post amused me greatly, thanks!<br /> To use Katana, just make a Lightning Strike using beast, potentially with Eye of heaven and weakness exposed, works great with swords <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I always imagined this with hands because Beast, but SHIT MAN, You just made Begotten Kenshin!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-19-2019, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:50:14-07:00","id":1297989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297916#post1297916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit, while I reacted to Camilla's post much like Satchel... I realized something:<br /> <br /> The only thing that Beast, and playing as Beasts, is missing from what Camilla wants out of a gaming session.... is a reason to use katanas. Beast favors Athletics and Brawl for combat focused characters to keep up with their theme as bestial creatures that use their bodies to fight instead of weapons. Otherwise everything, even the &quot;doing it because I get a kick out of pissing certain people off for playing what they think is badwrongfun,&quot; you can get out of just playing Beast.<br /> <br /> Reasons for lots of immersive RP and social interactions? Check. The crossover and brood mechanics give a strong game play loop that puts mechanical goodies as rewards for engaging in this. If you want those fun Nightmares and Kinship Merits... you need to go have your PC have all that social RP to form the bonds that like to the Condition that leads to access to those.<br /> <br /> Atavism focused combat Beasts are insanely intense combatants that with strong style and lots of action. Sure you'll get more Attack on Titan (as a Titan Shifter), Parasyte, or Tokyo Ghoul in visual/action themes than you'd get trench coats and katanas... but like I said the katanas are the lacking part... there's plenty of cool clothes in those anime.<br /> <br /> There is nothing in Beast that compels the Begotten to be &quot;woe is me&quot; about anything. Their response to being part of a cycle of violence that's supposed to end with them dying is presented not as &quot;alas what a poor fate we have,&quot; but, &quot;fuck that noise, I'm not dying because some narrative says so.&quot;<br /> <br /> The game has explicit endings to aim for in the Inheritances, and you can actively pursue the &quot;good&quot; ones while avoiding the &quot;downer&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> You're not going to find the Beast fans around here particularly upset at the idea of an action heavy Beast game because... it's pretty damn common for Beasts to get violent.<br /> <br /> Beast isn't actually &quot;brash contrarianism&quot; or even all that punk. Yes, Beasts reject the monomyth... but because it says they're supposed to die just for existing. &quot;I want the right to live because I am what I am, and that shouldn't be a death sentence,&quot; isn't really all that contrarian or punk to assert. Plus Beasts get their power from being the ones with power, not fighting the ones with power as punk encourages as an aesthetic.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about redemption and salvation as irresponsible Beasts, or ones stuck at Satiety 0, are brought back to their senses to live a more balanced life.<br /> <br /> Beasts can be about adventure and danger as they explore the world around them, their kin, and their enemies.<br /> <br /> There are clear and present &quot;evil&quot; things to fight in the Insatiable, plus any of the equally irredeemable bad guys from the other game lines Beasts might get drawn into fighting; Beasts are awesome allies to have for most supernaturals when it comes to fighting things like the Gentry.<br /> <br /> So... the katana aesthetic (which isn't disallowed, just not effective)... is really all that's missing.<br /> <br /> Yet Camilla hates the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, I will admit that my hatred of Beast was sort of preemptive due to my personal of dislike for Black Hat Matt, a dislike that goes back years to the days of the old WW Forums back in 2010-2011 and another reason I reacted towards Beast the way that I did was the Heroes angle.<br /> <br /> Part of what set me off of Beast when it was announced was the Heroes angle. The fact that the main villains are literally called &quot;Heroes&quot; raised a red flag for me and gave me some really bad vibes.<br /> <br /> Maybe if they were called &quot;Zealots&quot; or something like that, it wouldn't be as big of a deal. Combine that with the fact that several example Heroes in the earliest Beast books were obvious straw men with unfortunate political implications and it left a bad taste in my mouth, so I preemptively boycotted it.<br /> <br /> So, I admit I judged a game without actually reading it due to my dislike of the author, which I admit was a very bad move on my part and I truly am sorry for fucking up so badly.<br /> <br /> The good news is that Black Hat Matt no longer works on this game, and if I were to invest in a copy of the core book, I could easily invoke some minor Rule Zero. Avoid the straw-manning and just call Heroes something like Fanatics or Zealots instead or focus on other baddies in the setting.<br /> <br /> Hmm...maybe I should just run a slightly different take on Beast without having to rewrite the entire game mechanics.<br /> <br /> Why need a new gameline when I can just run Beast? I think I may have found a new favorite gameline. I'm serious here too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 03-19-2019, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T09:53:28-07:00","id":1297991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297980#post1297980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, I always imagined this with hands because Beast, but SHIT MAN, You just made Begotten Kenshin!</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Glad you like it. If you want the full Wuxia feel, you can always add Wings of the Raptor.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> <br /> I'd also be curious as to what a game session you'd consider fun would look like. Think of it in terms of engineering: you describe to someone what driving the car should feel like and knowing the roads you like to drive etc. gives one an idea of what that car could look like, but seeing a similar one in action gives a much clearer impression.<br /> I am once again reminded of this: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/e4/59/e5/e459e53fd72e3b8dda0942c721a6ec06.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T10:11:12-07:00","id":1297995,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>, I will say you seem stuck to the idea that ALL heroes are zealots. this is not true. Heroes are varied, but LOW-INTEGRITY Heroes are the most likely to seek out beast just to kill them. I would suggest you read conquering heroes for a better idea of how they are (many of the Heroes are sympathetic and have goals beyond fame. one of them does not even hunt beasts at all.).<br /> <br /> another thing. Heroes are called Heroes because they represent the ancient legends. a Hero in the end does seek out to kill the monster in THEIR story, and they have powers that make them seemingly HEROIC","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T17:08:26-07:00","id":1298078,"title":"","content":"Something I see over and over is people assuming that most of what the corebook has to say about Heroes is from an objective, word of god perspective. Some of that is on the writing, it doesn't explicitly differentiate voices as well as it could. But I also feel like people tend to willfully ignore the fact that a lot of what's there is written from the biased perspectives of Beasts themselves, and should be taken with several grains of salt.<br /> <br /> Sometimes Beasts really are just evil monsters. Some humans are both evil and monstrous, and Beasts have more incentive than normal humans to inflict trauma on others.<br /> Sometimes Heroes really are justified in trying to kill them. The problem is, the Heroes that Beasts encounter disproportionately believe that they are <i>always</i> justified in trying to kill Beasts, and not all Beasts are evil. I don't think that the corebook discussed this nuance as clearly as it could, particularly in the original draft that many people used to form their opinion of the line. I also feel like many people had a knee jerk reaction to the smug, self righteous &quot;monsters good, heroes bad&quot; tone they saw, and refused to look deeper as edits and additional material clarified and improved the narrative. Which sure, they're under no obligation to do further reading if they don't like it, but we get a lot of people coming in here wanting to fix it but not read it and that gets grating.<br /> <br /> It's absolutely possible to play a heroic Beast. Goku is a pretty good example of a heroic Anakim Tyrant. He even has a Horror in the Oozaru. Loves improving himself physically and fighting strong opponents, and this sometimes leads him to take foolish risks that put others in harm's way, but he's still a kind person and a loyal friend and he saves the earth more than he endangers it.<br /> <br /> Wreck It Ralph is another good one. Designated bad guy! His narrative inescapably ends with him losing and being reviled, so he tries to venture outside it.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles setting has plenty of things that are pretty unambiguously bad to and for humanity, and it's not too hard to pick another player faction to join and fight against far worse monsters. You can even use the family dinner option to feed from their resources (indirectly) and avoid having to sate your Horror through its preferred traumas. Joining a Changeling Freehold and fending off Huntsmen is one of the easier paths to unambiguous good guy status if that's your goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T17:27:11-07:00","id":1298079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298078#post1298078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Joining a Changeling Freehold and fending off Huntsmen is one of the easier paths to unambiguous good guy status if that's your goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, I've even had an idea rattling about on a Freehold whose Bargain is with proxy-Mothra and proxy-Battra: two kaiju-Beasts who offer mutual protection to the changelings of their respective courts, because said Beasts see the changelings as their family that must be protected from the invasive True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T17:33:53-07:00","id":1298080,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> Honestly there's a reason Exalted spends so much word count talking about How Classical/Mythic heroes were seen as profoundly different from the modern take. If I met Gilgamesh in Real life I would find him equally as dangerously monsterous as anything he killed. Same with Hercules. If you have an issue with calling them &quot;Heroes&quot; perhaps you should call them &quot;Great Men&quot; because Great Men Trample the world by their nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T18:21:53-07:00","id":1298089,"title":"","content":"I think \u2018Hero\u2018 Original Men who did impressive/great Things.<br /> Kind of like when Hitler was man of the year he was a Terrible human.<br /> <br /> But he did do Impressive\u2019great\u2019 things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T18:28:27-07:00","id":1298090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297412#post1297412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the devouring makes sense to me, the human still must consciously make the decision after all (but I do agree it needs work)<br /> <br /> now that I'm calmed down, I must say if you want a &amp;quot;subversive&amp;quot; Hero game, do this. make the hero and beast relationship the same, but make heroes that are more self aware of the fact that reality is not black and white. In fact make this the core theme: heroes must maintain a proper view of morality, fight against a plain black and white view. call this Judgement or something I dont know, but dont make beasts irredeemably evil, or other monsters for that matter</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the Homecoming because it reminded my when i realized I hade Depression.i wasn\u2019t lazy I had a serious mental issues.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like saying your lazy for having broken both your legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-19T18:34:08-07:00","id":1298093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298090#post1298090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked the Homecoming because it reminded my when i realized I hade Depression.i wasn\u2019t lazy I had a serious mental issues.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s like saying your lazy for having broken both your legs.</div> </div> </div> </div>is it ok if you explain what the devouring took away? (also, I hope you are doing better now and getting whatever help you need)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T04:42:46-07:00","id":1298121,"title":"","content":"I liked the Homecoming becuase sometime shit just happens. Me Having Clinical Depression It just happens.<br /> <br /> And autism. <br /> <br /> The devouring is like if someone else is responsible for your suffering but that\u2019s not always the case Fucked up shit just happens<br /> <br /> Sometimes random horrific things happen and you don\u2019t need to tie it in to anything bigger.<br /> <br /> Like the lessons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-20-2019, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T06:04:29-07:00","id":1298129,"title":"","content":"I assume you mean homecoming is something you decide to do yourself, no other Beast pushing you toward it. but the Devouring is much the same no? you feel like there is something missing (or maybe feel something needs to go away) and when the time comes, you choose whether you reject it or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T08:22:04-07:00","id":1298148,"title":"","content":"about that im also autistic and dont like spending all my time with other people .<br /> <br /> im okay with watching a movie with my mom. school day. but i am like a Cat i like spending time with people on my own terms. and eating and resting alot.<br /> <br /> if i cat doesn't want to spend time with you. they go away.<br /> <br /> the devouring makes what should be a very private moment and involve other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T09:01:20-07:00","id":1298156,"title":"","content":"The Devouring doesn't require anyone else to be there, it's just easier/safer with someone that understands what's happening. Kinda like how figuring out you have clinical depression, and learning healthy coping mechanisms for it, usually goes a lot better with a skilled therapist in your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T09:46:20-07:00","id":1298162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298156#post1298156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Devouring doesn't require anyone else to be there, it's just easier/safer with someone that understands what's happening. Kinda like how figuring out you have clinical depression, and learning healthy coping mechanisms for it, usually goes a lot better with a skilled therapist in your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>this right here. the Devouring only made it to where beast could sense a nascent one. otherwise it's the same thing, just a new name to fit the nightmare atavistic vernacular","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:49:48-07:00","id":1298208,"title":"","content":"Well, the Begotten that's aiding in the nascent Beast's transformation can 'clear out' the soul for the Horror to inhabit the new Beast more smoothly, which is more than just sensing it happening and being a mentor figure. It doesn't change that the merging is still between the human and the Horror to create a new Beast, it just means one of the hardest steps can be handled by someone with experience.<br /> <br /> In-universe that's not always a good thing... if the experienced Beast makes a mistake and devours the soul of a soon-to-be-Beast early, they might reject the merging and die as the Horror fights the rejection.<br /> <br /> But, for me at least, on a narrative level that's a good thing to have in the game, because it makes assisted Devourings something with risk tension that's unique form the other game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T17:23:52-07:00","id":1298224,"title":"","content":"But it\u2019s called the Devouring and involved eating there Soul. I know that Souls in COfD are not the seat of your personality. But it still involves A monster eating your your soul, it just rubs my the wrong way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T17:36:01-07:00","id":1298226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298224#post1298224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it\u2019s called the Devouring and involved eating there Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>always</i> involved a monster eating your soul. The Homecoming just had your confrontation with the empty mirror in the dark serve as the culmination of a single recurring lifelong nightmare instead of an individual tipping point after a lifetime of different ways your dreams gave you bad news. The former doesn't have any truck with Family beyond the vague draws of sympathetic resonance, and the latter just emphasizes the role the outside world plays in your self-discovery. The Horror was still always going to be <i>you</i>, as far as any definition of predestination that applied to the Homecoming matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T18:23:48-07:00","id":1298239,"title":"","content":"This is also something of a shifting of the goal posts each time sort of situation.<br /> <br /> We've gone from, &quot;sometime shit just happens,&quot; being the desire, but the Devouring still works like that sometimes too.<br /> <br /> Then it's, &quot; what should be a very private moment and involve other people,&quot; which again, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Then, &quot;but it still involves A monster eating your your soul, it just rubs my the wrong way.&quot; and... we're in the &quot;too subjective to really debate&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> It feels like we've reached, &quot;I liked Homecoming a lot, but they changed it and what they changed it to doesn't really matter, because it's not Homecoming and that emotional response isn't going to be recaptured.&quot; The actual strengths and weaknesses of the two concepts doesn't matter if that's what we're dealing with. As I tend to go to as a refrain, you can't get someone that loves chocolate ice-cream to get excited about vanilla ice-cream with logic. You just hope they'll go with vanilla because it's still ice-cream.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could post all about how the Devouring resonates with me way better than Homecoming did, based on my psychiatric diagnostic journey and therapy ordeals. But that's just me saying I like vanilla better to someone that likes chocolate better. I try to focus on things like why Devouring works better as a gaming element, because it's job is to facilitate playing the game, but that only works if the goal is to discuss the merits of the concept; not just post which we have the more visceral reaction to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T19:11:31-07:00","id":1298255,"title":"","content":"SO I had somehow missed this earlier, and I wish I had continued to, but now that I've seen it, I've got to say something.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1297762#post1297762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to lie, you're showing signs of near-obsessive hatred of me and it's creeping me the fuck out.<br /> <br /> I don't want to be your enemy or your rival, and if anything I'd like to make peace</div> </div> </div> </div>Look dude. I'm not saying you have to like or be comfortable with my problems with you, because that's absurd?<br /> <br /> But at least realize that you have been doing the exact same thing <b><u><i>for a decade now</i></u></b>. Recognize what that does to a person.<br /> <br /> You don't have to like it, but at least acknowledge you bought it, and that you had plenty of other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-21-2019, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T08:09:29-07:00","id":1298331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298255#post1298255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SO I had somehow missed this earlier, and I wish I had continued to, but now that I've seen it, and I've got to say something.<br /> <br /> Look dude. I'm not saying you have to like or be comfortable with my problems with you, because that's absurd?<br /> <br /> But at least realize that you have been doing the exact same thing <b><u><i>for a decade now</i></u></b>. Recognize what that does to a person.<br /> <br /> You don't have to like it, but at least acknowledge you bought it, and that you had plenty of other options.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, I admit that I did not help things with my obsessive paranoia and spiteful attitude that led to this decade of raging.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, okay. I don't know what else to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T09:35:38-07:00","id":1298347,"title":"","content":"So, to again bring this back to an actual homebrew thread, I have added some more to the idea:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Themes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Redemption</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Salvation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mood</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Adventure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The life of a hero is rarely boring, their connection to the dream draws them to hotspots of excitement as well as repeatedly bringing calls to action to their doorstep.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Danger</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heroes very existence cause the world around them to grow more dangerous, they are always at risk if harm and their loved ones doubly so as they don't have the heroes defenses.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">What is a Hero</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#202124\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Defenders of humanity since time immemorial, heroes are those individuals with a connection to the Primordial Dream that drives them to fight evil and protect the world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Just a rough couple sentences, but a start. The Themes really need input from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a> before they can take shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T17:31:50-07:00","id":1298433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298239#post1298239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also something of a shifting of the goal posts each time sort of situation.<br /> <br /> We've gone from, &quot;sometime shit just happens,&quot; being the desire, but the Devouring still works like that sometimes too.<br /> <br /> Then it's, &quot; what should be a very private moment and involve other people,&quot; which again, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> Then, &quot;but it still involves A monster eating your your soul, it just rubs my the wrong way.&quot; and... we're in the &quot;too subjective to really debate&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> It feels like we've reached, &quot;I liked Homecoming a lot, but they changed it and what they changed it to doesn't really matter, because it's not Homecoming and that emotional response isn't going to be recaptured.&quot; The actual strengths and weaknesses of the two concepts doesn't matter if that's what we're dealing with. As I tend to go to as a refrain, you can't get someone that loves chocolate ice-cream to get excited about vanilla ice-cream with logic. You just hope they'll go with vanilla because it's still ice-cream.<br /> <br /> I mean, I could post all about how the Devouring resonates with me way better than Homecoming did, based on my psychiatric diagnostic journey and therapy ordeals. But that's just me saying I like vanilla better to someone that likes chocolate better. I try to focus on things like why Devouring works better as a gaming element, because it's job is to facilitate playing the game, but that only works if the goal is to discuss the merits of the concept; not just post which we have the more visceral reaction to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally cried when they changed the Homecoming to the Devouring .<br /> <br /> It was mostly the Straw that Broke the Camels back. And I was in a bad place.<br /> <br /> But still the change made me Upset on such a Visceral leval.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou were normal, once. At least more than you are now. You got up and went about your daily routine like anyone else \u2014 work, school, family, friends \u2014 with the same petty complaints and ambitions as anyone else you knew, except that you never quite fit in. It always felt like you stood apart from the rest of the herd; no matter how much you tried to be good, no one could argue that you had a cruel streak that ran bone deep.<br /> Then came the day when you came face to face with the monster inside you, and suddenly it all made sense. You didn\u2019t fit in with other people for the same reason a fox doesn\u2019t fit in with a room full of poodles. It wasn\u2019t cruelty in your nature: it was Hunger. Now you knew just how to feed it. Maybe it\u2019s not pretty, sating these drives, but you don\u2019t have a choice. It\u2019s not your fault you\u2019re what you are; since you can\u2019t go back, you might as well make the best of it.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-21-2019, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T18:37:28-07:00","id":1298453,"title":"","content":"That's sorta my point though? This isn't about anything wrong with the Devouring; or even if the Devouring is a worse/better thing for the game. It's about your emotional reaction to the Homecoming and there's nothing to really debate there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T18:55:22-07:00","id":1298456,"title":"","content":"Maybe they should have spent more time on the reversions? It just reeks of a slapdash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:04:56-07:00","id":1298460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists#post1297255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally, I just invoke Rule Zero and excise Beast entirely from my CofD games, but I actually had an idea recently to fix that. It's subversive and intentionally runs counter to the default themes of Beast anyway, but I was never one for thematic purism to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I\u2019m late to this party, but man... the irony of calling \u201cwhat if the HEROES were the good guys and the MONSTERS were the bad guys?!\u201d subversive is really funny to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:10:21-07:00","id":1298461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298460#post1298460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know I\u2019m late to this party, but man... the irony of calling \u201cwhat if the HEROES were the good guys and the MONSTERS were the bad guys?!\u201d subversive is really funny to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is definitely the....<i>most particular way</i> someone could have gone at the topic, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298456#post1298456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they should have spent more time on the reversions? It just reeks of a slapdash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Work timelines don't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:45:46-07:00","id":1298467,"title":"","content":"&quot;Reeks of slapdash&quot; is also a fairly meaningless phrase.<br /> <br /> To me, Homecoming is a neat idea, but it &quot;reeks&quot; of early development brainstorming that needed to be revised for the final text. People attached to it are people that are also somewhat guilty of forgetting that they're seeing the sausage getting made, and the sometimes concepts get redone/removed even in the very late development cycle.<br /> <br /> Devouring is, for me, a more mature concept that is far better suited for the game it's supposed to be part of, and even if the core writing would have been better with even more time, it is actually presented just fine.<br /> <br /> I'd wager that most people that feel Homecoming &gt; Devouring, wouldn't feel that way if they never saw the earlier version of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T19:47:22-07:00","id":1298469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298456#post1298456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe they should have spent more time on the reversions? It just reeks of a slapdash.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok now, not to insult your personal problems, but you may be seeing this on a little bit of a personal level. the devouring is able to act just the same way as homecoming, it even makes a point of this and says how beast feel they are always different. the devouring merely made it to where beast can sense and potentially influence it<br /> <br /> once again, not to offend, but you may be seeing a difference that isn't really there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:07:30-07:00","id":1298470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298467#post1298467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Reeks of slapdash&quot; is also a fairly meaningless phrase.<br /> <br /> To me, Homecoming is a neat idea, but it &quot;reeks&quot; of early development brainstorming that needed to be revised for the final text. People attached to it are people that are also somewhat guilty of forgetting that they're seeing the sausage getting made, and the sometimes concepts get redone/removed even in the very late development cycle.<br /> <br /> Devouring is, for me, a more mature concept that is far better suited for the game it's supposed to be part of, and even if the core writing would have been better with even more time, it is actually presented just fine.<br /> <br /> I'd wager that most people that feel Homecoming &gt; Devouring, wouldn't feel that way if they never saw the earlier version of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I strongly disagree with that sentiment. I really don't see why you think this is something convincing to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:16:44-07:00","id":1298473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298470#post1298470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I strongly disagree with that sentiment. I really don't see why you think this is something convincing to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> (Because I'll be honest, while I had some initial misgivings about losing Homecoming as the term, I have since come around to the ouroboros of actualization that is the Devouring <i>hard.)</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:27:33-07:00","id":1298475,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve got no skin in the Devouring vs. Homecoming race, but as a big fan of Underhill Lost, gotta say I\u2019m more sympathetic towards the folks who preferred the Homecoming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:33:01-07:00","id":1298476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298473#post1298473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How so?<br /> <br /> (Because I'll be honest, while I had some initial misgivings about losing Homecoming as the term, I have since come around to the ouroboros of actualization that is the Devouring <i>hard.)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I've.... talked about this before. I don't really think this is the thread to dig into this, again, because it doesn't really focus on the actual topic of the thread and... Honestly, I've not much patience to really dig into it. Not anything from you folks, just ongoing stuff.<br /> <br /> Sometime, when I've got my head in a better space, would creating a thread focused on discussing the Homecoming and the Devouring be helpful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:05:02-07:00","id":1298482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298475#post1298475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve got no skin in the Devouring vs. Homecoming race, but as a big fan of Underhill Lost, gotta say <b>I\u2019m more sympathetic towards the folks who preferred the Homecoming.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>...you mean the thing that was retroactively added back in (kinda-sorta) in the Beast Player's Guide?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418