But yes, Beast Player's Guide is basically filled with retroactive-errata, clarifications on existing material in the corebook made confusing by the inconsistent editing, on top of new material. Which includes talking about the Devouring...and in short making it obvious Beasts have no fucking clue what it is. Including what conditions consistently cause it. And it lists something similar to Homecoming, where pre-Devouring Beasts feel like something about them is different, and once the Devouring happens they feel at peace, having this innate sense that this was as things were meant to be.<br /> <br /> Hence why at this point, 3 years later since the final PDF has dropped and people have had time to digest the game's mechanics and themes, why people respond in frustration to people who say otherwise. The type that stopped with the KS draft or final draft, come barging in saying that they hate Beast and that they've figured out how to &quot;fix&quot; it, and expect everyone who know and like Beast to just accept their take without any sot of criticism or question? It's pure nonsense.<br /> <br /> It comes off as haters speaking from a place of ignorance. Unintentional or willful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-22-2019, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:09:02-07:00","id":1298500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298497#post1298497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah pretty much. Just a thing that happens from time to time among the Beghotten. Its still considered the Devouring just definitely on the easier side of the transitional scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>.Oh, neat!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:17:49-07:00","id":1298502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298498#post1298498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I know? I backed the KS too.<br /> <br /> But yes, Beast Player's Guide is basically filled with retroactive-errata, clarifications on existing material in the corebook made confusing by the inconsistent editing, on top of new material. Which includes talking about the Devouring...and in short making it obvious Beasts have no fucking clue what it is. Including what conditions consistently cause it. And it lists something similar to Homecoming, where pre-Devouring Beasts feel like something about them is different, and once the Devouring happens they feel at peace, having this innate sense that this was as things were meant to be.<br /> <br /> Hence why at this point, 3 years later since the final PDF has dropped and people have had time to digest the game's mechanics and themes, why people respond in frustration to people who say otherwise. The type that stopped with the KS draft or final draft, come barging in saying that they hate Beast and that they've figured out how to &amp;quot;fix&amp;quot; it, and expect everyone who know and like Beast to just accept their take without any sot of criticism or question? It's pure nonsense.<br /> <br /> It comes off as haters speaking from a place of ignorance. Unintentional or willful.</div> </div> </div> </div>OR the beast will be disappointed by what he thought was his true self and neglect and reject it to his own detriment. cant forget that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:23:12-07:00","id":1298504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298467#post1298467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd wager that most people that feel Homecoming &gt; Devouring, wouldn't feel that way if they never saw the earlier version of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>From a raw nomenclature perspective, at least, I can see an argument to be made for &quot;Homecoming&quot; being more appropriate to the outcome the line arrived at \u2014 I've pointed out before in a couple places that the original Kickstarter draft was a lot more oriented toward Beasts as self-contained and self-concerned monsters of Hunger than the supernatural fixtures of the darker world that Kinship ties onto \u2014 and there's no denying that &quot;Devouring&quot; sounds more like a thing that was done to you than a thing you happened upon in the course of living your life.<br /> <br /> The mess of connotations Homecoming was tangled up with, though, has me doubtful that its proponents aren't just talking about the cathartic resonance of the concept in isolation from its larger context, because &quot;I am what I am and I can't and won't change&quot; becomes a lot more overtly anti-aspirational when blown up into &quot;You are basically doomed to inhabit a cycle of violence wherein you and the people you associate with are increasingly likely to be serial killers and their accomplices.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:25:31-07:00","id":1298505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298470#post1298470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see why you think this is something convincing to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't?<br /> <br /> My whole point on this tangent is that we're largely in the &quot;chocolate vs. vanilla&quot; argument where people aren't discussing the pros and cons, but just reacting based on emotional reaction. I'm just pushing back on attempts to paint it as otherwise with some sort of appeal to a 'con' by calling it slapdash without further justification.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298475#post1298475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve got no skin in the Devouring vs. Homecoming race, but as a big fan of Underhill Lost, gotta say I\u2019m more sympathetic towards the folks who preferred the Homecoming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have sympathy, but that's an apples and oranges comparison. The Underhill Lost is a majorly different take on Changeling from the official 2e book.<br /> <br /> Homecoming vs. Devouring is more like debating CtL 1e's Seeming Contracts vs. CtL 2e's Seeming favored Regalia Contracts as a conceptual design.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298482#post1298482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...you mean the thing that was retroactively added back in (kinda-sorta) in the Beast Player's Guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the final BtP core book on a basic level. Rose talked about the re-writes on Chapter 2 specifically back during the KS when people were concerned with Homecoming getting changed when the Chapter 1 re-write was released, and pointed out that a Homecoming style experience was purposefully included in the Devouring section to show that the Devouring didn't take anything away.<br /> <br /> The PG just expanded on it more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:31:33-07:00","id":1298507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298504#post1298504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a raw nomenclature perspective, at least, I can see an argument to be made for &quot;Homecoming&quot; being more appropriate to the outcome the line arrived at...</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. If this was the primary argument I saw from people? I'd be less baffled by the attachment to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:32:35-07:00","id":1298508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298505#post1298505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's in the final BtP core book on a basic level. Rose talked about the re-writes on Chapter 2 specifically back during the KS when people were concerned with Homecoming getting changed when the Chapter 1 re-write was released, and pointed out that a Homecoming style experience was purposefully included in the Devouring section to show that the Devouring didn't take anything away.<br /> <br /> The PG just expanded on it more.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and yet here we are where people are still able to confuse the two and claim that Devouring is definitely-a-completely-different-thing-from-Homecoming, with no room to say otherwise without feeling like they're rewriting a bit of the setting.<br /> <br /> Even if it's already been clarified that they don't need to do that and it was there the whole time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:32:36-07:00","id":1298509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298505#post1298505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have sympathy, but that's an apples and oranges comparison. The Underhill Lost is a majorly different take on Changeling from the official 2e book.<br /> <br /> Homecoming vs. Devouring is more like debating CtL 1e's Seeming Contracts vs. CtL 2e's Seeming favored Regalia Contracts as a conceptual design</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. I probably shouldn\u2019t have said anything, I don\u2019t have enough context and just ended up putting my foot in my mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:33:30-07:00","id":1298511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298498#post1298498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I know? I backed the KS too.<br /> <br /> But yes, Beast Player's Guide is basically filled with retroactive-errata, clarifications on existing material in the corebook made confusing by the inconsistent editing, on top of new material. Which includes talking about the Devouring...and in short making it obvious Beasts have no fucking clue what it is. Including what conditions consistently cause it. And it lists something similar to Homecoming, where pre-Devouring Beasts feel like something about them is different, and once the Devouring happens they feel at peace, having this innate sense that this was as things were meant to be.<br /> <br /> Hence why at this point, 3 years later since the final PDF has dropped and people have had time to digest the game's mechanics and themes, why people respond in frustration to people who say otherwise. The type that stopped with the KS draft or final draft, come barging in saying that they hate Beast and that they've figured out how to &quot;fix&quot; it, and expect everyone who know and like Beast to just accept their take without any sot of criticism or question? It's pure nonsense.<br /> <br /> It comes off as haters speaking from a place of ignorance. Unintentional or willful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This looks like you're conflating people who are dissatisfied with the Devouring replacing the Homecoming as being the same as someone like the OP of this thread...<br /> <br /> Am I mistaken by that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:53:09-07:00","id":1298516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298511#post1298511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks like you're conflating people who are dissatisfied with the Devouring replacing the Homecoming as being the same as someone like the OP of this thread...<br /> <br /> Am I mistaken by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>More like the former can be a symptom of the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T22:54:07-07:00","id":1298518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298505#post1298505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't?<br /> <br /> My whole point on this tangent is that we're largely in the &quot;chocolate vs. vanilla&quot; argument where people aren't discussing the pros and cons, but just reacting based on emotional reaction. I'm just pushing back on attempts to paint it as otherwise with some sort of appeal to a 'con' by calling it slapdash without further justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell you what, when I make the thread for talking about this in depth, if you'd like I'll tag you into it so you're notified of it and then you can weigh in as you like about it.<br /> <br /> I'd like to keep it something civil and relaxed, with a focus on sharing rather than having the goal of trying to convince. Ultimately, it doesn't matter much, since the books are what the books are and people can handle their games however they want. But maybe it'll help with understanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:02:20-07:00","id":1298521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298516#post1298516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More like the former can be a symptom of the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>....Wow. Alright, then.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:07:28-07:00","id":1298522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298521#post1298521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ....Wow. Alright, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;can be&quot;, meaning I don't believe everyone is like that.<br /> <br /> Look, I realize that Beast has it's faults, some lingering even after BPG's release, but it's still frustrating to me that people continue base some of these perceived faults off of increasingly inaccurate information, on top of deliberately choosing not to look into the updated information.<br /> <br /> It breeds misunderstandings when there really shouldn't be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:08:09-07:00","id":1298523,"title":"","content":"So on a bit more of an on topic metric. The easiest method to play as a Hero and you know the good guy would be playing the higher integrity Heroes. The lower ones are basically defined by their desire and need to kill Beasts. Essentially Heroes sense disturbances in the Primordial Dream and are drawn to fix it, with your lower integrity Hero it becomes find the monster ,because obviously this is the work of a monster, and kill it. Your higher integrity Hero has more to them than this, so they'd have more avenues open to them than that since they'd be interpreting the feeling as something being wrong and them needing to fix it. This is probably going to end up with a weird mix of stuff from books and just my ideas, so yeah.<br /> <br /> As previously noted you are technically playing a Hunter spliced with an action hero, take that as you will. Fun note this isn't without precedent in the actual Beast line.Conquering Heroes has an ex-Hunter referred to as the Silver Smith who pretty much plays this way. Now running your character as this you'll want to decide if they've already killed a Beast, since that'll determine whether or not they have access to Anathema, just treat it the same as buying an extra dot in the supernatural stat, like Lair or whatever.<br /> <br /> Now potential conflicts in this. 1) The Quest: your character has to deal with the fact that part of their mind, their soul, their being knows they have a calling, a purpose in this world. You feel a disturbance and part of you screams that you should go fix it, the bigger the ripple the more difficult it may be to resist the urge to go and fix this even if they have no clue how they could fix things or how it might impact their own life.<br /> <br /> 2) The Beghotten and leveling up: When your lucky the Beast you've come into conflict with will make this easy. The one's that can't stand living with the gnawing hunger and the ones who've decided that its not a good meal unless everyone in a three block radius died screaming are probably going to be of minimal conflict to one's consciousness on killing and claiming the subsequent powerup. What if the problem isn't related to a Beast? Beast was local to the area and the disturbance isn't their doing, or they showed up because as a Ravager they feed on what's probably going to happen without lifting a finger when that hurricane hits. What do you do with the grey areas The Beghotten handling cleanup on Masquerade violation for a local kindred clan even if this occasionally means disposing of the odd normal human, the ones playing Dexter and making sure they only hunt bad people. If you end up teaming up with a Beast, do you kill them in the end? Hell if the Beast is about to die to something else do you kill steal that thing since you'll get a powerup for killing the Beast, and is this a thing you tell the Beghotten at the start of the teamup?<br /> <br /> 3) Other Heroes: Pretty much what it sounds like. You'll come into conflict with them, so how do you handle it? What do you do with the low integrity Heroes? These are people who've basically thrown away everything for that purpose you feel, do they scare you, do you envy them, do you pity them? Do you try to help them find more than just killing the monsters, do you just go for a non-aggression pact, what's the line you'll allow them to cross?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 03-22-2019, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T23:11:28-07:00","id":1298526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298522#post1298522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I said &quot;can be&quot;, meaning I don't believe everyone is like that.<br /> <br /> Look, I realize that Beast has it's faults, some lingering even after BPG's release, but it's still frustrating to me that people continue base some of these perceived faults off of increasingly inaccurate information, on top of deliberately choosing not to look into the updated information.<br /> <br /> It breeds misunderstandings when there really shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll say that I share in your frustration on dealing with the perception of the game some people have that isn't even based on reading the material. It definitely can be frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T01:07:37-07:00","id":1298544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298511#post1298511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This looks like you're conflating people who are dissatisfied with the Devouring replacing the Homecoming as being the same as someone like the OP of this thread...<br /> <br /> Am I mistaken by that?</div> </div> </div> </div>The two people you are discussing are completely separate, and Heavy Arms is <i>not</i> missing a distinction between the two.<br /> <br /> Cam is dissatisfied with Beast on the whole, never <i>at once</i> satisfied by what Beast was or intended to be (and before anyone jumps down my throat, that's fine, Cam's not the only one dis-satisfied with how Beast turned out, and on <i>some</i> level that is indicative of how games can never satisfy everyone at once). Konrad, by contrast, seems to really enjoy Beast, except for this one aspect that spoke to them before vs. after. Any real experience with Konrad reveals that.<br /> <br /> There are a <i>lot</i> of people who like Beast <i>after</i> the fact of the name change [and all of it's connotations] and still take issue with Devouring supplanting Homecoming, including Konrad. There are, also, a lot of people who never liked Beast, <i>even after</i> the facts of issues addressable (and addressed) <i>because they had made their minds up</i>.<br /> <br /> I think that Arms, as someone who has demonstrated, <i>rather a lot of time and time again</i> an understanding and empathy for people on both sides with also a clear understanding of both sides, <i>is not wrong in laying down a line where one is coming from good faith and one is not<u>(particularly since he has articulated his feelings on both in depth)</u></i>.<br /> <br /> Particularly since one case opposite him <b><u><i>has a long and still demonstrable case of bad faith arguments on their side.</i></u></b>(*cough*)<br /> <br /> I think assuming anyone can lump Konrad and Cam into the same category is a false assumption, and I think that's <i>really clear,</i> and I think that's <b><i><u>really kind of clear</u></i>. </b> I think, equally so, it's kind of clear where the lines exist, and who is addressing whom.<br /> <br /> ****Who wow, could I clarify on points. I won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-22-2019, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T11:06:04-07:00","id":1298667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298544#post1298544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two people you are discussing are completely separate, and Heavy Arms is <i>not</i> missing a distinction between the two.<br /> <br /> Cam is dissatisfied with Beast on the whole, never <i>at once</i> satisfied by what Beast was or intended to be (and before anyone jumps down my throat, that's fine, Cam's not the only one dis-satisfied with how Beast turned out, and on <i>some</i> level that is indicative of how games can never satisfy everyone at once). Konrad, by contrast, seems to really enjoy Beast, except for this one aspect that spoke to them before vs. after. Any real experience with Konrad reveals that.<br /> <br /> There are a <i>lot</i> of people who like Beast <i>after</i> the fact of the name change [and all of it's connotations] and still take issue with Devouring supplanting Homecoming, including Konrad. There are, also, a lot of people who never liked Beast, <i>even after</i> the facts of issues addressable (and addressed) <i>because they had made their minds up</i>.<br /> <br /> I think that Arms, as someone who has demonstrated, <i>rather a lot of time and time again</i> an understanding and empathy for people on both sides with also a clear understanding of both sides, <i>is not wrong in laying down a line where one is coming from good faith and one is not<u>(particularly since he has articulated his feelings on both in depth)</u></i>.<br /> <br /> Particularly since one case opposite him <b><u><i>has a long and still demonstrable case of bad faith arguments on their side.</i></u></b>(*cough*)<br /> <br /> I think assuming anyone can lump Konrad and Cam into the same category is a false assumption, and I think that's <i>really clear,</i> and I think that's <b><i><u>really kind of clear</u></i>. </b> I think, equally so, it's kind of clear where the lines exist, and who is addressing whom.<br /> <br /> ****Who wow, could I clarify on points. I won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... What you're quoting was not in response to Heavy Arms. It was in response to another poster, and they even further clarified their point, associating the two.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty much in agreement with what you're saying here, mind.<br /> <br /> But you're talking of Heavy Arms, while I was addressing tasti man LH. So I think there might be a little confusion here...? ^^;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T19:46:46-07:00","id":1298829,"title":"","content":"For the OP.<br /> <br /> I must agree with the others that the whole heroes hunting monsters thing is better done with Hunter or one of the many non Onyx Path games that focus on such action, like Monster of the Week. But it can be done with Beast if that is your wish and it doesnt even have to involve any changes to the game itself, you can even have your katanas and trenchcoats (an aesthetic I myself am rather fond of which is obvious in the way I dress amongst other things). With a certain build one can easily make a Beast version of Batman, vigilante hunting criminals and monsters that threathen common folk, feeding of the fears of the monsters.<br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming Vs Devouring matter I have always been on the homecoming camp. And while I do agree, grudgingly, with Heavy Arms that the whole matter is about apples and oranges and the feelings we all attach to them and thus not really worth fighting over especially now 3, has it really been that long, years into the game I still cant help feeling kinda bummed out by the nomeclanture changes made into the final draft. I just felt that the Homecoming and Soul were much more fitting and appropriate than Devouring and Horror.<br /> <br /> My problem with Devouring is that it emphasizes and implies that something comes to you and devours a part of you before replacing itself with the devoured part, I also disliked its emphasis on it being something other Beasts do to you, closing in on the whole embrace matter. Homecoming as a term sounds warm and welcoming, it in the first draft put the emphasis on how you always felt different and incomplete and now that you faced your Nightmares you realized you are those Nightmares and you have always been them, you just finally found your way back home. It also de-emphasised any outer party interference removing itself from embrace like matters where another monster makes you into a being like it.<br /> <br /> Similarly after you become a Beast and it feels correct why would you call your inner self, your true being, a Horror? It does not horrify you after all it is you. Which is why I preferred the Soul term over the Horror term.<br /> <br /> Similarly the first draft of BtP had no mentions of lessons which is what I personally preferred, and which is another matter talked about in the BPG. If Vampires have no excuse for their feeding and general bloodlust other than survival or the Uratha need no other reason to hunt other than the wolf must hunt why do the Begotten have excuses for their hunger? Beasts feed because they must, there is no need for a complicated excuse. But again this is a matter of taste and opinion and YMMV.<br /> <br /> But in the end these are just matters of taste, easily handled at each table, and they do not really affect the game itself and are thus more or less meaningless things to argue about but they can and should be matters that can be civilly discussed despite the emotional attachments we might have regarding them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T20:20:36-07:00","id":1298833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298829#post1298829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the OP.<br /> <br /> I must agree with the others that the whole heroes hunting monsters thing is better done with Hunter or one of the many non Onyx Path games that focus on such action, like Monster of the Week. But it can be done with Beast if that is your wish and it doesnt even have to involve any changes to the game itself, you can even have your katanas and trenchcoats (an aesthetic I myself am rather fond of which is obvious in the way I dress amongst other things). With a certain build one can easily make a Beast version of Batman, vigilante hunting criminals and monsters that threathen common folk, feeding of the fears of the monsters.<br /> <br /> As for the Homecoming Vs Devouring matter I have always been on the homecoming camp. And while I do agree, grudgingly, with Heavy Arms that the whole matter is about apples and oranges and the feelings we all attach to them and thus not really worth fighting over especially now 3, has it really been that long, years into the game I still cant help feeling kinda bummed out by the nomeclanture changes made into the final draft. I just felt that the Homecoming and Soul were much more fitting and appropriate than Devouring and Horror.<br /> <br /> My problem with Devouring is that it emphasizes and implies that something comes to you and devours a part of you before replacing itself with the devoured part, I also disliked its emphasis on it being something other Beasts do to you, closing in on the whole embrace matter. Homecoming as a term sounds warm and welcoming, it in the first draft put the emphasis on how you always felt different and incomplete and now that you faced your Nightmares you realized you are those Nightmares and you have always been them, you just finally found your way back home. It also de-emphasised any outer party interference removing itself from embrace like matters where another monster makes you into a being like it.<br /> <br /> Similarly after you become a Beast and it feels correct why would you call your inner self, your true being, a Horror? It does not horrify you after all it is you. Which is why I preferred the Soul term over the Horror term.<br /> <br /> Similarly the first draft of BtP had no mentions of lessons which is what I personally preferred, and which is another matter talked about in the BPG. If Vampires have no excuse for their feeding and general bloodlust other than survival or the Uratha need no other reason to hunt other than the wolf must hunt why do the Begotten have excuses for their hunger? Beasts feed because they must, there is no need for a complicated excuse. But again this is a matter of taste and opinion and YMMV.<br /> <br /> But in the end these are just matters of taste, easily handled at each table, and they do not really affect the game itself and are thus more or less meaningless things to argue about but they can and should be matters that can be civilly discussed despite the emotional attachments we might have regarding them.</div> </div> </div> </div>in the latter paragraphs, the devouring, while yes, does have the idea that the horror consumed the soul, the corebook still emphasizes that beasts feel like this is who they truly are upon meeting the Horror. now whether one regrets the choice or not is another. now that beasts can influence that choice, they dont, unlike a vampire, MAKE you into a beast. the potential was always there, just now you have a beast encouraging you to take that final step.<br /> <br /> As for lessons, it makes a lot of sense. werewolves hunt because of duty, not necessarily just because they can. it should be noted this is considered a sacred duty both just of their nature and because of abstract reasons. now for vampires, hungering for blood because you can die from not doing so is WAY different from wanting to inspire pure fear into somebody not because you'll die but because nightmares will run rampant.<br /> <br /> Lessons are there to give beasts their OWN purpose. unlike the vampire who lives his own undeath, the beast is put into a story where he is pure evil and must die. unlike a werewolf who hunts to bring balance, a beast hunts someone not for food or balance, but simply because he must give SOMETHING that fear. lessons help beasts gain individuality and the chance to be seen as more than a mere monster to be killed. and for those who think all of that is crap, they see the importance in that it refines your hunger and restrains from overfeeding (and helps with incarnate)<br /> <br /> PS: regarding the terminology, I think it honestly makes sense. beast IS horror game that has the main theme of mythic monsters and fear. homecoming and Soul is just all warm and fuzzy and to be honest, unfitting when you bring up all the other terms. the devouring and horror are a lot more visceral and definitely fit with words like atavism, nightmares, broods","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:05:11-07:00","id":1298838,"title":"","content":"Hunting for werewolves is not a duty. It's a drive that they find consuming, a complete need that must be satisfied. It's not just because they can. The Wolf <i>MUST </i>Hunt.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast slowly starve if they don't feed their Satiety. Their Horror running amuck in a desperate attempt to feed itself will happen. But if the Horror isn't successful, the Beast will die. Having the Ravenous Condition can absolutely kill a Beast, probably within a couple of weeks, as they take one Lethal damage every day their Satiety is at zero.<br /> <br /> Satiety Conditions affect a LOT of behavior for Beasts. Most of them provide Beats for encouraging the Player to take detrimental actions for their character. But the Ravenous Condition is pretty strict in forcing the Beast to always take up opportunities to feed, even when low-Satiety meals (generally the easiest to accomplish) won't provide them any Satiety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:52:09-07:00","id":1298846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298838#post1298838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunting for werewolves is not a duty. It's a drive that they find consuming, a complete need that must be satisfied. It's not just because they can. The Wolf <i>MUST </i>Hunt.<br /> <br /> Also, Beast slowly starve if they don't feed their Satiety. Their Horror running amuck in a desperate attempt to feed itself will happen. But if the Horror isn't successful, the Beast will die. Having the Ravenous Condition can absolutely kill a Beast, probably within a couple of weeks, as they take one Lethal damage every day their Satiety is at zero.<br /> <br /> Satiety Conditions affect a LOT of behavior for Beasts. Most of them provide Beats for encouraging the Player to take detrimental actions for their character. But the Ravenous Condition is pretty strict in forcing the Beast to always take up opportunities to feed, even when low-Satiety meals (generally the easiest to accomplish) won't provide them any Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>on werewolves, yes that was my mistake. however, the wolf must hunt does not stop the fact that forsaken use it for the purpose of balancing the gauntlet and other such things.<br /> <br /> now on beasts, that was definitely my bad and I hate that I forgot that (for obvious reasons). I'm not sure how you feel about lessons in general <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, but I'd still say that lessons were made by beasts both due to the nature of their hungers and because of the relationship they have with Heroes. while I can understand &quot;well vampires dont make lessons&quot;, vampires also have a more literal hunger and dont have a metaphysical force making them a monster in need of getting killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:30:01-07:00","id":1298849,"title":"","content":"A small thing on the terminology tangent:<br /> <br /> Beast really couldn't functionally keep Soul. Souls are things in the CofD, with powers that can directly manipulate them. While the expansive nature of the CofD means some terminology overlap is inevitable, you don't want to constantly have to deal with, &quot;no, mages can't use that power on a Beast's Soul, it only works on souls.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:48:21-07:00","id":1298853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298846#post1298846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> on werewolves, yes that was my mistake. however, the wolf must hunt does not stop the fact that forsaken use it for the purpose of balancing the gauntlet and other such things.<br /> <br /> now on beasts, that was definitely my bad and I hate that I forgot that (for obvious reasons). I'm not sure how you feel about lessons in general <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, but I'd still say that lessons were made by beasts both due to the nature of their hungers and because of the relationship they have with Heroes. while I can understand &quot;well vampires dont make lessons&quot;, vampires also have a more literal hunger and dont have a metaphysical force making them a monster in need of getting killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the subject of Lessons? Personally, I feel like it was badly handled in the core book and I think this for several reasons, not just because it wasn't part of the draft manuscript presented in the Kickstarter.<br /> <br /> Lessons just don't really have any structure in the game to hook onto. There is absolutely zero interaction between the concept of Lessons and Beasts feeding their Satiety, which means there is no mechanical reasons for why Beasts would consider &quot;Lessons&quot; to be something they all consider and know of. Now, it can be pointed to the concept of Lessons being a social structure for Beasts, as in how you say &quot;To give meaning to their feeding&quot;.<br /> <br /> But what society actually exists for Beasts? The only social structure really defined for Beasts in the core book is Broods. And they are very intimate close-knit groups.<br /> <br /> Beasts have no Covenants, no Orders or Legacies, no Courts, no Tribes, no Lodges.... All of these are present in the other games in order to provide societal structure of expectations of behavior or standards of interaction or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Beasts, as presented in the Core book, don't have anything like that. So, having some kind of creed of &quot;Lessons&quot; seems very.... tacked on. Disconnected. Because they don't really have any structure in place to share such teachings or expectations of behavior.<br /> <br /> (I think the game was designed to not have any kind of &quot;Society Splat&quot;, but that creates issues that need to be addressed as what kind of society they do have, even if that society is &quot;a lack of society&quot;. Now, the Players Guide comes out with four groups, but they're each kind of their own thing and further again, they still don't have any recognized structure that fits with Beasts as presented in the Core.)<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I don't think the concept of Lessons is bad. I think it's better as something that a noted faction of Beasts believe, espouse, and support, and would be better buttressed by showing other factions that reject the concept of Lessons, or have differing ideas of how their feeding has purpose. But we don't get that, and Lessons gets shoved really hard.<br /> <br /> Basically, I'm seeing two conflicting things here, which is something the Core really should've fixed before it was finalized.<br /> <br /> And I know the Players Guide is going to be pointed to again as having &quot;fixed&quot; this, but I don't see it that way. I'll quote a couple of things from the book. Page 130 under The Culture of Lessons: &quot;Not all Beasts buy into the concept of lessons as deeply as others, but all Begotten hear about the concept of lessons shortly after their Devouring, and sometimes before.&quot;<br /> <br /> How?<br /> <br /> Page 131, under Lessons Learned: &quot;Few Beasts come through the other side of a Devouring without any other family around. From the very beginning, other Children begin speaking of the lessons they teach. They tie Hungers to lessons and teach the new Beast to explore the lessons that satisfy her Horror the best. They don't tell each other how the Horror doesn't care about the lesson, how if left unsated it will feed from the nearest and weakest prey available, no lesson learned. Sure, the Children know these things are true, but if they talk about it, they make a lie out of their own lessons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Who is this constant &quot;They&quot;? Where is this social push to share everything about &quot;lessons&quot; coming from? Where did those Beasts come across it? Why is there such pressure here for &quot;lessons&quot; when Beasts somehow know that it's all lies?<br /> <br /> Same section: &quot;Pinning a purpose on that pain, creating order within the madness of that fear, puts everything else into perspective. To prevent that kind of emotional breakdown in newly Devoured Beasts, other Children talk about lessons early and often. Even the most nihilistic of Beasts understands the concept of lessons, and understands why they are important to the Children, even if he doesn't consider them necessary for himself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where is this impending &quot;emotional breakdown&quot; from new Beasts? Why do &quot;even the most nihilistic of Beasts&quot; somehow agree with this?<br /> <br /> Where are the arguments? Where are the challenges to their lore? Where are the disagreements? Where are the other opinions?<br /> <br /> You know... I think one of the biggest problems I have with how the Player's Guide approaches Lessons, is how it strives so hard to have &quot;Lessons&quot; somehow something universal to all Beasts, and yet wants to have Beasts to have their individuality too. This circle was not squared for me. I honestly got to say... Probably the best proof that the Devouring and Teaching Lessons is something that was mishandled in the Core book, is how much word count gets used in the Player's Guide hashing over the concepts again.<br /> <br /> I do not mean to be attacking the work of the writers who wrote this stuff with this. I view this as something the Developer really needed to tie together, to expand better, and provide the writers with better direction for the various sections to support each other better. The writers can only give their best with the direction they're given. And well, Beast: The Primordial isn't really different from other Chronicles of Darkness games in this manner. Mage: The Awakening, Werewolf: The Forsaken, Changeling: The Lost, each have really shined with a Second Edition. Each had some significant problems with their First Editions. I'm really hopeful that Beast: The Primordial gets it's Second Edition when that time approaches. I think it'll be something awesome to behold. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T22:58:05-07:00","id":1298854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298849#post1298849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A small thing on the terminology tangent:<br /> <br /> Beast really couldn't functionally keep Soul. Souls are things in the CofD, with powers that can directly manipulate them. While the expansive nature of the CofD means some terminology overlap is inevitable, you don't want to constantly have to deal with, &quot;no, mages can't use that power on a Beast's Soul, it only works on souls.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Soul&quot; still actually shows up in the book, for that context. In my copy at least, which I think is a recent download, it shows up on pages 226, 267, 270, 275 and 294-295 at least in the Core. (Editedit: Holy crap, it's even in the Eshmaki's writeup...)<br /> <br /> And the book actually provides support that Mages CAN use their powers on a Beast's Soul/Horror. Page 226, &quot;Worst of all are mages who steal the souls of victims for use in experiments or fuel for strange powers; a Beast's soul is a difficult but prestigious prize for so-called &quot;Reapers.&quot; Due to Beast's connection to their Lair mages can't steal the soul of a Begotten just by casting a spell in the physical world. It requires as much ability with the Arcana as taking the soul of a mage, and can only be cast inside the Lair.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: Man, I really do love this game. But the last minute changes to the manuscript really screwed the core book up in <i>so many ways</i>....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-23-2019, 02:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:23:34-07:00","id":1298856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298522#post1298522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I realize that Beast has it's faults, some lingering even after BPG's release, but it's still frustrating to me that people continue base some of these perceived faults off of increasingly inaccurate information, on top of deliberately choosing not to look into the updated information.<br /> <br /> It breeds misunderstandings when there really shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ain\u2019t that just the story of CofD in a nutshell though?<br /> <br /> \u201cRequiem is watered-down Masquerade\u201d<br /> \u201cWerewolves are fuzzy spirit cops\u201d<br /> \u201cSomething, something, Atlantis is lame\u201d<br /> \u201cBut what about transhumanism\u201d<br /> \u201cArcadia, wut\u201d<br /> (What dumb thing do people say about Vigil?)<br /> \u201cGeists are OP\u201d<br /> \u201cI\u2019m waiting for the 2e version\u201d<br /> \u201cDemon turned CofD into The Matrix\u201d<br /> <br /> Every game line makes a few missteps early on, which are always addressed in later material that most people who didn\u2019t already love the line will never read. It sucks, but you only get one chance to make a first impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-23-2019, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:28:19-07:00","id":1298858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298856#post1298856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ain\u2019t that just the story of CofD in a nutshell though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it keeps happening doesn't mean it should be encouraged.<br /> <br /> Yes, some people's opinions won't change no matter what, but there's no excuse to allow false information to fester, act surprised when someone steps in clarify, or worse, foster toxic behaviors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:30:31-07:00","id":1298860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298856#post1298856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ain\u2019t that just the story of CofD in a nutshell though?<br /> <br /> \u201cRequiem is watered-down Masquerade\u201d<br /> \u201cWerewolves are fuzzy spirit cops\u201d<br /> \u201cSomething, something, Atlantis is lame\u201d<br /> \u201cBut what about transhumanism\u201d<br /> \u201cArcadia, wut\u201d<br /> (What dumb thing do people say about Vigil?)<br /> \u201cGeists are OP\u201d<br /> \u201cI\u2019m waiting for the 2e version\u201d<br /> \u201cDemon turned CofD into The Matrix\u201d<br /> <br /> Every game line makes a few missteps early on, which are always addressed in later material that most people who didn\u2019t already love the line will never read. It sucks, but you only get one chance to make a first impression.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually like the shortcut explanation of &quot;Werewolves are fuzzy spirit cops&quot;... &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> I mean... It's <i>not wrong. </i>But there really is a lot more nuance that is missed, as short cuts are short cuts, you know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:37:46-07:00","id":1298863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298853#post1298853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 131, under Lessons Learned: &quot;Few Beasts come through the other side of a Devouring without any other family around. From the very beginning, other Children begin speaking of the lessons they teach. They tie Hungers to lessons and teach the new Beast to explore the lessons that satisfy her Horror the best. They don't tell each other how the Horror doesn't care about the lesson, how if left unsated it will feed from the nearest and weakest prey available, no lesson learned. Sure, the Children know these things are true, but if they talk about it, they make a lie out of their own lessons.&quot;<br /> <br /> Who is this constant &quot;They&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Children. It's right there in the sentence preceding the switch to a generalized pronoun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where is this social push to share everything about &quot;lessons&quot; coming from? </div> </div> </div>Approximately the same place that Requiem's Traditions and Forsaken's Oath of the Moon come from: <i>cultural grounding with historical inertia</i>.<br /> <br /> When the monsters who tend to stick around for a long time are the ones who mediate their activities and have a digestible rationale for doing like they do, it tends to develop some institutional memory, particularly when those monsters are part meme, tend to be better equipped to change monsters' minds through conversation, and associate with other monsters who live nearby.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where did those Beasts come across it? Why is there such pressure here for &quot;lessons&quot; when Beasts somehow know that it's all lies? </div> </div> </div>They &quot;somehow&quot; know that the hungry monster that they're feeding isn't picky when it comes to what comes after the shock, which doesn't change the fact that a lot of people are still going to balk at the prospect of engaging in what is commonly understood as at least mildly cruel behavior on a regular basis right out of the gate.<br /> <br /> &quot;People are going to have a takeaway from what happens because of you, so think about the takeaway before you act on your Hunger&quot; is a not-remotely-complex selective pressure to see emerge from a population whose carelessness can lead to angry mobs and home invasions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Same section: &quot;Pinning a purpose on that pain, creating order within the madness of that fear, puts everything else into perspective. To prevent that kind of emotional breakdown in newly Devoured Beasts, other Children talk about lessons early and often. Even the most nihilistic of Beasts understands the concept of lessons, and understands why they are important to the Children, even if he doesn't consider them necessary for himself.&quot;<br /> <br /> Where is this impending &quot;emotional breakdown&quot; from new Beasts? </div> </div> </div>Empathy tends to make people a little uncomfortable engaging in behavior that harms others Just Because and leaning into that activity without a filter can go maladaptive very easily. Literally the sentence before the one you're opening this quote with points to the prospect of confronting &quot;You cause pain not just <i>by</i> fulfilling your needs but <i>to</i> fulfill your needs&quot; leading to an existential crisis \u2014 like the kind of things that directly contribute to Beasts pursuing the lesser Inheritances.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do &quot;even the most nihilistic of Beasts&quot; somehow agree with this? </div> </div> </div>The very first sample character we are shown in the book ends up a nonsapient monster attended to by the vampire he self-destructed with and her progeny. Most Beasts in a position to evince nihilism do so with the benefit of a human mind and understand well enough that the framework of lessons is a cultural method to keep the Begotten's human mind intact. They don't have to agree that a grounding framework is necessary to understand why other Beasts use it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where are the arguments? Where are the challenges to their lore? Where are the disagreements? Where are the other opinions? </div> </div> </div>There's no lore to challenge that actually exists at the heart of the concept, as is explicitly pointed out in that section: Lessons as a cultural framing are there to give their feeding a larger context with which to keep aware of the consequences of their actions.<br /> <br /> The other opinions and disagreements and arguments are matters for individual characters and frameworks for the same reason 1e Promethean didn't spend a lot of wordcount on Refusers: You don't actually need to dedicate much attention to characters using their supernatural powers in ways that are counter to the high-minded cultural touchstone the game puts forth as common enough to be in the corebook, because those rationales are generally more individually focused and the practical outcome seldom looks very different unless the character is on the fast track to a sticky end.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like, I get and agree that a Second Edition of Beast would doubtless refine the concept, but &quot;Be smart about your serial villainy because the world is watching&quot; is not nearly as out-there as some of its detractors have made it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T23:47:41-07:00","id":1298866,"title":"","content":"I'm really not wanting to have an argument about it. Especially not with you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. I was responding to Primordial Newcomer's statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T00:12:22-07:00","id":1298870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298858#post1298858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because it keeps happening doesn't mean it should be encouraged.<br /> <br /> Yes, some people's opinions won't change no matter what, but there's no excuse to allow false information to fester, act surprised when someone steps in clarify, or worse, foster toxic behaviors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely don\u2019t think it should be encouraged. It\u2019s just a thing that happens, and it\u2019s obnoxious but what can you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T07:03:36-07:00","id":1298941,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say I can't help to appreciate how this thread evolved in a passionate discussion of all things Beast between sharp and well-informed people. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-23-2019, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:31:13-07:00","id":1298960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298866#post1298866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really not wanting to have an argument about it. Especially not with you, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a>. I was responding to Primordial Newcomer's statement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be honest, Satchel covered a lot of it. other more mature beast teach nascent ones the concept of lessons. nihilist beast only use the framework because it provides control of your hunger.<br /> <br /> on that last part, you also said lessons dont give you more satiety. you are correct in that lessons themselves do not do that. however, a beast can gain more satiety through acts that can be considered that of a lesson.<br /> <br /> a beast with the hunger of transgressions can get low satiety from, say, making a guy cheat on his girlfriend. that same beast can gain a LOT more satiety from a husband cheating on his wife. <br /> <br /> from the above, lessons give beasts ideas for framework such as this, and for ambitious beast carve a path for incarnation.<br /> <br /> as for beast society, I do see your point in that. personally I would not be surprised if a second edition of beast expanded on them. as for their relationship with lessons, I will admit the players guide does not touch upon that. its ultimately up to the storyteller on how they see it. Who knows, you could say the Athenaeum could discover that back when beast did not have to feed so often (a VERY long time ago), the Heroes did the work of revealing what lesson that monster was showing (likely unintentionally). nowadays due to the change of the primordial dream, beast now have to refine what they do for more satiety and in the process made lessons (along with separating themselves from a story where they HAVE to die)<br /> <br /> let me note that last paragraph is purely hypothetical<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>, if you want us to stop these off topic discussions, just say so. until then I'll be discussing the concept of lessons with paradim (and if it's fine with paradim anyone else who wants to join)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-23-2019, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:46:59-07:00","id":1298969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298960#post1298960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be honest, Satchel covered a lot of it. other more mature beast teach nascent ones the concept of lessons. nihilist beast only use the framework because it provides control of your hunger.<br /> <br /> on that last part, you also said lessons dont give you more satiety. you are correct in that lessons themselves do not do that. however, a beast can gain more satiety through acts that can be considered that of a lesson.<br /> <br /> a beast with the hunger of transgressions can get low satiety from, say, making a guy cheat on his girlfriend. that same beast can gain a LOT more satiety from a husband cheating on his wife.<br /> <br /> from the above, lessons give beasts ideas for framework such as this, and for ambitious beast carve a path for incarnation.<br /> <br /> as for beast society, I do see your point in that. personally I would not be surprised if a second edition of beast expanded on them. as for their relationship with lessons, I will admit the players guide does not touch upon that. its ultimately up to the storyteller on how they see it. Who knows, you could say the Athenaeum could discover that back when beast did not have to feed so often (a VERY long time ago), the Heroes did the work of revealing what lesson that monster was showing (likely unintentionally). nowadays due to the change of the primordial dream, beast now have to refine what they do for more satiety and in the process made lessons (along with separating themselves from a story where they HAVE to die)<br /> <br /> let me note that last paragraph is purely hypothetical<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>, if you want us to stop these off topic discussions, just say so. until then I'll be discussing the concept of lessons with paradim (and if it's fine with paradim anyone else who wants to join)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, keep discussing this stuff. It's actually interesting reading it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T08:56:27-07:00","id":1298970,"title":"","content":"The BPG did offer a really great vehicle for Beast society that will probably get more stress in a 2e: Primordial cults. Cults let a Beast formalize their concept of lessons into the cult's practices, and any new Beast fostered within the cult, or that simply comes in and takes over a cult that lost its Beast, would learn about that particular view of lessons simply by engaging with those humans. There's also some fun narratives to explore around accepting the role of another Beast and if you can find a path towards Inheritance on someone else's coattails, or struggling to rework a cult in your image, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T09:20:30-07:00","id":1298974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298970#post1298970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BPG did offer a really great vehicle for Beast society that will probably get more stress in a 2e: Primordial cults. Cults let a Beast formalize their concept of lessons into the cult's practices, and any new Beast fostered within the cult, or that simply comes in and takes over a cult that lost its Beast, would learn about that particular view of lessons simply by engaging with those humans. There's also some fun narratives to explore around accepting the role of another Beast and if you can find a path towards Inheritance on someone else's coattails, or struggling to rework a cult in your image, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>cant believe I forgot to mention cults. as you said heavy arms, cults allow a beast to have the way people perceive them change and be able to rule through some loyalty besides fear (and we all know fear alone only works for so long). a supplement for beast society and cults would definitely be appreciated as they would help flesh out the cultures of beast and practicality of lessons (which you are correct <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, lessons do need more fleshing out compared to the social constructs made by other supernaturals)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:53:04-07:00","id":1299005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298960#post1298960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be honest, Satchel covered a lot of it. other more mature beast teach nascent ones the concept of lessons. nihilist beast only use the framework because it provides control of your hunger.<br /> <br /> on that last part, you also said lessons dont give you more satiety. you are correct in that lessons themselves do not do that. however, a beast can gain more satiety through acts that can be considered that of a lesson.<br /> <br /> a beast with the hunger of transgressions can get low satiety from, say, making a guy cheat on his girlfriend. that same beast can gain a LOT more satiety from a husband cheating on his wife.<br /> <br /> from the above, lessons give beasts ideas for framework such as this, and for ambitious beast carve a path for incarnation.<br /> <br /> as for beast society, I do see your point in that. personally I would not be surprised if a second edition of beast expanded on them. as for their relationship with lessons, I will admit the players guide does not touch upon that. its ultimately up to the storyteller on how they see it. Who knows, you could say the Athenaeum could discover that back when beast did not have to feed so often (a VERY long time ago), the Heroes did the work of revealing what lesson that monster was showing (likely unintentionally). nowadays due to the change of the primordial dream, beast now have to refine what they do for more satiety and in the process made lessons (along with separating themselves from a story where they HAVE to die)<br /> <br /> let me note that last paragraph is purely hypothetical<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1579_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1579\" data-vbnamecard=\"1579\">Camilla</a>, if you want us to stop these off topic discussions, just say so. until then I'll be discussing the concept of lessons with paradim (and if it's fine with paradim anyone else who wants to join)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Satchel actually ignored a lot of my post and just focused on the examples, nitpicking them, while not addressing anything else I said. It's why I don't want to argue with them. It doesn't help. Like saying &quot;They&quot; is in reference to other Beasts? Well, no shit. So WHO are these other Beasts? Is it in reference to ALL Beasts? ALL Beasts do this? ALL Beasts talk about Lessons? It's this completely universal thing for an entire supernatural species? What social teaching do ALL Werewolves have on how to behave? What about ALL Mages? Or ALL Vampires?<br /> <br /> It doesn't fit. Anyways...<br /> <br /> On Beasts getting more Satiety through acts that can be considered a lesson... Where is that from? I'm looking at the Feeding modifiers on page 108 and I'm not seeing any modifiers based on &quot;teaching a lesson&quot; or something like that... I'm open to missing something there and thought I initially did, but... still missing it. ^^;<br /> <br /> And thank you for admitting to seeing the point, regarding Beast society. I'm not trying to argue for one way or another on this. Beasts don't NEED to have a strict society, and I can see how a lack of society for them can help push them to interact with the societies of other supernatural groups. but when you add a societal push for &quot;Lessons&quot;... It falls apart for me, because there is no noted structure for that to be pushed through, and even worse, it completely misses opportunities for differences of opinion amongst Beasts in order to push a single agenda. And that is tragic, because we don't need a single agenda pushed, we need multiple agendas pushed.<br /> <br /> That's conflict.<br /> <br /> The topic of Lessons for Beasts? Is an amazing area where Beasts can come into conflict with each other through opposing viewpoints. But we have <i>none </i>of that, because the concept of Lessons was shoehorned into a universal &quot;understanding&quot; that we're just <i>told </i>all Beasts somehow understand, and somehow all Beasts <i>tell </i>each other &quot;Lessons are important yo&quot;, when the books flat out <i>tell </i>us that the Horror/Soul just doesn't give a crap about Lessons repeatedly.<br /> <br /> And... I'm just disappointed. Because conflict for Beasts is something the game really struggles with. I really would have loved to see the philosophical differences between Beasts, in what it means for them to feed, in ways that drive them into conflict with one another, and maybe even see how these philosophical differences inform Beasts on why Heroes go after them. Like, consider this idea...<br /> <br /> What if Beasts can't agree on WHY Heroes go after them? What if some Beasts think that the reason Heroes target Beasts is because they're feeding in the <i>wrong </i>way or for the <i>wrong </i>reasons?<br /> <br /> Ultimately, Heroes don't, because there's something off with Heroes themselves. But Beasts don't <i>know </i>this. So what if they're trying to come up with new philosophies of what they're <i>meant </i>to do with their feeding, because they wonder if they've veered off the &quot;proper path&quot;? How do Beasts react to each other when they come to different conclusions as to what the &quot;proper path&quot; is?<br /> <br /> That's conflict! And conflict is necessary for stories. Now, this is just off the top of my head speculation and is greatly unrefined, so take this all with a big grain of salt. Think of how you could use this for your own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T12:07:22-07:00","id":1299011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298974#post1298974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> cant believe I forgot to mention cults. as you said heavy arms, cults allow a beast to have the way people perceive them change and be able to rule through some loyalty besides fear (and we all know fear alone only works for so long). a supplement for beast society and cults would definitely be appreciated as they would help flesh out the cultures of beast and practicality of lessons (which you are correct <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, lessons do need more fleshing out compared to the social constructs made by other supernaturals)</div> </div> </div> </div>Cults definitely are interesting, though that is more of an interaction between Beasts and Mortals, I think? But not all Beasts do Cults.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you're seeing my viewpoint on this. I don't think that Lessons are &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;shouldn't be in the game&quot;. I can absolutely see a place for it in the game, just... not how it was implemented.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, it's just my opinion, and we've got the books that we've got. I'm making do for my own game (and my Beast player doesn't like Lessons either, I quote &quot;They take away my character's agency for no reason and I hate that&quot;, so I just don't have Lessons be something that gets hammered at the player/character like the books present and just let the character work out their own meaning for feeding).<br /> <br /> Hrm... Thinking of it... It could be kind of interesting if the concept of &quot;Lessons&quot; was more based upon what Mortals reason out as to why a Beast is feeding. Like, Mortals work out their own &quot;Lessons&quot;, and maybe Beasts could gain more Satiety through conforming to those expectations... I need to mull that over more...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T12:20:44-07:00","id":1299013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1298970#post1298970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BPG did offer a really great vehicle for Beast society that will probably get more stress in a 2e: Primordial cults. Cults let a Beast formalize their concept of lessons into the cult's practices, and any new Beast fostered within the cult, or that simply comes in and takes over a cult that lost its Beast, would learn about that particular view of lessons simply by engaging with those humans. There's also some fun narratives to explore around accepting the role of another Beast and if you can find a path towards Inheritance on someone else's coattails, or struggling to rework a cult in your image, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A plot I'm working out for my own game will actually use a Cult. My player doesn't want their Beast to go actively making a Cult (just doesn't fit the character's mentality or attitude). So something I'm going to be doing to show how the Beast's actions are impacting the setting, I'm going to have mortals pull together as a Cult of the Beast themselves, and then see how the Beast handles learning of that. I might do something regarding the concept of &quot;Lessons&quot; in it, as that seems like a good place to fit how the Beast's actions are fitting into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T13:09:09-07:00","id":1299020,"title":"","content":"on your first post response, when it says they, I honestly thought it simply meant many beast did with the idea being that, due to the deep kinship beast feel for each other, they teach the concept of lessons less to tell a new beast &quot;this is our job&quot; and more easing them into what they are (that, and the nightmares nascent beast experience can easily be misconceived as a lesson). I will say though it is very vague on that aspect. I also find the idea you have about exploring lessons through exploring the primordial dream and relationship with heroes. but I will say, philosophically speaking, beasts with different lessons can have conflict with each other too (the hunger for punishment and hunger for transgressions being prime examples). as for heroes, I remember that the corebook mentions that heroes used to delve into the dream to find a lesson and give wisdom to society. I think it would be great if high integrity heroes could be introduced this way (as that would make a great conflict with beast who believe heroes ALWAYS have no idea what they are talking about).<br /> <br /> for the second post, I've always found cults to be an interesting concept for beasts and agree the idea of mortals seeing lessons is an interesting one. but I also see it gives another reason for lessons to be used for purely practical, exploitive uses. <br /> <br /> on your last post <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, that sounds like a very good idea! it should definitely make for a fun and interesting Chronicle. and its proof you are not averse to the idea of lessons, but the implementation like you said.<br /> <br /> finally, sorry for lack of clarity regarding lessons giving more satiety. what I meant was acts that could be mistaken as a lesson tend to get more satiety, like a priest committing adultery (hunger for transgression) or a famed hunter being the hunted (hunger for prey). this could actually go into your idea that mortals see lessons in things that aren't there. if you would reconcile that with beasts ideas on lessons, you could say beasts simply took advantage of a big misunderstanding (and as the generations passed started to believe they made the concept all themselves)<br /> <br /> oh and this. you mentioned your player felt like lessons forced his character into something he didnt want. I will admit I've never felt lessons forced your character into a direction you didnt want. to me lessons aren't like the 3 laws vampires have that even the Circle follows, even if loosely. lessons to me are simply a social construct beasts made to control their feedings habits from overindulgence (and as I've stressed, build a Myth). not only that, but once again it reinforces in beast the idea they are creatures that dont HAVE to die. that, and lessons provide a sort of masquerade in beasts not feeding all over the place","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T14:31:14-07:00","id":1299032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299020#post1299020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">finally, sorry for lack of clarity regarding lessons giving more satiety. what I meant was acts that could be mistaken as a lesson tend to get more satiety, like a priest committing adultery (hunger for transgression) or a famed hunter being the hunted (hunger for prey). this could actually go into your idea that mortals see lessons in things that aren't there. if you would reconcile that with beasts ideas on lessons, you could say beasts simply took advantage of a big misunderstanding (and as the generations passed started to believe they made the concept all themselves)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still not following you on this. What do you mean by &quot;acts that could be mistaken as a lesson tend to get more satiety&quot;?<br /> <br /> The best I've got for what you mean there is the +1 modifier for &quot;Fitting with your Beast's specific preferences&quot;? But &quot;specific preferences&quot; has no grounding in &quot;lessons&quot;...<br /> <br /> When you're talking about the hunger for prey and hunger for transgression, I'm not sure what you mean by that, either. Would you mind expanding on what you mean some more, so I can better understand?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T14:55:14-07:00","id":1299038,"title":"","content":"consider this. the hunger for prey gives you satiety for hunting down creatures and giving them fear. doing stuff like running over a guy would give you satiety, not much but still. now consider this: a mob boss feared by everyone and always kept safe in an anonymous location and with guards armed to the teeth. if a beast were to strike fear into HIM, he would gain a lot more satiety. this can be seen as a lesson. no matter much power you have, no matter how far your reach, there is always a bigger fish ready to eat you up. this is where lessons come from. that same beast could indiscriminately feed, not gaining as much satiety but pissing off a LOT of people. Lessons in this way can less be about teaching people, but be a catch all term for how a beast focuses his hunger to get better feedings.<br /> <br /> lessons don't get you more satiety. more satiety for focused feedings gave birth to the idea of lessons","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:01:26-07:00","id":1299041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299038#post1299038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">consider this. the hunger for prey gives you satiety for hunting down creatures and giving them fear. doing stuff like running over a guy would give you satiety, not much but still. now consider this: a mob boss feared by everyone and always kept safe in an anonymous location and with guards armed to the teeth. if a beast were to strike fear into HIM, he would gain a lot more satiety. this can be seen as a lesson. no matter much power you have, no matter how far your reach, there is always a bigger fish ready to eat you up. this is where lessons come from. that same beast could indiscriminately feed, not gaining as much satiety but pissing off a LOT of people. Lessons in this way can less be about teaching people, but be a catch all term for how a beast focuses his hunger to get better feedings.<br /> <br /> lessons don't get you more satiety. more satiety for focused feedings gave birth to the idea of lessons</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ooohkay, so what you're saying is that lessons could be used to develop the framework for what counts as a greater satiety feeding.<br /> <br /> I get that. I could see Lessons as being useful for doing that.<br /> <br /> It would be nice if the books actually developed that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:20:05-07:00","id":1299046,"title":"","content":"I think BPG actually did that well enough<br /> <br /> (pg 131) In another way, following the narrative of lessons makes a <br /> Beast more careful, less likely to let her Horror roam unchecked, <br /> and less likely to leave a string of bodies in the wake of her feed-<br /> ing \u2014 all things that would attract a Hero. Certainly, the lesson <br /> doesn\u2019t stop Heroes from showing up on the door of a Beast\u2019s <br /> Lair. No amount of careful feeding and measured action could <br /> prevent that. Instead, it allows a Beast to prepare herself for her <br /> eventual encounter with a Hero. Her narrative now becomes a <br /> primal struggle for ideological dominance. This dominance is <br /> essential to the power of the Beast \u2014 her tale must be ascendant. <br /> The Hero now poses the challenges to the Beast\u2019s personal <br /> narrative. In a way, he becomes the Beast\u2019s method of testing <br /> herself, proving her dominance, and again taking control over <br /> her own Legend. It changes her struggle from one of survival <br /> to one of Legend.<br /> <br /> I'm going to note that the sections &quot;Family Values&quot;, is just below this paragraph . it discusses how the beast who tends to eschew lessons tend to fall into the narrative heroes want to tell, and how lessons is sorta like the 3 traditions in that it keeps beast from being too obvious.<br /> <br /> I do agree, however, that it would've been nice if there was a beast example where the beast, after realizing his hunger was sated more easily from tougher targets, made lessons out of it (not to actually teach, but to find targets that could get him fed more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:39:00-07:00","id":1299054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299046#post1299046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree, however, that it would've been nice if there was a beast example where the beast, after realizing his hunger was sated more easily from tougher targets, made lessons out of it (not to actually teach, but to find targets that could get him fed more)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is more what I mean by being more developed. How Lessons fits into gaining Satiety, for identifying targets, for determining greater Satiety values for feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:51:29-07:00","id":1299059,"title":"","content":"I can understand that. well I think this is a good ending point and I think this was a very beneficial discussion for the both of us <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>. thank you for your time (if you want to continue that's fine. but I must go for now)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T06:04:00-07:00","id":1299188,"title":"","content":"I hate the \u2018lessons\u2019 Bullshit it gives the book a Werid Victim-blaming Layer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:16:50-07:00","id":1299236,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a>, have you not read any of the discussion? you cant just lash out on an emotional level. to see it as &quot;victim-blaming&quot; is a BIG misinterpretation of what lessons are for. hell the books even show it's more than just an excuse to terrify AND the ChoD admit it has it's bad side in the form of the hunter compact Yuri's group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:39:06-07:00","id":1299247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299236#post1299236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a>, have you not read any of the discussion? you cant just lash out on an emotional level. to see it as &quot;victim-blaming&quot; is a BIG misinterpretation of what lessons are for. hell the books even show it's more than just an excuse to terrify AND the ChoD admit it has it's bad side in the form of the hunter compact Yuri's group</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a valid interpretation, actually.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the concept of Lessons is the Beast trying to justify their feeding. It's the stance that these people deserve to have the Beast happen to them (I really struggled for a neutral word there, but... There isn't really, so victimized, abused, harassed, threatened, hurt, etc etc, pick a word for you). But the object of the &quot;Lesson&quot; doesn't even need to be legitimate. It could be the Beast deciding to punish someone because they didn't wear green on St. Paddy's day or that they walked and chewed bubblegum at the same time.<br /> <br /> I think that aspect of Lessons needs to be examined by the books. It highlights that, no Beasts really are awful and monsters. I think it's important, because even vampires at their best are predatory, even werewolves at their best are savage, even mages at their best are obsessive.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say Beasts can't have redeeming qualities, but that even at their best, Beasts are still monsters.<br /> <br /> It is vital that when holding up Lessons as justification, the books need to examine how that justification is also bullshit.<br /> <br /> So Lessons is victim-blaming has to be valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:45:07-07:00","id":1299249,"title":"","content":"I suppose. but it just angers me beast get this crap while werewolves and vampires seem to get a pass. such as werewolves killing whole towns if &quot;the herd finds out&quot; and no one bats an eye because they &quot;have to do that&quot;. Vampires are known to feed and keep ghouls and many other addicts chained to them in an incredibly perverted relationship, and yet Beasts are the still the undisputed worst monsters out there<br /> <br /> and the books HAVE admitted what they do is truly monstrous like the other gamelines<br /> <br /> EDIT: Finally, before anyone starts thinking I think beast shouldn't be seen as monsters, they absolutely should. but when people see what they do and their reasons for doing it as suddenly worse than any other gamelines reasons, I see a problem in bias","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-24-2019, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:00:50-07:00","id":1299255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299249#post1299249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose. but it just angers me beast get this crap while werewolves and vampires seem to get a pass. such as werewolves killing whole towns if &quot;the herd finds out&quot; and no one bats an eye because they &quot;have to do that&quot;. Vampires are known to feed and keep ghouls and many other addicts chained to them in an incredibly perverted relationship, and yet Beasts are the still the undisputed worst monsters out there<br /> <br /> and the books HAVE admitted what they do is truly monstrous like the other gamelines<br /> <br /> EDIT: Finally, before anyone starts thinking I think beast shouldn't be seen as monsters, they absolutely should. but when people see what they do and their reasons for doing it as suddenly worse than any other gamelines reasons, I see a problem in bias</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts absolutely aren't the worst monsters. The &quot;worst&quot; is a meaningless adjective. Werewolves absolutely do terrible things. So do Vampires and Mages. None of their behaviors should get a pass. None of it should be minimized. They all victimize people.<br /> <br /> This is honestly what I've always liked about White Wolf and Onyx Path games. You are the monster. Now deal with it (probably badly, it's meant to be a horror game afterall).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:05:23-07:00","id":1299258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299249#post1299249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose. but it just angers me beast get this crap while werewolves and vampires seem to get a pass. such as werewolves killing whole towns if &amp;quot;the herd finds out&amp;quot; and no one bats an eye because they &amp;quot;have to do that&amp;quot;. Vampires are known to feed and keep ghouls and many other addicts chained to them in an incredibly perverted relationship, and yet Beasts are the still the undisputed worst monsters out there<br /> <br /> and the books HAVE admitted what they do is truly monstrous like the other gamelines</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly what I dont understand about the lessons. Like said Vampires are horrid monsters that feed upon humanity and hold no excuses for their behaviour, they feed because they must. Werewolves are Savage monsters that maim and kill as a matter of fact and hold no excuses for their behaviour they hunt because the wolf must hunt. Why then do Beasts need these lessons and excuses for their feeding? All the lessons do is highlight the Beasts monstrous nature and make it seem like they see even themselves as so monstrous as to need excuses for their hungers, like their somehow worse than Vampires or werewolves. They are not any worse than anyother monster outthere and thus should need no more excuses than the rest.<br /> <br /> Beast should feed because it is their nature, and forget this crap about lessons and justifications, just like Vampires feed because that is what Vampires do and werewolves because they must. The lessons do not make Beasts any more approachable or less monstrous they just make them hippocrites unlike the the rest of the monsters whom are what they are honestly.<br /> <br /> That is my main problem with the whole concept of lessons. Not only are they obviously tacked on after the fact they make Beasts seem like they are unable to honestly be themselves.<br /> <br /> Hence my question is why in your opinion, you being anyone who likes lessons, Beast are so different from all other supernaturals as to need excuses for their own nature? What makes them so different from Vampires and werewolves to need to explain their own hunger away as something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:52:59-07:00","id":1299271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299258#post1299258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is exactly what I dont understand about the lessons. Like said Vampires are horrid monsters that feed upon humanity and hold no excuses for their behaviour, they feed because they must. Werewolves are Savage monsters that maim and kill as a matter of fact and hold no excuses for their behaviour they hunt because the wolf must hunt. Why then do Beasts need these lessons and excuses for their feeding? All the lessons do is highlight the Beasts monstrous nature and make it seem like they see even themselves as so monstrous as to need excuses for their hungers, like their somehow worse than Vampires or werewolves. They are not any worse than anyother monster outthere and thus should need no more excuses than the rest.<br /> <br /> Beast should feed because it is their nature, and forget this crap about lessons and justifications, just like Vampires feed because that is what Vampires do and werewolves because they must. The lessons do not make Beasts any more approachable or less monstrous they just make them hippocrites unlike the the rest of the monsters whom are what they are honestly.<br /> <br /> That is my main problem with the whole concept of lessons. Not only are they obviously tacked on after the fact they make Beasts seem like they are unable to honestly be themselves.<br /> <br /> Hence my question is why in your opinion, you being anyone who likes lessons, Beast are so different from all other supernaturals as to need excuses for their own nature? What makes them so different from Vampires and werewolves to need to explain their own hunger away as something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>it's to cope. same reasons covenants are too cope. same reason the main idea the Lancea sanctum has is that they &quot;teach fear&quot;, to the unworthy Christians (which NEVER started an uproar).<br /> <br /> werewolves do have excuses in the oath of the moon. you can say, &quot;but they cant eat people or kill the people&quot;. they CAN kill the herd just for knowing (even if it's their fault for them knowing in the first place<br /> <br /> lessons aren't an excuse for the horrible things beasts do. they are a coping mechanism to keep their feeding habits under control just like how vampires have territories and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:34:52-07:00","id":1299290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299247#post1299247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a valid interpretation, actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't and your one-sided calls for civility are grating on me and making participation in this threat exceedingly tedious.<br /> <br /> If you care about good discussions of the game, don't enable posting that toes the line of trolling.<br /> <br /> [quoite]Ultimately, the concept of Lessons is the Beast trying to justify their feeding.[/quote]<br /> <br /> No, it isn't. It's the Beast's trying to justify that their feeding doesn't make them inherently evil and that the Heroes are right about them. It's about giving their feeding purpose, to justifying it outright.<br /> <br /> Also, you know what the book should do? What it did:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BtP, p. 64</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teaching a lesson through terror is morally reprehensible to most people\u2026but Beasts are not people.<br /> They use lessons to give context and purpose to their<br /> feeding practices. If Beasts are honest, they admit<br /> they use the concept of \u201clessons\u201d to make what they<br /> do more palatable. Some Beasts rail at that notion,<br /> claiming divine purpose. Others try to make the<br /> lessons matter and improve humanity \u2014 whether the<br /> Dark Mother charges them with it or not, it\u2019s a noble<br /> pursuit. Still others shrug, cast off even the idea of a<br /> higher calling, and just feast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Victim blaming is putting the responsibility for a crime or negative action on the victim of it. The game doesn't do that. Lessons are an in-game social construct to try to encourage Beasts to pick victims that deserve it, rather than blaming all humanity and feeding on whoever they want. It can be a spiritual belief (as noted the game implies the Dark Mother seems to promote this in an unverifiable faith-ish sort of way), an earnest philosophic belief, a personal line just because (Batman doesn't kill not because he actually has a problem with killing criminals, but because he knows that if he started killing them he'd go overboard), a purely practical positions (feeding off of 'bad' people is less likely to draw ire from humanity and Heroes), or just a thin veneer the Beast pays lip service to. All of that puts the blame on the Beast, not the victim.<br /> <br /> This is already addressed by the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Lessons is victim-blaming has to be valid. </div> </div> </div><br /> Only to the extend that some Beasts do this as a personal interpretation of what teaching lessons means, not something inherent to the concept; which again, addressed in the books already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299258#post1299258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast should feed because it is their nature, and forget this crap about lessons and justifications, just like Vampires feed because that is what Vampires do and werewolves because they must. The lessons do not make Beasts any more approachable or less monstrous they just make them hippocrites unlike the the rest of the monsters whom are what they are honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts feed because it's their nature. Lessons are a framework to keep themselves in check. Just like Humanity or the Oath of the Moon. A vampire that forgets their Humanity and just gives into their urge to feed falls to their beast and becomes an unplayable mindless killing machine. A werewolf that forgets the balance and duty of their Oath to Luna struggle to keep their Harmony and end up casing damage to their hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> A vampire that doesn't 'give a crap' about how they feed is doomed to lose their Humanity and their existence.<br /> <br /> A werewolf that doesn't 'give a crap' about how they hunt is going to fall out of Harmony, damage their territory, and risk themselves to any number of threats (including their own packmates).<br /> <br /> So, no, the other critters of the CofD are not 'more honest' about what they are, nor do they engage with their equivalents to feeding without context and purpose providing social structures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hence my question is why in your opinion, you being anyone who likes lessons, Beast are so different from all other supernaturals as to need excuses for their own nature? What makes them so different from Vampires and werewolves to need to explain their own hunger away as something else? </div> </div> </div>This is a complete strawman that's unanswerable because it's not about Lessons in BtP, it's about the bad-faith &quot;Lessons&quot; that exist in the heads of people that don't actually know that the book says. I have no interest in defending your misconceptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:53:50-07:00","id":1299301,"title":"","content":"And what many people seem to ignore that I've BEEN saying over and over is that lessons give them a purpose in defense of heroes who think they should die, no matter how horrible or not the beast is. seriously it's just conveniently ignored","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:13:53-07:00","id":1299306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299290#post1299290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't and your one-sided calls for civility are grating on me and making participation in this threat exceedingly tedious.<br /> <br /> If you care about good discussions of the game, don't enable posting that toes the line of trolling.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think a post is trolling, then report it and let the mods deal with it.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that post was trolling. This is about encouraging positive discussion of difficult subject matters. To say that someone has a &quot;valid interpretation&quot; doesn't mean that it is the <i>only </i>interpretation. It is to say that, &quot;Yes, what you are seeing can be problematic and in order to be respectful to the subject matter, it should be examined and addressed for the circumstances it applies in.&quot;<br /> <br /> It is not a &quot;one-sided call for civility&quot; to say &quot;I hear what you're saying&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299290#post1299290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't. It's the Beast's trying to justify that their feeding doesn't make them inherently evil and that the Heroes are right about them. It's about giving their feeding purpose, to justifying it outright.<br /> <br /> Also, you know what the book should do? What it did:<br /> <br /> Victim blaming is putting the responsibility for a crime or negative action on the victim of it. The game doesn't do that. Lessons are an in-game social construct to try to encourage Beasts to pick victims that deserve it, rather than blaming all humanity and feeding on whoever they want. It can be a spiritual belief (as noted the game implies the Dark Mother seems to promote this in an unverifiable faith-ish sort of way), an earnest philosophic belief, a personal line just because (Batman doesn't kill not because he actually has a problem with killing criminals, but because he knows that if he started killing them he'd go overboard), a purely practical positions (feeding off of 'bad' people is less likely to draw ire from humanity and Heroes), or just a thin veneer the Beast pays lip service to. All of that puts the blame on the Beast, not the victim.<br /> <br /> This is already addressed by the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>As what you quote, &quot;If Beasts are honest, they admit they use the concept of &quot;lessons&quot; to make what they do palatable.&quot; This is pretty explicit of victim-blaming, with a Beast saying, &quot;Because I say you did this, you deserve for me to feed upon you.&quot;<br /> <br /> How does what you say here not validate an interpretation of Lessons as being victim-blaming?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299290#post1299290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only to the extend that some Beasts do this as a personal interpretation of what teaching lessons means, not something inherent to the concept; which again, addressed in the books already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, but what you're quoting and what you're saying only supports an interpretation of Lessons as victim-blaming. And that's fine. There should be room in the game for Beast's to question this. When part of the game is about exploring the question of &quot;Is it <i>wrong </i>for us to feed when we hunger?&quot; , then examining different answers is important and just as the possible answer of &quot;It's not wrong to be what I am&quot;, so too is a possible answer of &quot;Suffering is still wrong, even if I'm the one causing it&quot;, as well as untold many other possible answers. And none of them are wrong answers or right answers, strictly.<br /> <br /> And this is a good thing for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:16:00-07:00","id":1299308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299301#post1299301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what many people seem to ignore that I've BEEN saying over and over is that lessons give them a purpose in defense of heroes who think they should die, no matter how horrible or not the beast is. seriously it's just conveniently ignored</div> </div> </div> </div>Does a Beast practicing teaching lessons actually stop a Hero from coming after that Beast to kill them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:35:13-07:00","id":1299319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299308#post1299308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does a Beast practicing teaching lessons actually stop a Hero from coming after that Beast to kill them?</div> </div> </div> </div>it actually does help. lessons allow them to focus and have a defense against a hero. and heroes HATE this due to it making a beast more than a monster in need of being killed. lessons are also used for cults as previously discussed, and heroes hate that these cultists will defend Beasts. and once again, controlling your hunger means less frequent feeding, meaning less likely the hero will come as quickly<br /> <br /> lessons ARENT victim blaming. is a changeling victim blaming an oathbreaker (who likely didmt even know the oath was in effect)? no, they're not at all. not all beast go in thinking &quot;oh he deserves this this is all his fault&quot; many also think &quot;ok this is a good target, this will build my legend&quot; (and by the way, on the idea of legend, I think that, though not for sure, that many also think Legend and life should be explored more, to which I agree)<br /> <br /> and I do think konrads post was unnecessary on the point of trolling. he ignored everything and just said &quot;lessons are dumb I hate them&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 09-23-2019, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:43:58-07:00","id":1299327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299319#post1299319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it actually does help. lessons allow them to focus and have a defense against a hero. and heroes HATE this due to it making a beast more than a monster in need of being killed. lessons are also used for cults as previously discussed, and heroes hate that these cultists will defend heroes. and once again, controlling your hunger means less frequent feeding, meaning less likely the hero will come as quickly</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this defense against a hero?<br /> <br /> Controlling your hunger is just practicing moderation, and lessons aren't inherent to the idea of moderating yourself. Lessons is just a single philosophy on <i>how </i>you can moderate yourself. I really wish there were others presented.<br /> <br /> (And yeah, Legend and Life could do with some more exploring.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:48:51-07:00","id":1299338,"title":"","content":"lessons help because it gives a beast context. a beast isn't just a creature causing fear to the population, the beast is showing the population that nobody is all powerful. this can show the population that leaders are not invincible and can even have a positive impact against cult leaders. a hero hearing of this can easily get rattled that a beast could do this. lessons may be a single philosophy, but it is a flexible philosophy that can suit any beast","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:57:39-07:00","id":1299342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299338#post1299338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">lessons help because it gives a beast context. a beast isn't just a creature causing fear to the population, the beast is showing the population that nobody is all powerful. this can show the population that leaders are not invincible and can even have a positive impact against cult leaders. a hero hearing of this can easily get rattled that a beast could do this. lessons may be a single philosophy, but it is a flexible philosophy that can suit any beast</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, I'm not seeing as how teaching lessons provides a defense against Heroes. I can definitely see how such a philosophy and practice would help a Beast feel better about themselves, if they need that, but I can't really see a low Integrity Hero (the kind usually targeting Beasts to kill them) would really be turned away. And there certainly isn't any mechanical benefits to it that I can see.<br /> <br /> I could potentially see a high Integrity Hero thinking &quot;Well, I guess those people really did deserve it&quot;, but then again if a high Integrity Hero gets put on the trail of a Beast, maybe they would decide differently? I don't know, we don't really have a lot of information about those kinds of Heroes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:12:04-07:00","id":1299354,"title":"","content":"I'm not trying to be blunt here, but what's not to see? it's not that the low integrity hero will give up, it's that it will enrage him and make him erratic. in the process it makes it much more difficult to convince the population that the beast needs to die","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:22:04-07:00","id":1299362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299354#post1299354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to be blunt here, but what's not to see? it's not that the low integrity hero will give up, it's that it will enrage him and make him erratic. in the process it makes it much more difficult to convince the population that the beast needs to die</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not seeing that as doing much? I mean, the Beast still has someone trying to kill them. Heroes even have Anathema they can pin on a Beast in order to make them more monstrous in order to garner more Followers. But then, whether a Hero has any Followers is entirely up to the Storyteller to decide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:26:13-07:00","id":1299364,"title":"","content":"it's a pretty big help to have a defense in a narrative made against you. Anathema does not make you more monstrous as much just give you a weakness that you never had before (yes there are ones like rage, but anathema does not suddenly make people think &quot;oh well he's a monster&quot;). it's also up to a storyteller to make sure your actions as a beast effect the narrative the hero has against you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:28:58-07:00","id":1299365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299342#post1299342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I'm not seeing as how teaching lessons provides a defense against Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does, but not directly. The best it can do, which is still valuable, is to provide Beasts a better framework to feed as they need in a less distruptive way. Which in turn lowers the chances of the Horror running amok and the overall strain a Begotten inflicts on the astral tapestry, with consequent diminished chances of them showing up on the Heroes' radar. Eventually, it will fail, for reasons that range from bad luck to one's Legend growing.<br /> <br /> Primordial Newcomer is right about that one. Not a perfect solution, but it makes things better. That's the sort of &quot;imperfect but still valuable and worth teaching others regardless of their opinion about Lessons&quot; trick that will survive over time and space.<br /> <br /> Now, will it stop Heroes from attacking? Well, even low-Integrity ones are not slashers (though they can come close), so it might give them pause, but the truth is that Lessons are not guaranteed to save Beast from Heroes. You can behave as best as you can, but one day an Hero will come to hunt you down. Which is both scary, frustrating and ultimately appropriate for the game. Beast and Heroes are meant to clash against each other. It's what happens when the Monomyth comes knocking: that thing does not care for actual behavior, social constructs or who's wrong or right. It just comes, and it's up to the Begotten to try and handle it. Lots of Beast is damage control, though the idea of what needs to be preserved or discarded varies from Begotten to Begotten.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Roof, it rains. A bleeding Beast cries as she kicks the corpse of the man who stalked her through the city to slay her. &quot;I did everything right! I helped all the others to survive, shared what they reaped. Fed as I should, not too much, not too little! Always on people that deserved it, I swear! Anything to keep the Gorgon asleep! Anything to not get here...&quot; Another kick. &quot;And you! You still came for me!&quot; More kicks. &quot;You fucking bastard still came after me!&quot; She then drops on her knees and keeps crying.<br /> <br /> Quick and hastily written, but I hope it's an useful example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-24-2019, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:38:39-07:00","id":1299372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299365#post1299365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does, but not directly. The best it can do, which is still valuable, is to provide Beasts a better framework to feed as they need in a less distruptive way. Which in turn lowers the chances of the Horror running amok and the overall strain a Begotten inflicts on the astral tapestry, with consequent diminished chances of them showing up on the Heroes' radar. Eventually, it will fail.<br /> <br /> Primordial Newcomer is right about that one. Not a perfect solution, but it makes things better. That's the sort of &quot;imperfect but still valuable and worth teaching others regardless of their opinion about Lessons&quot; trick that will survive over time and space.<br /> <br /> Now, will it stop Heroes from attacking? Well, even low-Integrity ones are not slashers, so it might give them pause, but the truth is that Lessons are not guaranteed to save Beast from Heroes. You can behave as best as you can, but one day an Hero will come to hunt you down. Which is both scary, frustrating and ultimately appropriate for the game. Beast and Heroes are meant to clash against each other. It's what happens when the Monomyth comes knocking: that thing does not care for actual behavior, social constructs or who's wrong or right. It just comes, and it's up to the Begotten to try and handle it. Lots of Beast is damage control, though the idea of what needs to be preserved or discarded varies from Begotten to Begotten.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's kind of what I'm getting at with Lessons just being a philosophy for practicing moderation with. I'd really love for there to be other philosophies. There <i>should </i>be more philosophies. Beasts are so individualized that they should have differences of opinion on this stuff.<br /> <br /> If every game has their actors divided on various philosophies, why is it that Beast: The Primordial is stuck with a single one? It just becomes monolithic through representation, and I see that as running counter to one of the core themes of the game, &quot;No Neat Little Boxes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:44:15-07:00","id":1299373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299372#post1299372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's kind of what I'm getting at with Lessons just being a philosophy for practicing moderation with. I'd really love for there to be other philosophies. There <i>should </i>be more philosophies. Beasts are so individualized that they should have differences of opinion on this stuff.<br /> <br /> If every game has their actors divided on various philosophies, why is it that Beast: The Primordial is stuck with a single one? It just becomes monolithic through representation, and I see that as running counter to one of the core themes of the game, &quot;No Neat Little Boxes&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>lessons are unique to individual beasts. it's a flexible philosophy and different beasts have their own beliefs about it. a beast who focuses on lessons of vanity is very different from the one who focuses on the lesson of letting go of the past. <br /> <br /> as for needing different philosophies, why should all the vampire covenants keep to the same 3 traditions? shouldn't there be different philosophies than just those?<br /> <br /> it's the same as the oath of the moon. it's a set in stone philosophy, but with many different interpretations (especially for blood talons)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:02:11-07:00","id":1299379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299306#post1299306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think a post is trolling, then report it and let the mods deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think a post is straining the civility of a thread then report it and let the mods deal with it. But you make calls for civility anyway, right?<br /> <br /> And I said &quot;toes the line&quot; as in, &quot;I don't think it is reportable trolling, but it's straining my patience for keeping to that opinion.&quot; But why engage with what people are saying? You're making it clear you're not going to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is about encouraging positive discussion of difficult subject matters. </div> </div> </div>Then you could be calling out Konradleijon for posts that don't actually promote positive discussions, instead of enabling them by validating them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To say that someone has a &quot;valid interpretation&quot; doesn't mean that it is the <i>only </i>interpretation. </div> </div> </div>Great, I proved it wrong on it's face anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not a &quot;one-sided call for civility&quot; to say &quot;I hear what you're saying&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The two are hardly mutually exclusive. In fact, they usually go hand in hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As what you quote, &quot;If Beasts are honest, they admit they use the concept of &quot;lessons&quot; to make what they do palatable.&quot; This is pretty explicit of victim-blaming, with a Beast saying, &quot;Because I say you did this, you deserve for me to feed upon you.&quot; </div> </div> </div>No it isn't. This is a patently absurd reading of the text.<br /> <br /> There is no logical connector between. &quot;Lessons let me feed under a moral framework so I can live with myself with what I do to feed,&quot; and, &quot;it is my victim's fault I need to do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Victim blaming is <b>blaming the victim for the action or situation</b>.<br /> <br /> &quot;What did she expect to happen walking around dressed like that?&quot; Is victim blaming. It's suggesting that the victim is responsible for creating the situation that traumatized them, rather than holding the perpetrators as the ones responsible. Nothing in that quote, or the book, justify treating lessons as doing that.<br /> <br /> The quote clearly keeps the blame in the Beast's court, thus isn't blaming the victim. Lessons are not framed as, &quot;feed because humans deserve it,&quot; but, &quot;try to feed in a fashion that's useful since you have to feed anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does what you say here not validate an interpretation of Lessons as being victim-blaming? </div> </div> </div>Because it does the exact opposite. I don't think you get what victim blaming is.<br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's kind of what I'm getting at with Lessons just being a philosophy for practicing moderation with. I'd really love for there to be other philosophies. There <i>should </i>be more philosophies. Beasts are so individualized that they should have differences of opinion on this stuff. </div> </div> </div>You're not entirely wrong here, but we all know that as a matter of practicality Lessons was introduced late in the development process because early reactions to the first KS draft include valid concerns that Beasts didn't have anything to guide what they actually do in play. There wasn't time for the game to fully develop either more philosophies under the same umbrella of 'Lessons' or some alternatives to Lessons. So the game relies on the 'no neat boxes' and has lessons be more personalized rather than having more grand philosophies under the necessities of actually making the game.<br /> <br /> None of this actually proves that lessons are bad as-is though.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:39:57-07:00","id":1299401,"title":"","content":"Why did beasts need anything to do?<br /> <br /> Maybe the theme could be Nihilism actual Nihilism.<br /> <br /> That We where put on this Earth Thanks to lots of Random shit starting with the Big Bang what ever caused life to spawn in the first place. Some other stuff happened . And by some random Gene mutantions Human mangeded to become Intelligent to muster up life to be able to eke out some From living Almost anywhere they go.<br /> <br /> Your birth was thanks to a series of random Coincidences. And it\u2019s up to you to create your on meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:47:42-07:00","id":1299406,"title":"","content":"what? konrad dont project your own thoughts if that's what you're doing. your posts are bringing nothing to the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:00:34-07:00","id":1299413,"title":"","content":"Why aren\u2019t my post Addding anything to the conversation?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not being sarcastic or trolling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:08:30-07:00","id":1299417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299401#post1299401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did beasts need anything to do?<br /> <br /> Maybe the theme could be Nihilism actual Nihilism.<br /> <br /> That We where put on this Earth Thanks to lots of Random shit starting with the Big Bang what ever caused life to spawn in the first place. Some other stuff happened . And by some random Gene mutantions Human mangeded to become Intelligent to muster up life to be able to eke out some From living Almost anywhere they go.<br /> <br /> Your birth was thanks to a series of random Coincidences. And it\u2019s up to you to create your on meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>this whole thing is literally, with no context, saying that beast should just take the theme of nihilism because...you want it to? not to mention the last part is something that applies to basically all supernaturals. it sounds like you are just lashing out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:11:11-07:00","id":1299420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299236#post1299236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, have you not read any of the discussion? you cant just lash out on an emotional level. to see it as &amp;quot;victim-blaming&amp;quot; is a BIG misinterpretation of what lessons are for. hell the books even show it's more than just an excuse to terrify AND the ChoD admit it has it's bad side in the form of the hunter compact Yuri's group</div> </div> </div> </div>I know but I loved the Origina draft in everything except hero\u2019s and I get that they where trying to do pointing out that Lots of \u201cHeroic\u201d Myth stories .<br /> <br /> See The Trojan Cicle,Lots of Blockbusters films. Enforce the Status quo with Patriarchal ideals. See the portrayal of Women in Greek mythology.<br /> <br /> And are often told and about the Ruling class and powerful people.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s some theories that The difference between Myths and Fairytales is about class and power see this article <a href=\"https://www.tor.com/2017/12/29/die-hard-is-a-modern-fairy-tale/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.tor.com/2017/12/29/die-h...rn-fairy-tale/</a>, And how most ancient hero\u2019s where Sociopaths. See fates version of Gilgamesh. But the fact they where caused by beasts made The metaphor Hazy. As they where The victims","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:18:25-07:00","id":1299423,"title":"","content":"the original draft had nothing about nihilism. heroes HAVE been progressing as villains (conquering heroes being the thing to read for that). not perfect, but MUCH better. what does any of this post have to do with explaining your point?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I going to be honest, heroes are NOT about patriarchy or ruling class. that's not beast. beast is a deconstruction of the monomyth. it does not try to preach patriarchy and a class system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-24-2019, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:28:00-07:00","id":1299427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299423#post1299423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the original draft had nothing about nihilism. heroes HAVE been progressing as villains (conquering heroes being the thing to read for that). not perfect, but MUCH better. what does any of this post have to do with explaining your point?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I going to be honest, heroes are NOT about patriarchy or ruling class. that's not beast. beast is a deconstruction of the monomyth. it does not try to preach patriarchy and a class system</div> </div> </div> </div>I know but many Monomyth stories exist to uphold the status quo.<br /> <br /> And the hero\u2019s are the villains them represent the Status quo , Bourgeoisie ,patriarchy Means Beast is Critiquing does things,<br /> <br /> And I think the Nihilism thing could have been added in the Revisions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 03-24-2019, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:33:32-07:00","id":1299432,"title":"","content":"no. no they really dont. the monomyth is an epic to tell the story of a hero who kills the beast. in fact heroes like orpheus, heracles and even beowulf are simply about the Hero being the good beating the evil (and it could be said that the monsters were there BEFORE the heroes were, so if anything the status quo changes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:37:16-07:00","id":1299433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299401#post1299401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did beasts need anything to do?<br /> <br /> Maybe the theme could be Nihilism actual Nihilism.<br /> <br /> That We where put on this Earth Thanks to lots of Random shit starting with the Big Bang what ever caused life to spawn in the first place. Some other stuff happened . And by some random Gene mutantions Human mangeded to become Intelligent to muster up life to be able to eke out some From living Almost anywhere they go.<br /> <br /> Your birth was thanks to a series of random Coincidences. And it\u2019s up to you to create your on meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a larger post and then refreshed the page without posting it, so I'll probably have to deal with the majority of those thoughts when I come back to Lessons proper, but for now:<br /> <br /> Simply put, <i>pure</i> nihilism is a <i>bad</i> baseline for designing <i>game character bases</i> because basically it incentives unmotivated characters, and an unmotivated character is a character who doesn't do anything, which is antithetical to telling good stories at a table with other people(see where Genius First's presentation fucked up). You can also see this in the shift with the Acanthus in Awakening, from a character who tells you they don't aspire to anything because they just manage their way through whatever to a character who seems effortless at what they do because they are furiously pedaling behind the scenes to makes things work <i>exactly</i> the way they want them, which in short translates to &quot;Character who never gives a shit about anything&quot; to &quot;Character who gives all the shits about this thing in particular, what could it be, YOU DECIDE AND DELIVER&quot;.<br /> <br /> By simply introducing Lessons as a cultural concept for the character type, you get to have your nihilism cake and eat it too-you can challenge it or accept it, have both stand points challenged, and have nihilism ultimately affirmed in a more meaningful way through the nuance of the conversation than just simple binge-eating to binge-eat. It creates motivated characters who will inherently have a character conflict baked in, because if nothing else, at all times a Beast has to ask themselves &quot;What the fuck am I doing with my life&quot; no matter whether they pursue it or leave it alone.<br /> <br /> Just tackling nihilism straight away for no other reason may still allow for that freedom, but as the initial draft of Beast proved, it tends to more often result in people asking &quot;Well then why the fuck am I bothering?&quot;, again ala Genius First. Better to give players something clear to chase after and heavily question along the way than nothing to do at the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-24-2019, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:39:27-07:00","id":1299435,"title":"","content":"I completely forgot genius showed the flaw in that as a main theme already","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:46:13-07:00","id":1299437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299435#post1299435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely forgot genius showed the flaw in that as a main theme already</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, writing a god damn short story about Genius's problems embedded a lot of important game design principles in my head.<br /> <br /> The third part of The Noble and the Sovereign was heavily informed by a very defeatist attitude about power until I remembered Genius, at which point I basically scrapped everything I had done and started from the beginning because <i>players should be able to win if their ability to lose is going to mean something</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T15:50:46-07:00","id":1299439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299437#post1299437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funnily enough, writing a god damn short story about Genius's problems embedded a lot of important game design principles in my head.<br /> <br /> The third part of The Noble and the Sovereign was heavily informed by a very defeatist attitude about power until I remembered Genius, at which point I basically scrapped everything I had done and started from the beginning because <i>players should be able to win if their ability to lose is going to mean something</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>i hope the best for genius 2nd edition, it should be a pretty big improvement<br /> <br /> that last part, you mind if I keep that as a quote from you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:01:08-07:00","id":1299442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299439#post1299439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i hope the best for genius 2nd edition, it should be a pretty big improvement<br /> <br /> that last part, you mind if I keep that as a quote from you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> Failure is an important part of storytelling, and sometimes an oft-ignored transtitional function by some creators. It is all too easy, by contrast, to go the other extreme, particularly concerning nihilism and it's popular-in-media cousin postmodern existentialism. A good rule of thumb is if it's not how Cowboy Bebop* would do it, you're doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> *Yeah, it's the popular cousin rather than nihilism, but still.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And of course, because i got lost on the train about failure, let me note that it's less about failure than meaninglessness. Beast succeeds on the subject because, lessons or no, success or no, nihilism is baked into the questions and answers of anything you do regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-24-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:34:31-07:00","id":1299454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299379#post1299379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you think a post is straining the civility of a thread then report it and let the mods deal with it. But you make calls for civility anyway, right?<br /> <br /> And I said &quot;toes the line&quot; as in, &quot;I don't think it is reportable trolling, but it's straining my patience for keeping to that opinion.&quot; But why engage with what people are saying? You're making it clear you're not going to.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really hammering hard on this &quot;calls for civility&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I make an effort to engage with what people are saying. There was a great back and forth between Primordial Newcomer and I earlier in the thread, where we each started with a stance and with patience with each other, we both came to see that there were areas that we could agree on. And that helped us better understanding where we're each coming from. Even on places where we disagree, I don't think they're <i>wrong</i>. That is just differences of opinion and interpretation.<br /> <br /> And it's okay to have differences of opinion and interpretation. There doesn't need to be a Right or Wrong answer, here.<br /> <br /> \u200bHonestly, I was hoping a little that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23952_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23952\" data-vbnamecard=\"23952\">Konradleijon</a> might be willing to speak up a bit more about their views, considering they seemed to have a strong stance on it and one with some emotion behind it. I can see at least one way that they got to that interpretation and I'd hoped that some support would encourage them to engage more, and maybe see if there is a way they could see the idea of Lessons as being useful in some fashion to them (like how Primordial Newcomer helped me see that I could use Lessons specifically in the context of that out-of-control Cult for my own game, where the Cultists are reasoning out what Lessons they think the Beast is trying to teach, with the Beast being completely unaware of this). <br /> <br /> Look, there is a lot of passion for this game from a lot of sides. And you can love and hate a lot of things about the stuff you're passionate with. When you're passionate about something, it's really easy to react emotionally in response to something. I'll call out an example of my own behavior in this thread, specifically where Satchel responded to one of my posts, and honestly? I shut down on it. I just couldn't deal with Satchel's post, badly even, considering I got passive aggressive with it (and speaking of which... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I'm sorry, that was rude of me and I acknowledge that. I'm trying to work on being better, but currently that means I'm relying on &quot;flight&quot; responses. I don't think you're a bad person, and if it amuses you, feel free to think of me as shyly ducking behind a lamp or something, or you know, just ignore me as you've got that button and I wouldn't blame you for it). <br /> <br /> However, the response I'm seeing to Konrad's post is also an emotional reaction. The flat denial that this interpretation has anything to it. The sideways accusation of trolling. And I get it, we're all passionate about this game. While it's great to discuss the positive feelings we have about this game, it's also good to discuss the negative feelings. Because by sharing what we don't like, if we're open about it, we can learn how to mitigate or nullify what we don't like, and have an even better game at our tables for it. In a way, that's kind of like how Beasts do it between themselves and their Kin. Like that, I kind of see the forum community as Family.<br /> <br /> And with Family, sometimes you just have to agree to disagree. That's fine. I don't have to think you're a bad person for it. I don't have to think you're &quot;wrong&quot; for it. You just see things differently than I do, and that can be immensely beneficial to this community having that difference in perspective.<br /> <br /> Saying that, I think I'm about to test your patience more. Just remember, we can agree to disagree and just be done like that, I'll still do the dishes if you'll still vacuum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299379#post1299379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No it isn't. This is a patently absurd reading of the text.<br /> <br /> There is no logical connector between. &quot;Lessons let me feed under a moral framework so I can live with myself with what I do to feed,&quot; and, &quot;it is my victim's fault I need to do this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Victim blaming is <b>blaming the victim for the action or situation</b>.<br /> <br /> &quot;What did she expect to happen walking around dressed like that?&quot; Is victim blaming. It's suggesting that the victim is responsible for creating the situation that traumatized them, rather than holding the perpetrators as the ones responsible. Nothing in that quote, or the book, justify treating lessons as doing that.<br /> <br /> The quote clearly keeps the blame in the Beast's court, thus isn't blaming the victim. Lessons are not framed as, &quot;feed because humans deserve it,&quot; but, &quot;try to feed in a fashion that's useful since you have to feed anyway.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because it does the exact opposite. I don't think you get what victim blaming is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to quote you here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Victim blaming is putting the responsibility for a crime or negative action on the victim of it. The game doesn't do that. Lessons are an in-game social construct to try to encourage Beasts <b>to pick victims that deserve it</b>, rather than blaming all humanity and feeding on whoever they want. </div> </div> </div>You recognize that at least some of the feeding Beasts do is victimizing people, and that the concept of Lessons is based on justifying why one person deserves to be victimized over someone else. With your example of &quot;What did she expect to happen walking around dressed like that?&quot; there is a Lesson being taught there. And no, it is not a good or healthy &quot;lesson&quot; that should be lauded.<br /> <br /> The entire point is to help Beasts feel better about what they do, but the game still calls out that it is bullshit. Just because the game says &quot;Oh, yeah, this is bullshit&quot; while still saying that Beasts continue to use Lessons to feel better about feeding doesn't mean that Beasts engaging in that aren't victim-blaming (by saying their targets deserve what they do to them) or not encouraging other Beasts to be victim-blaming by teaching about Lessons (&quot;Hey trust me, you'll feel better about what you're feeding from if you know the poor SOB deserves what you're doing to them.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Calling it out as bullshit to the reader really has no impact or meaning, when the game doesn't show any representation of other Beasts going, &quot;Hey, this is bullshit. How about this as another way?&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead, we get text saying that even the most nihilistic Beasts will continue to support the practice of &quot;teaching lessons&quot; to other Beasts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299379#post1299379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not entirely wrong here, but we all know that as a matter of practicality Lessons was introduced late in the development process because early reactions to the first KS draft include valid concerns that Beasts didn't have anything to guide what they actually do in play. There wasn't time for the game to fully develop either more philosophies under the same umbrella of 'Lessons' or some alternatives to Lessons. So the game relies on the 'no neat boxes' and has lessons be more personalized rather than having more grand philosophies under the necessities of actually making the game.<br /> <br /> None of this actually proves that lessons are bad as-is though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My stance is simply that the concept of Lessons is underdeveloped for the game. It is not a bad concept and it is workable, but it could be vastly improved and needed further development. I would have preferred that Beast: The Primordial be delayed in order for the last minute revisions be fully integrated and the manuscript edited for the changes (like how &quot;Soul&quot; is still being used in the text for the Horror).<br /> <br /> There was also an opportunity with the Player's Guide. To excuse the underdeveloped state of Lessons with &quot;but there wasn't time&quot; falls a bit flat when there was a second chance to really build up the concept and buttress it with other viable philosophies. And that is really a tragic shame, because something Beast: The Primordial really needs is more areas for Beasts to come into conflict with one another. And arguing about purpose is a great way to introduce conflict.<br /> <br /> (I wonder how many commas I used typing this... I'm betting the count is &quot;excessive&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:18:21-07:00","id":1299466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299290#post1299290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beasts feed because it's their nature. Lessons are a framework to keep themselves in check. Just like Humanity or the Oath of the Moon. A vampire that forgets their Humanity and just gives into their urge to feed falls to their beast and becomes an unplayable mindless killing machine. A werewolf that forgets the balance and duty of their Oath to Luna struggle to keep their Harmony and end up casing damage to their hunting grounds.<br /> <br /> A vampire that doesn't 'give a crap' about how they feed is doomed to lose their Humanity and their existence.<br /> <br /> A werewolf that doesn't 'give a crap' about how they hunt is going to fall out of Harmony, damage their territory, and risk themselves to any number of threats (including their own packmates).<br /> <br /> So, no, the other critters of the CofD are not 'more honest' about what they are, nor do they engage with their equivalents to feeding without context and purpose providing social structures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is a complete strawman that's unanswerable because it's not about Lessons in BtP, it's about the bad-faith &amp;quot;Lessons&amp;quot; that exist in the heads of people that don't actually know that the book says. I have no interest in defending your misconceptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about not giving a crap on how to feed. Vampires excess is somewhat curtained by Humanity, though they may just take a bane to invalidate feeding from affecting their humanity, but mainly they are governed by being clever about their feeding so they do not attract attention to themselves. None of this is affected by the fact that each one of them feeds because they are Vampires and need the blood and each of them acknowledges this as a fact. Similarly the Uratha are gverned by their Oath but the oath is not why they hunt and they know it. <br /> <br /> While most supernatural monsters may have rules for their feeding/hunting that are there to make sure they are not caught. Beasts and lessons are not about not getting caught quite the contrary I\u2019d argue that making sure your victims, or those left behind, learn a lesson from your feeding makes it easier to get caught. It also gives you an even clearer signature than your hunger already does.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying Beasts should rampage around like idiots, I am saying that in my opinion they do not need the whole lesson thing. It clearly wasn\u2019t even part of the original plan for Beasts but was tacked on to it which is why it feels so wrong to me. Basic truths are that Vampires need Blood, wolf must hunt and the Beast must feed.<br /> <br /> But like I said earlier these are matters easily handled and talked over at each individual table and so not really worth fighting over. I wouldn\u2019t have even felt the need to answer again if not for such blatant misreading of my earlier post. To reiterate I never claimed that Vampires, werewolves or Beasts shouldnt give a crap about how they feed quite on the contrary they all should so as to not get caught but what I do claim is that the lessons are crap and even the book agrees on that by saying that the Beasts know the lessons to be a lie and that the horror simply does not care about such things. But as always YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T17:27:37-07:00","id":1299467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299466#post1299466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never said anything about not giving a crap on how to feed. Vampires excess is somewhat curtained by Humanity, though they may just take a bane to invalidate feeding from affecting their humanity, but mainly they are governed by being clever about their feeding so they do not attract attention to themselves. None of this is affected by the fact that each one of them feeds because they are Vampires and need the blood and each of them acknowledges this as a fact. Similarly the Uratha are gverned by their Oath but the oath is not why they hunt and they know it. <br /> <br /> While most supernatural monsters may have rules for their feeding/hunting that are there to make sure they are not caught. Beasts and lessons are not about not getting caught quite the contrary I\u2019d argue that making sure your victims, or those left behind, learn a lesson from your feeding makes it easier to get caught. It also gives you an even clearer signature than your hunger already does.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying Beasts should rampage around like idiots, I am saying that in my opinion they do not need the whole lesson thing. It clearly wasn\u2019t even part of the original plan for Beasts but was tacked on to it which is why it feels so wrong to me. Basic truths are that Vampires need Blood, wolf must hunt and the Beast must feed.<br /> <br /> But like I said earlier these are matters easily handled and talked over at each individual table and so not really worth fighting over. I wouldn\u2019t have even felt the need to answer again if not for such blatant misreading of my earlier post. To reiterate I never claimed that Vampires, werewolves or Beasts shouldnt give a crap about how they feed quite on the contrary they all should so as to not get caught but what I do claim is that the lessons are crap and even the book agrees on that by saying that the Beasts know the lessons to be a lie and that the horror simply does not care about such things. But as always YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>beasts dont expect their victims to learn a lesson. the BPG literally states that whether a victim learns his lesson or not is a shot in the dark. a beast knows this as lessons are a framing mechanism for them to control their feeding.<br /> <br /> and as you said here &quot;Beast should feed because it is their nature, and forget this crap about lessons and justifications, just like Vampires feed because that is what Vampires do and werewolves because they must. The lessons do not make Beasts any more approachable or less monstrous they just make them hippocrites unlike the the rest of the monsters whom are what they are honestly.&quot; you did state vampires and werewolves do what they do not because they must, but because that's what they do. vampires do MANY things to keep what they do in check, just like how beast have lessons. vampires have their multitudes of laws in society and werewolves have the oath of the moon (and belials brood and the pure show what they would be like if that simply what they &quot;do&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T19:01:55-07:00","id":1299491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299454#post1299454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're really hammering hard on this &quot;calls for civility&quot; thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it a particularly frustrating thing in Internet conversations because it is rarely done in an even handed fashion that acknowledges the perceptions that those calling for look like they're overly focused on those that disagree with them while not doing anything to push back at the bad behaviors of those they disagree with.<br /> <br /> Things like, &quot;well you should just report them,&quot; doesn't help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the response I'm seeing to Konrad's post is also an emotional reaction. </div> </div> </div>Yes, to the repeated posts that amount to, &quot;I know this is a heated thing, but I'm just going to shit on parts of the game.&quot; That tends to piss people off. They tend to react. That needs to not happen for positive conversation to occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The flat denial that this interpretation has anything to it. </div> </div> </div>Sometimes things are wrong. I made my case for this being wrong. You can disagree with that, but it doesn't make it a raw emotional response any more than me flatly denying someone trying to argue that 2 + 2 can't equal four.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sideways accusation of trolling. </div> </div> </div>The direct statement that this was posting bordering on trolling, not a sideways accusation.<br /> <br /> &quot;Civility is a cudgel to passive aggressively beat people that disagree with me&quot; note #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While it's great to discuss the positive feelings we have about this game, it's also good to discuss the negative feelings. </div> </div> </div>Sure. Discussions. Not, &quot;this is shit!&quot; or &quot;this is victim-blaming,&quot; followed by refusal to anything but stick to that position and shout down disagreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saying that, I think I'm about to test your patience more. Just remember, we can agree to disagree and just be done like that, I'll still do the dishes if you'll still vacuum </div> </div> </div>You know you're going to say something that'll piss me off but you're just going to say it anyway and put it on me to disengage? Civility cudgel note #2,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You recognize that at least some of the feeding Beasts do is victimizing people, and that the concept of Lessons is based on justifying why one person deserves to be victimized over someone else. </div> </div> </div>Twisting my words. Cudgel #3.<br /> <br /> The concept of Lessons is about trying to direct the need to victimize people (because most Hungers flat out require this, not just some feeding) in a productive fashion. Some people need lessons more than other people. That's why people get different grade in school. It's why some crimes get you a ticket, and some people land you in prison for life. Any serious discussion of teaching lessons involves proportionality as feedback. One of things that makes Beasts bad at Lessons, is that they're bad at proportionality, because their Hunger drives them to overdo it.<br /> <br /> But the goal is to try to find that proportionality in your feeding. If you need to feed by punishing people, you find people that have done things that need punishing to teach them a lesson. This is not victim blaming. Victim blaming is punishing someone and them blaming them for making you do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With your example of &quot;What did she expect to happen walking around dressed like that?&quot; there is a Lesson being taught there. And no, it is not a good or healthy &quot;lesson&quot; that should be lauded. </div> </div> </div>Well the lesson to be taught there is, &quot;how a woman dresses doesn't mean she's consenting to any sexual advances, so back off,&quot; which is a plenty good and healthy lesson to teach people that need it.<br /> <br /> The related lesson of, &quot;hey, you're your own person, and in a perfect world this wouldn't be a problem, but what you're doing isn't safe because there are bad people out there,&quot; is also a good and healthy lesson to be taught, but is a very different thing.<br /> <br /> Neither of these involve attacking a woman for how she's dressed. Which some Beasts might do &quot;as a lesson,&quot; but so would plenty of normal humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because the game says &quot;Oh, yeah, this is bullshit&quot; while still saying that Beasts continue to use Lessons to feel better about feeding doesn't mean that Beasts engaging in that aren't victim-blaming (by saying their targets deserve what they do to them) or not encouraging other Beasts to be victim-blaming by teaching about Lessons (&quot;Hey trust me, you'll feel better about what you're feeding from if you know the poor SOB deserves what you're doing to them.&quot;) </div> </div> </div>And the problem with your whole argument here is that you're taking &quot;Lessons are inherently victim blaming&quot; as true before examining the evidence, and contorting the evidence to fit that conclusion.<br /> <br /> The text doesn't mean that Beasts aren't engaging in victim blaming, or that they are. Rather, it says that individuals do what they do, and some will victim blame and others don't; that the Lessons concept itself is neutral to it. Your position requires actually showing that Lessons are victim blaming, not misrepresenting what I or the text says.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Calling it out as bullshit to the reader really has no impact or meaning, when the game doesn't show any representation of other Beasts going, &quot;Hey, this is bullshit. How about this as another way?&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;I don't even bother with lessons,&quot; is &quot;another way&quot; the book presents as an alternative. So yes, it does have meaning and impact by your own standard even if I don't think that is'a valid one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead, we get text saying that even the most nihilistic Beasts will continue to support the practice of &quot;teaching lessons&quot; to other Beasts. </div> </div> </div>I literally quote the book not saying that. &quot;Still others shrug, cast off even the idea of a higher calling, and just feast.&quot; The text literally says, as I quoted, some Beasts don't give a shit about lessons and just do what they do. I quoted it directly. What were you saying about actually trying to engage with what people are saying again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My stance is simply that the concept of Lessons is underdeveloped for the game. </div> </div> </div>Goalpost shifting! Note #4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is not a bad concept and it is workable, but it could be vastly improved and needed further development. </div> </div> </div>Yet your'e also supporting attacking it as nothing more than victim blaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There was also an opportunity with the Player's Guide. To excuse the underdeveloped state of Lessons with &quot;but there wasn't time&quot; falls a bit flat when there was a second chance to really build up the concept and buttress it with other viable philosophies. </div> </div> </div>Just because the PG didn't do what you want by doubling down on Lessons instead of expanding to more philosophies, it did plenty of further development of Lessons to the point where the Lessons concept is not fairly classified as &quot;underdeveloped&quot; at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299466#post1299466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said anything about not giving a crap on how to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said that Beasts should be like vampires and feed because they must, instead of concerning themselves with lessons. That's pretty much the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of this is affected by the fact that each one of them feeds because they are Vampires and need the blood and each of them acknowledges this as a fact. Similarly the Uratha are gverned by their Oath but the oath is not why they hunt and they know it. </div> </div> </div>And Beasts feed because they have a Horror to keep feed or they die. Lessons are a framing around feeding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beasts and lessons are not about not getting caught quite the contrary I\u2019d argue that making sure your victims, or those left behind, learn a lesson from your feeding makes it easier to get caught. It also gives you an even clearer signature than your hunger already does. </div> </div> </div>They're not about not getting caught in general, but as noted and expanded on in the books, they help guard against Heroes because careless feeding provokes Heroes. And Heroes are a bigger concern to Beasts that general secrecy is for creatures like vampires. Beasts can easily live apart from human society with little risk of suffering for it, or operate legally (if distastefully) among normal humans as they feed in the open. They don't have to worry about sunlight, Rage, mobs with pitchforks, or whatever. Thus they're protective secrecy is oriented around what impacts things like the Primordial Dream rather than what normal folks might see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but was tacked on to it which is why it feels so wrong to me. </div> </div> </div>But that's ignoring <b>why</b> it was added. Otherwise all the stuff that got added to Requiem or Forsaken in their new editions would be wrong too. &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; should be wrong then, because that was tacked on later, not part of the original plan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....what I do claim is that the lessons are crap and even the book agrees on that by saying that the Beasts know the lessons to be a lie and that the horror simply does not care about such things. </div> </div> </div>The book doesn't agree with you. There's a difference between acknowledging that something is a bullshit thing the Beasts made up to replace having... nothing to fill that void for them, and claiming that it has no value in-game or as a game element.<br /> <br /> Countries, nations, etc. are bullshit things humans made up. They aren't something that's part of our natural biology or even filling our biological needs. They're inventions to regular behavior in social units that are too big for our instincts. Thus they still have value to us even if they're made up and frequently used to abuse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T20:29:14-07:00","id":1299503,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> We're just going to need to agree to disagree and leave it at that. I don't really need to say anything more about it.<br /> <br /> I'm not hitting you with cudgels or shifting goalposts, and I'm not going to get into a shouting match at you of logical fallacies or things like that. I don't need to do that. I'm sorry if I wasn't clear enough in my posts to make you think that my position has changed. It has not.<br /> <br /> And we can just end it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 03-24-2019, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:24:44-07:00","id":1299648,"title":"","content":"I genuinely wonder if the people that look at this game and laser-focus on the fact that the protagonists victimize people have ever played another game <i>of anything in the CofD or WoD.</i><br /> <br /> These gamelines have had monsters that victimize people for a living (literally) since the very first vampire product was released. This is <i>not a new concept</i><i> to the setting</i>. Beast approaches the subject matter differently, and the bullshit they tell themselves so they can sleep at night is much more transparently seen for what it is by the reader (bullshit) but if the average vampire player, for example, spent five minutes reflecting on the nature of that gameline's protagonists they'd see through the bullshit justifications there, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":".  A word 03-25-2019, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T10:51:14-07:00","id":1299653,"title":"","content":"I have been more than a little surprised at the 'They're monsters!' shock. There was a lot more to have issue with when the game came out than 'They're bad guys!'<br /> <br /> That said, I do think some of it is that Vitae/Lethal damage is abstract enough and non-real enough many people seem disassociated from the fact that vampires drain people's lives away, or it matters less in where the majority of RPGs are of the 'How many did you kill? Because that's how you're rewarded!' mindset that's so commonplace. While in a world of terrorists and fear mongers, having someone try to play upon people's fears and leave them a terrified wreck hits more close to home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2019, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:28:19-07:00","id":1299688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299648#post1299648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I genuinely wonder if the people that look at this game and laser-focus on the fact that the protagonists victimize people have ever played another game <i>of anything in the CofD or WoD.</i><br /> <br /> These gamelines have had monsters that victimize people for a living (literally) since the very first vampire product was released. This is <i>not a new concept</i><i> to the setting</i>. Beast approaches the subject matter differently, and the bullshit they tell themselves so they can sleep at night is much more transparently seen for what it is by the reader (bullshit) but if the average vampire player, for example, spent five minutes reflecting on the nature of that gameline's protagonists they'd see through the bullshit justifications there, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299653#post1299653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been more than a little surprised at the 'They're monsters!' shock. There was a lot more to have issue with when the game came out than 'They're bad guys!'<br /> <br /> That said, I do think some of it is that Vitae/Lethal damage is abstract enough and non-real enough many people seem disassociated from the fact that vampires drain people's lives away, or it matters less in where the majority of RPGs are of the 'How many did you kill? Because that's how you're rewarded!' mindset that's so commonplace. While in a world of terrorists and fear mongers, having someone try to play upon people's fears and leave them a terrified wreck hits more close to home.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I have an idea for. It's mostly that Beast doesn't bullshit around with the fact that you are a monster:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1299506-on-the-problematic-nature-of-beast-and-why-i-think-that-s-a-good-thing?p=1299534#post1299534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While all of the CofD gamelines have some sort of metaphor for playing as &quot;the other&quot;, they all offer shortcuts so the negative side of it that can be side-stepped. It not being necessary to drop mortal hunters (Vigil hunters or otherwise) on any of the gameline's monsters, being a monster carrying its own duties that don't involved being ostracized as an &quot;other&quot; (Werewolf, Geist), being the &quot;other&quot; is portrayed as cool, sexy, and empowering (Vampire, Changeling), or even being cathartic in allowing PCs to change the world into a better place (Mage, Hunter).<br /> <br /> Plus, despite CofD (and by extension, its progenitor WoD) lofty (or more cynically, &quot;pretentious&quot;) goals of trying to offer more mature and in-depth storytelling versus the EVILS of murderhobo &quot;rollplaying&quot; from mainstream titles like D&amp;D or Pathfinder...there is still an element of escapist power-fantasy involved in the previous CofD games.<br /> <br /> Beast doesn't really allow for that. At least, not in the conventional way.<br /> <br /> As talked about above, Beast does have escapist power-fantasy embedded in it...just not based off of positive emotions. And, as an &quot;other&quot;, people don't react well to the idea of embracing their other-ness through negative emotions since it runs counter to everything we're taught about how to achieve integration of minorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>For instance, looking at Satiety and the other &quot;feeding&quot; methods of the other CofD gamelines...<br /> <br /> Vampires can make the blood-drinking thing less icky by either investing in the Herd Merit, and rationalize it away as consenting adults being ok with some more intense love bites, or flat out just defaulting to blood bags. Or abstracting the feeding roll to a single dice roll, no scene needed (which even then, TBF, according to Vampire STs I've talked to, it gets repetitive and dull to have to keep doing feeding scenes, so making it the abstract roll is a necessity).<br /> <br /> Werewolves aren't required to kill the targets of their Sacred Hunt, and depending on the game you might actively choose to not even have any Iron Masters around, and thus no humans to worry about Hunting. And all of the other prey rationalize away as not being human at all, or that they're so far gone that they aren't even human anymore.<br /> <br /> Mages and their Mysteries don't require human victims at all, Promethean's Disquiet being something they can't help, Changelings aren't required to be the source of whatever generated emotion is needed to create Glamour, etc.<br /> <br /> Beast, as of right now, doesn't have those convenient shortcuts.<br /> <br /> Even when using Family Dinner, you still have to cause intense fear in their prospective target. There's really no way to get around that, and that's why people tend to draw a line between Beast and the other CofD gamelines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T12:29:33-07:00","id":1299690,"title":"","content":"Still... Changeling the Dreaming and Wraith the Oblivion went there (even if more optionally than Beast) over 20 years ago. Perhaps it's why people talk about the big three instead of the original five a lot, but those two games and some very hard to disassociate from real life ways of 'feeding;' and some of the most disturbing aren't even inherently violent. A CtD Changeling that specializes in Ravaging for Glamour would probably make a good number of Beasts balk at how vicious it is to just drain away all the positivity and creativity via purposeful emotional sabotage on someone until they're a depressed wreck of a human being... and keep doing it until you've broken them completely... is way farther than most Beasts would go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T15:20:30-07:00","id":1299749,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not a big OWOD fan. Can you explain to my how Wraith went there?<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t wraiths feed on being rembred?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T15:38:50-07:00","id":1299753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299749#post1299749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t wraiths feed on being rembred?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. What you're thinking of is the Memoriam Background...which, well, not every Wraith has that.<br /> <br /> They feed off of emotions to gain their fuel stat, Pathos. Their Passions are linked to strong emotions that keep a wraith stuck in the Shadowlands/Underworld, usually tied to something in life that they left unresolved. While it's possible for them to gain Pathos from secondhand sources that just experience the emotion, it's easier for them to get it back by experiencing their Passion as a whole. And since some Passions are specific enough to not always occur, that means the Wraith might need to engineer a situation so that they CAN get the Pathos they need...regardless if any mortals involved are aware of it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Apologies if my answer is a bit rushed, I'm stepping off to work right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-25-2019, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:17:39-07:00","id":1299761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299688#post1299688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That I have an idea for. It's mostly that Beast doesn't bullshit around with the fact that you are a monster:</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it kind of does, though. Vampire, as disassociated as it is from the act of harming people, doesn't tell people they're out there doing good in the world the way the Beast attempted with its lesson belief system. While you could argue that the Lancea et Sanctum are chosen by god to do the will of god, it seems fairly clear that that is them clinging to straws, rather than the developer telling us that god is giving them the go ahead as part of their plan.<br /> <br /> While the covenants are structures designed to maintain a semblance of humanity as one is already a monster, they're clearly painted as coping mechanisms developed over the ages, rather than the universe going out and telling them 'This is the way.'<br /> <br /> Though I think your perspective on the 'tangibility' of the damage done to humans is pretty well thought out (and that we're a bit likeminded on this point, even if our own opinions on the games are different), Beasts do have a way around it via the Family Dinner option, which is the way to have the fear-mongering monster without the baggage of being a fear-monger, just sort of assisting one. Of course that also weakens my argument about terror in the modern world versus the disassociation of physical harm in tabletop games too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-25-2019, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:54:01-07:00","id":1299774,"title":"","content":"family dinner, while a very useful ability, should be noted that beast cant expect to find every supernatural, much less think that they will be friendly to them and ALWAYS be friendly with them.<br /> <br /> family dinner in the end has 2 big shortcomings. it relies on the beast being able to establish a relationship with a supernatural who likely wont always be there for him, and 2 hope that new friend is willing to be more overt in his methods so the beast can feed. now the first part can be argued that they dont NEED to be in a relationship, but a beast can only be stealthy for so long before being found out (and this is ignoring have to know the unknowing associated whereabouts). the 2nd part may matter less with werewolves compared to other supernaturals, but for many creatures it's best to be subtle around humans and not cause fear willy-nilly. having a beast tell you to just scare the crap out of someone would be a chore for many (though to be fair, that beast should help in return obviously)<br /> <br /> to end it off, a beast surviving on family dinner is likely only doing that. surviving and never living<br /> <br /> EDIT: I am VERY sorry if I misinterpreted and that you simply met beast DOES have a way to avoid scaring people, instead of saying it was a viable alternative to just feeding themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-25-2019, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:14:22-07:00","id":1299781,"title":"","content":"Family Dinner is a very useful dial to have if you want to run stories on the less monstrous side though. There are a fair number of ways to use it for low impact feeding, sometimes even lower impact than the other splats could manage alone, and far lower than if the two were both feeding separately.<br /> <br /> For example, a Beast with Relentless Hunter befriends a vampire and establishes family ties. Once or twice a week they go out and hunt down a mortal and the vampire takes a single point of vitae so the Beast can get that sweet three satiety. The rest of the time the vampire stays topped off on the Beast, who recovers as much blood in two hours as a mortal does in a week. The vamp is taking a fraction of the mortal blood they would otherwise need just to stay alive and the Beast is just tagging along. It's never completely victimless, but it's as close as you can get in these games.<br /> <br /> Sure, it isn't always that easy. You wouldn't want it to always be that easy. But it's a nice option to have. Sometimes you want to play a &quot;designated bad guy&quot; who has worked hard to make a positive difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:31:51-07:00","id":1299788,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5328\" data-vbnamecard=\"5328\">HelmsDerp</a>, re-reading family dinner, my bad. I misremembered how it worked.<br /> <br /> you do have a point, but it should still be noted that such a smooth partnership would be exceptionally rare. (though I will say much more beneficial than I once thought for the beast. I thought the partner would still have to inspire fear)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T18:58:52-07:00","id":1299812,"title":"","content":"Well, it wouldn't be much of a game if there were never any complications, but I think Beasts with that Atavism wouldn't have too much trouble finding a vampire willing to bite, pun very much intended. Removing most of the effort and worry of feeding is a damn good incentive for an alliance.<br /> <br /> Another personal favorite strategy for low impact feeding: Follow some Summer Court Changelings to a political protest. A few people go home a bit more emotionally drained as the changelings harvest glamour, but it's nothing a good night's sleep won't fix. You can adjust the event based on court. Attend a concert with Spring or a wake with Winter. Help Autumn run the best haunted house in the county. The main thing a Beast has to offer in that dynamic is the relative safety with which they can thwart Huntsmen, given that they have no special weakness to iron and many strong combat powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:24:24-07:00","id":1302185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1299761#post1299761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you could argue that the Lancea et Sanctum are chosen by god to do the will of god, it seems fairly clear that that is them clinging to straws, rather than the developer telling us that god is giving them the go ahead as part of their plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lancea Sanctum's tactics as working is never called into question. Likewise, they don't pay the humanity piper for their actions. The narrative of God existing and sending them forth is called into question (because Requiem isn't really about metaphysical validation), but their tactics working as far as stoking faith and maintaining their humanity is never called into question. Beast lesson stuff is nothing new for the game, but its called into question for beasts, while LS doing the things that would tank the humanity of any other vampire is never called into question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T09:32:05-07:00","id":1302243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1302185#post1302185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lancea Sanctum's tactics as working is never called into question. Likewise, they don't pay the humanity piper for their actions. The narrative of God existing and sending them forth is called into question (because Requiem isn't really about metaphysical validation), but their tactics working as far as stoking faith and maintaining their humanity is never called into question. Beast lesson stuff is nothing new for the game, but its called into question for beasts, while LS doing the things that would tank the humanity of any other vampire is never called into question.</div> </div> </div> </div>to be fair here, the Lancea Sanctum (and granted this is from their 1st edition supplement) not only bring their faith in to stop their humanity from draining, but also initiated programs like confessions to lift burdens from vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T13:18:59-07:00","id":1302311,"title":"","content":"I could make a case about the LeS does work in a very human way, even if not in a very good way. There's plenty very human about twisting religion to justify morally reprehensible actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T01:11:02-07:00","id":1302499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1297255-a-different-take-heroes-as-protagonists-and-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1302311#post1302311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could make a case about the LeS does work in a very human way, even if not in a very good way. There's plenty very human about twisting religion to justify morally reprehensible actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but that's... not actually how Humanity works, for anyone but them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}